msgctxt "FateEvent:31:0:59"
msgid "Aid the beekeepers?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь пчеловодам?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этой F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: むむむ……。<br>このままじゃ、蜂蜜が……。
#. de: Verstehe ... Dann nimmt das große Bienensterben wohl seinen Lauf ...
#. fr: Q-quoi<nbsp>? Mais sans miel, nous ne pourrons plus produire d'hydromel, et je ne suis pas sûr de vouloir vivre dans un monde sans hydromel...
#. column 56: An adventurer! Oh, I never thought I'd be so happy to see one of your lot!
#. column 57: It's those damnable imps! Not only are they pinching the honey from all our hives, but they're killing the precious bees in the process.
#. column 58: Please, you must lend us your blade!
#. column 59: Aid the beekeepers?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:31:0:62"
msgid "Think of all the unruly tosspots who'll venture out into the forest if they don't get their mead! Please reconsider!"
msgstr "Подумай о том, сколько всяких пьяниц полезут в лес, если им не достанется медовухи! Прошу, передумай!"

#. ja: ふぅ……<br>ようやく、ラノシアオレンジを摘み終えた。<br>後は、納品先へ運ぶだけなんだが……
#. de: Die Orangen sind endlich gepflückt und verpackt. Eigentlich müsste ich jetzt nur noch auf die Karawane warten, die sie zur Gladion-Bucht transportieren soll ...
#. fr: Ouf...<nbsp>! Les oranges ont été cueillies et sont enfin rangées dans leurs caisses. Je n'ai plus qu'à attendre que la caravane vienne les prendre...
#. column 57: The problem is, the caravan is nowhere in sight, and I can already hear the rats clawing their way out from under the rocks. It won't be long before they've found their way into the crates.
#. column 58: I beg of you, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>! Would you help me in keeping the rats clear of my oranges until the chocobos arrive?
#. column 59: Aid the farmer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Another harvest lost, then...
msgctxt "FateEvent:32:0:56"
msgid "The oranges are all picked and boxed. Now I need only wait for the caravan to come pick them up..."
msgstr "Апельсины уже собраны и уложены в ящики. Осталось только дождаться каравана..."

#. ja: 荷を造り終えると決まって<br>食い意地張ったラットどもが、<br>オレンジにたかってくるんだ！
#. de: Aber der Duft der Früchte lockt jedesmal Ratten aus den Docks an. Ein paar habe ich schon selbst erledigt und die Gelbjacken unterstützen uns auch, aber es gibt einfach zu viele von den Viechern.
#. fr: Le problème, c'est que je ne la vois pas venir et que j'entends déjà les rats griffer les rochers pour se frayer un chemin jusqu'ici. Ils ne mettront pas longtemps à atteindre les caisses.
#. column 56: The oranges are all picked and boxed. Now I need only wait for the caravan to come pick them up...
#. column 58: I beg of you, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>! Would you help me in keeping the rats clear of my oranges until the chocobos arrive?
#. column 59: Aid the farmer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Another harvest lost, then...
msgctxt "FateEvent:32:0:57"
msgid "The problem is, the caravan is nowhere in sight, and I can already hear the rats clawing their way out from under the rocks. It won't be long before they've found their way into the crates."
msgstr "Только вот каравана всё нет, а из-под камней уже слышно, как выбираются крысы. Скоро они доберутся до ящиков."

#. ja: だから、頼む！<br>押し寄せてきたラットどもを根こそぎ倒して、<br>大事な「オレンジ入りの木箱」を守り抜いてくれ！
#. de: Ich bitte dich, du musst mir helfen! Wenn die ganze Schufterei umsonst war, verkrafte ich das nicht.
#. fr: Je vous en prie<nbsp>! Vous voulez bien m'aider en tenant les rats à distance jusqu'à l'arrivée des chocobos<nbsp>?
#. column 56: The oranges are all picked and boxed. Now I need only wait for the caravan to come pick them up...
#. column 57: The problem is, the caravan is nowhere in sight, and I can already hear the rats clawing their way out from under the rocks. It won't be long before they've found their way into the crates.
#. column 59: Aid the farmer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Another harvest lost, then...
#. macro: <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:32:0:58"
msgid "I beg of you, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>! Would you help me in keeping the rats clear of my oranges until the chocobos arrive?"
msgstr "Умоляю, <if $gn4>госпожа<else>господин</if>! Помоги отогнать крыс от апельсинов, пока не приехали чокобо!"

#. ja: 守り抜きますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Dem Bauern helfen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider le fermier<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: The oranges are all picked and boxed. Now I need only wait for the caravan to come pick them up...
#. column 57: The problem is, the caravan is nowhere in sight, and I can already hear the rats clawing their way out from under the rocks. It won't be long before they've found their way into the crates.
#. column 58: I beg of you, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>! Would you help me in keeping the rats clear of my oranges until the chocobos arrive?
#. column 62: Another harvest lost, then...
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
