msgctxt "FateEvent:39:0:60"
msgid "That's right kind of you, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. You see? Here they come now!"
msgstr "Вот это по-доброму с вашей стороны, <if $gn4>сударыня<else>сударь</if>. Гляньте, вот и они!"

#. ja: ん……そうか、手伝えないか。<br>まぁ、無理強いもできないからな。<br>また今度、手の空いてる時に手伝ってくれればいいさ。
#. de: Das ist bedauernswert. Wenn sie sich an den Schafen sattgefressen haben, sind wir wahrscheinlich als Nächstes dran. Kannst du mit der Verantwortung leben?
#. fr: Toutes mes excuses, j'imagine que vous avez des affaires plus importantes à régler.
#. column 56: A moment of your time, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>?
#. column 57: The fields are crawling with ocean roselings─horrible creatures that choke out the crops and maim the tillers who tend to them. We hold our own against the seedkin, but it seems for every one we cut down, there are three more to take its place!
#. column 58: We'd be obliged if you could lend us your sword in clearing the fields.
#. column 59: Aid the tillers?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: That's right kind of you, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. You see? Here they come now!
#. macro: <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:39:0:62"
msgid "Apologies, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. I reckon you have matters of greater import what need attendin'."
msgstr "Простите, <if $gn4>госпожа<else>сударь</if>. Похоже, у вас дела поважнее, да и заняться ими надо прямо сейчас."

#. ja: オーシャン・ローズリングめ、どんどん出てきてるな！<br>よし、冒険者さん、片っ端からやっつけちまってくれ！<br>頼りにしてるからなっ！
#. de: Verdammte Ozean-Röslinge! Ausgerottet gehören die, mit Stumpf und Stiel!
#. fr: Comme je vous l'ai dit, il y a trois nouveaux monstres pour chacun que nous tuons. Si seulement nos plantes poussaient aussi bien<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:40:0:56"
msgid "Did I not tell you? Three more for every one slain. If only my crops grew so well!"
msgstr "Я же говорил: на каждого убитого трое новых. Вот бы урожай так рос!"

#. ja: 助けて、冒険者の人！<br>私一人じゃどうにもならないのよ！
#. de: Ah, <if $gn4>eine Abenteurerin<else>ein Abenteurer</if>, was für eine glückliche Fügung! Ich benötige dringend Hilfe!
#. fr: Pourquoi<nbsp>!? Mais pourquoi, je vous le demande<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Why would galagos want anything to do with my flour!? It's not as if they can bake it into bread or lemoncakes! They can't, can they?
#. column 58: But that doesn't stop them from raiding my granaries day in and day out. If this goes on much longer, I will have nothing to take to market and the moneylenders will come for my only daughter... Please! I beg of you! Help me drive off the beasts!
#. column 59: Aid the miller?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks! A thousand thousand thanks! If only I could find the words to thank you enou─ Oh! They're here!
#. column 62: Perhaps another will come along who can help...
msgctxt "FateEvent:41:0:56"
msgid "Why!? Why, I ask you!"
msgstr "Почему?! Да почему же, скажите на милость?!"

#. ja: 風車小屋で挽いた小麦粉を出荷したいんだけど、<br>お腹を空かせたガラゴが狙ってくるから運べないの。
#. de: Mein Getreide ist gemahlen und wartet auf seine Auslieferung. Genauso wie eine hungrige Meute Galagos, die ganz versessen auf das Zeug sind.
#. fr: Pourquoi ces chapardeurs de galagos s'en prennent à ma farine<nbsp>!? Ce n'est pas comme s'ils pouvaient faire du pain ou des gâteaux au citron<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Why!? Why, I ask you!
#. column 58: But that doesn't stop them from raiding my granaries day in and day out. If this goes on much longer, I will have nothing to take to market and the moneylenders will come for my only daughter... Please! I beg of you! Help me drive off the beasts!
#. column 59: Aid the miller?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks! A thousand thousand thanks! If only I could find the words to thank you enou─ Oh! They're here!
#. column 62: Perhaps another will come along who can help...
msgctxt "FateEvent:41:0:57"
msgid "Why would galagos want anything to do with my flour!? It's not as if they can bake it into bread or lemoncakes! They can't, can they?"
msgstr "Почему галлаго вообще нужна моя мука?! Неужели они и правда могут печь из неё хлеб или лимонные пирожные?"

#. ja: 味を覚えちゃったみたいで、運んでると襲ってくるのよ。<br>お願い、ガラゴたちをやっつけて！
#. de: So schnell kann mein Chocobo den Karren gar nicht ziehen, wie die ihn geentert haben. Drei Lieferungen haben die Räuber mir schon ruiniert. Ein weiterer Fehlschlag wäre mein finanzieller Ruin!
#. fr: Eh bien, ça ne les empêche pas de piller mes greniers tous les jours. Si ça continue, je n'aurai plus rien à vendre au quartier marchand et je vais faire faillite. Je vous en prie<nbsp>! Pitié<nbsp>! Aidez-moi à repousser ces vilains voleurs de farine<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Why!? Why, I ask you!
#. column 57: Why would galagos want anything to do with my flour!? It's not as if they can bake it into bread or lemoncakes! They can't, can they?
#. column 59: Aid the miller?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks! A thousand thousand thanks! If only I could find the words to thank you enou─ Oh! They're here!
#. column 62: Perhaps another will come along who can help...
msgctxt "FateEvent:41:0:58"
msgid "But that doesn't stop them from raiding my granaries day in and day out. If this goes on much longer, I will have nothing to take to market and the moneylenders will come for my only daughter... Please! I beg of you! Help me drive off the beasts!"
msgstr "Но им хоть бы что: день за днём шарят по амбарам. Если так пойдёт и дальше, мне нечего будет везти на рынок, а заимодавцы заберут мою единственную дочь... Прошу! Умоляю! Помогите прогнать этих тварей!"

#. ja: 退治を引き受けますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Die Galagos verjagen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider la meunière<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Why!? Why, I ask you!
#. column 57: Why would galagos want anything to do with my flour!? It's not as if they can bake it into bread or lemoncakes! They can't, can they?
#. column 58: But that doesn't stop them from raiding my granaries day in and day out. If this goes on much longer, I will have nothing to take to market and the moneylenders will come for my only daughter... Please! I beg of you! Help me drive off the beasts!
#. column 60: A thousand thanks! A thousand thousand thanks! If only I could find the words to thank you enou─ Oh! They're here!
#. column 62: Perhaps another will come along who can help...
