msgid "Aid the miller?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь мельничихе?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ありがとう、やっぱり冒険者さんは頼りになるわね。<br>じゃあ、よろしくお願いね！
#. de: Vielen Dank! Ihr Abenteurer seid ein Segen für Eorzea!
#. fr: Mille mercis<nbsp>! Je ne sais que dire pour vous remerci... Oh, par les Dieux, les voilà<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Why!? Why, I ask you!
#. column 57: Why would galagos want anything to do with my flour!? It's not as if they can bake it into bread or lemoncakes! They can't, can they?
#. column 58: But that doesn't stop them from raiding my granaries day in and day out. If this goes on much longer, I will have nothing to take to market and the moneylenders will come for my only daughter... Please! I beg of you! Help me drive off the beasts!
#. column 59: Aid the miller?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Perhaps another will come along who can help...
msgctxt "FateEvent:41:0:60"
msgid "A thousand thanks! A thousand thousand thanks! If only I could find the words to thank you enou─ Oh! They're here!"
msgstr "Тысячу раз спасибо! Тысячу тысяч раз спасибо! Вот бы ещё найти слова, чтобы отблагодарить вас как следует... Ой! Они уже здесь!"

#. ja: ああ、そう……じゃあ仕方ないわね。<br>残念だけど、他の人を探して頼むことにするわ。
#. de: Ich verstehe ... Hoffentlich finde ich jemand anderen.
#. fr: Je vois... Peut-être y aura-t-il une âme charitable pour m'aider...
#. column 56: Why!? Why, I ask you!
#. column 57: Why would galagos want anything to do with my flour!? It's not as if they can bake it into bread or lemoncakes! They can't, can they?
#. column 58: But that doesn't stop them from raiding my granaries day in and day out. If this goes on much longer, I will have nothing to take to market and the moneylenders will come for my only daughter... Please! I beg of you! Help me drive off the beasts!
#. column 59: Aid the miller?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks! A thousand thousand thanks! If only I could find the words to thank you enou─ Oh! They're here!
msgctxt "FateEvent:41:0:62"
msgid "Perhaps another will come along who can help..."
msgstr "Может, кто-нибудь ещё согласится помочь..."

#. ja: このあたりではリバートードが繁殖しやすくてね、<br>定期的に駆除しないと、大変なことになっちまうんだよ。<br>今はちょうど、その定期駆除の真っ最中ってわけさ。
#. de: Verdammte Aga-Kröten! Die Gelehrten unten an der Mealvaaner Zollbehörde meinten, die Viecher würden gute Schädlingsbekämpfer abgeben, also wurde hier zwischen den Getreidefeldern eine kleine Population ausgesetzt.
#. fr: Argh<nbsp>! Maudits soient ces crapauds buffles<nbsp>! Les érudits de la douane de Mealvaan disaient qu'ils nous débarrasseraient des criquets qui infestent nos champs chaque année, et ils ont donc libéré une caisse de ces créatures visqueuses dans la Basse-Noscea.
#. column 57: Not only did they not eat the locusts, but they began breedin' quicker 'an rabbits, and before we knew it, the whole damn region was burstin' at the seams with the ugly monsters.
#. column 58: Now, I spend my days catchin' and guttin' the toads at the behest of the same damned scholarlies who started this whole mess. It ain't a bad job, but it sure can be right lonely sometimes. Hey, you wouldn't mind keepin' a man company, would you?
#. column 59: That's a good <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. Now off you go while I stand watch here and make sure no one from the road bothers us.
#. column 60: Eh? You thought we was going to do the guttin' together? That's rich!
msgctxt "FateEvent:42:0:56"
msgid "Bloody cane toads! The scholarlies down at Mealvaan's Gate reckoned they would eat the locusts which overrun the wheat fields each year, and so allowed a crate of the slimy creatures to be released into lower La Noscea."
msgstr "Будь прокляты эти тростниковые жабы! Учёные из таможни Мелваанских ворот решили, что они будут пожирать саранчу, которая каждый год опустошает пшеничные поля. Вот и выпустили целый ящик этих склизких тварей в Нижней Ла-Носкеа."

#. ja: 慣れているとはいえ、楽な作業じゃなくてね。<br>よかったら、あんたも手伝ってくれないか？
#. de: Den Schädlingen haben sie den Garaus gemacht, das stimmt schon, aber gleichzeitig vermehrten sie sich auch so sprunghaft, dass jetzt das gesamte untere La Noscea voll von diesen hässlichen Biestern ist.
#. fr: Non seulement ils n'ont pas touché aux criquets, mais ils ont commencé à se reproduire comme des lapins et, maintenant, toute la région est infestée par ces horribles batraciens.
#. column 56: Bloody cane toads! The scholarlies down at Mealvaan's Gate reckoned they would eat the locusts which overrun the wheat fields each year, and so allowed a crate of the slimy creatures to be released into lower La Noscea.
#. column 58: Now, I spend my days catchin' and guttin' the toads at the behest of the same damned scholarlies who started this whole mess. It ain't a bad job, but it sure can be right lonely sometimes. Hey, you wouldn't mind keepin' a man company, would you?
#. column 59: That's a good <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. Now off you go while I stand watch here and make sure no one from the road bothers us.
#. column 60: Eh? You thought we was going to do the guttin' together? That's rich!
msgctxt "FateEvent:42:0:57"
msgid "Not only did they not eat the locusts, but they began breedin' quicker 'an rabbits, and before we knew it, the whole damn region was burstin' at the seams with the ugly monsters."
msgstr "Мало им оказалось саранчи — они стали плодиться быстрее кроликов. Оглянуться не успели, как вся округа кишела этими мерзкими тварями."

#. ja: 駆除対象は、リバートードの中でもとくに繁殖力の高い<br>ケーントードと呼ばれている個体だ。<br>通常の個体は、放っておいて構わない。
#. de: Und wer darf die Suppe auslöffeln? Ich natürlich! Den ganzen Tag nichts anderes als Kröten fangen und aufschlitzen! Im Grunde kein schlechter Job, aber auf die Dauer ziemlich eintönig. Warum gehst du mir nicht etwas zur Hand?
#. fr: Résultat, je passe mes journées à attraper ces crapauds pour les tuer, et comble de l'ironie, pour le compte de ces mêmes érudits qui sont à l'origine du problème<nbsp>! Il y a sûrement pire, mais je me sens un peu abandonné quelquefois. Vous ne voudriez pas me donner un coup de main<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Bloody cane toads! The scholarlies down at Mealvaan's Gate reckoned they would eat the locusts which overrun the wheat fields each year, and so allowed a crate of the slimy creatures to be released into lower La Noscea.
#. column 57: Not only did they not eat the locusts, but they began breedin' quicker 'an rabbits, and before we knew it, the whole damn region was burstin' at the seams with the ugly monsters.
#. column 59: That's a good <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. Now off you go while I stand watch here and make sure no one from the road bothers us.
#. column 60: Eh? You thought we was going to do the guttin' together? That's rich!
msgctxt "FateEvent:42:0:58"
msgid "Now, I spend my days catchin' and guttin' the toads at the behest of the same damned scholarlies who started this whole mess. It ain't a bad job, but it sure can be right lonely sometimes. Hey, you wouldn't mind keepin' a man company, would you?"
msgstr "Теперь я целыми днями ловлю и потрошу жаб по приказу тех самых проклятых учёных, что и заварили всю эту кашу. Работа неплохая, да только одному тоскливо. Эй, не составишь компанию?"

#. ja: それじゃあ頼むぞ、冒険者。<br>俺はここで街道を通る人が巻き込まれないよう、<br>見張っていることにする。
#. de: Besten Dank,  <if $gn4>meine Liebe<else>mein Lieber</if>. Dann kümmre dich mal um die Kröten, während ich hier aufpasse, dass dich niemand dabei stört.
#. fr: Merci beaucoup. Je vais monter la garde ici pour qu'on ne nous dérange pas. Occupez-vous des crapauds<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Bloody cane toads! The scholarlies down at Mealvaan's Gate reckoned they would eat the locusts which overrun the wheat fields each year, and so allowed a crate of the slimy creatures to be released into lower La Noscea.
#. column 57: Not only did they not eat the locusts, but they began breedin' quicker 'an rabbits, and before we knew it, the whole damn region was burstin' at the seams with the ugly monsters.
#. column 58: Now, I spend my days catchin' and guttin' the toads at the behest of the same damned scholarlies who started this whole mess. It ain't a bad job, but it sure can be right lonely sometimes. Hey, you wouldn't mind keepin' a man company, would you?
#. column 60: Eh? You thought we was going to do the guttin' together? That's rich!
#. macro: <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:42:0:59"
msgid "That's a good <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. Now off you go while I stand watch here and make sure no one from the road bothers us."
msgstr "Вот умница, <if $gn4>девочка<else>молодец</if>. А теперь ступай. Я тут постою на страже, чтобы никто с дороги нам не помешал."

#. ja: ……別に、トードが苦手な訳じゃないんだからな？
#. de: Was? Du dachtest, wir würden die Viecher gemeinsam bekämpfen? Ich will dir doch nicht den ganzen Spaß nehmen!
#. fr: Ne me dites pas que vous avez une sainte horreur de ces bestioles poisseuses, quand même...<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Bloody cane toads! The scholarlies down at Mealvaan's Gate reckoned they would eat the locusts which overrun the wheat fields each year, and so allowed a crate of the slimy creatures to be released into lower La Noscea.
#. column 57: Not only did they not eat the locusts, but they began breedin' quicker 'an rabbits, and before we knew it, the whole damn region was burstin' at the seams with the ugly monsters.
#. column 58: Now, I spend my days catchin' and guttin' the toads at the behest of the same damned scholarlies who started this whole mess. It ain't a bad job, but it sure can be right lonely sometimes. Hey, you wouldn't mind keepin' a man company, would you?
#. column 59: That's a good <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if>. Now off you go while I stand watch here and make sure no one from the road bothers us.
msgctxt "FateEvent:42:0:60"
msgid "Eh? You thought we was going to do the guttin' together? That's rich!"
msgstr "А? Ты думал, мы будем потрошить их вместе? Ну и насмешил!"

