msgctxt "FateEvent:66:0:59"
msgid "Aid the Immortal Flames?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь Бессмертному пламеню?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ムムッ、まだ命が惜しいか！<br>止むを得ん、我が単身乗り込んで、獅子奮迅の活躍を……。
#. de: Pah, was bist du denn für 'ne Memme? Da hat ja mein Hamster mehr Mumm in den Knochen! <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>? Dass ich nicht lache!
#. fr: Je vous suggère alors de quitter les lieux im<shy>mé<shy>dia<shy>te<shy>ment, car ce sera bientôt le chaos.
#. column 56: Ah, an adventurer. And one with fire in <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> eyes, no less. That fire is just what we need.
#. column 57: Spurred by rumors of a new Amalj'aa commander, I arrived outside the beast tribe encampment to find not only that the commander had arrived, but that the foul lizards were preparing to march on Ul'dah!
#. column 58: A request for reinforcements has already been sent via linkshell, but it will be several bells before they arrive, and by then it will be too late. No, we must stop the enemy before they advance, and since we are sorely outnumbered, I believe the only path to victory is to lower morale by targeting both their supplies and their leader.
#. column 59: Aid the Immortal Flames?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:66:0:62"
msgid "Then I suggest you leave this area immediately, for it will soon be engulfed in chaos."
msgstr "Тогда советую немедленно убраться отсюда. Скоро здесь начнётся хаос."

#. ja: 声を掛けたってことは、手伝う気があるのかしら？<br>ここのガーディアンに埋め込まれている、<br>ソウルストーンを集めているの。
#. de: Willst du mir helfen? Natürlich willst du das, nicht wahr? Warum sonst würdest du mich an diesem von den Göttern verlassenen Ort ansprechen, hohoho! Also gut, es geht um Folgendes ...
#. fr: Je le savais<nbsp>! Il me suffisait d'attendre dans le désert pour qu'un<if $gn4>e aventurière<else> aventurier</if> arrive. Je suis naturaliste, j'étudie l'aura magique émise par le temple englouti de Qarn, et je pense que c'est elle qui alimente ces golems de pierre qui garde l'entrée.
#. column 57: If I can learn to disrupt that aura, I may be able to render all the guardians inactive, opening the ruins for further exploration by scholars such as myself. But to do so, I first require the hearts of those very guardians, so I may study how they operate.
#. column 58: Collect soulstones for the naturalist?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Oh, I knew my plan would work!
#. column 62: You would forsake a woman in need? What would the good people of the Adventurers' Guild say to that!?
msgctxt "FateEvent:67:0:56"
msgid "I was right! Stand in the desert long enough, and an adventurer is bound to come calling. So, can one assume you are looking for employment? I am a naturalist studying the magicked aura emitted from the Sunken Temple of Qarn, and I believe this aura is what powers those stone golems which guard the entrance."
msgstr "Я так и знала! Постой в пустыне достаточно долго — и приключенец непременно объявится. Итак, ищешь работу? Я натуралистка, изучаю магическую ауру Затонувшего храма Карна. Думаю, именно она оживляет каменных големов, охраняющих вход."

#. ja: 古代魔法の研究に使うんだけど……<br>あんな堅くて大きいの、私の手には余るんですもの。
#. de: Für meine Studien altertümlicher Magie benötige ich Golem-Seelensteine und davon gibt's hier reichlich. Nur: Unglück<shy>licher<shy>weise trennen sich die Golems bloß ungern davon und mir fehlen die schlagenden Argumente, sie vom Gegenteil zu überzeugen.
#. fr: Si je savais comment brouiller cette aura, je pourrais peut-être désactiver ces gardiens et accéder aux ruines pour les explorer mi<shy>nu<shy>tieu<shy>se<shy>ment. Mais, pour ce faire, il me faut tout d'abord le cœur d'un de ces gardiens pour comprendre comment ils fonctionnent.
#. column 56: I was right! Stand in the desert long enough, and an adventurer is bound to come calling. So, can one assume you are looking for employment? I am a naturalist studying the magicked aura emitted from the Sunken Temple of Qarn, and I believe this aura is what powers those stone golems which guard the entrance.
#. column 58: Collect soulstones for the naturalist?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Oh, I knew my plan would work!
#. column 62: You would forsake a woman in need? What would the good people of the Adventurers' Guild say to that!?
msgctxt "FateEvent:67:0:57"
msgid "If I can learn to disrupt that aura, I may be able to render all the guardians inactive, opening the ruins for further exploration by scholars such as myself. But to do so, I first require the hearts of those very guardians, so I may study how they operate."
msgstr "Если я научусь нарушать эту ауру, то, возможно, смогу отключить стражей и открыть руины для исследований. Но сперва мне нужны сердца этих самых стражей, чтобы понять, как они устроены."

#. ja: 手を貸しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Seelensteine für die Naturkundlerin sammeln?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Récupérer des pierres d'âme pour la naturaliste<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: I was right! Stand in the desert long enough, and an adventurer is bound to come calling. So, can one assume you are looking for employment? I am a naturalist studying the magicked aura emitted from the Sunken Temple of Qarn, and I believe this aura is what powers those stone golems which guard the entrance.
#. column 57: If I can learn to disrupt that aura, I may be able to render all the guardians inactive, opening the ruins for further exploration by scholars such as myself. But to do so, I first require the hearts of those very guardians, so I may study how they operate.
#. column 60: Oh, I knew my plan would work!
#. column 62: You would forsake a woman in need? What would the good people of the Adventurers' Guild say to that!?
