msgid "Escort the son of Saint Coinach?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Сопроводить сына святого Койнаха?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ダメですか……残念です。<br>その、無理を言って、すみませんでしたね。<br>他を当たってみることにします。
#. de: Oh nein, was mache ich jetzt nur?!<br>Ich meine, es ist zwar nicht gefährlich, aber ... aber ... \<schluck>
#. fr: J'imagine que c'était un peu trop vous demander... Enfin, je respecte votre décision. Nous avons tous nos priorités.
#. column 56: Oh, thank the saints! You would <i>not</i> believe how long I have been standing here waiting for a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your ilk to happen by. Might I ask of you a favor?
#. column 57: I am one of a cadre of researchers, scholars, and naturalists who go by the collective name “the Sons of Saint Coinach.” I am returning from a foray into the lowlands of Coerthas to collect supplies, but find the road back to our site of study overrun with terrible creatures who were not there on my way north.
#. column 58: If you would be so kind as to lend me your talents in clearing the path and keeping my head securely attached to my shoulders, I would see to it that you are suitably rewarded.
#. column 59: Escort the son of Saint Coinach?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:128:0:62"
msgid "I suppose it was too much to ask... Well, I shan't think any less of you for your decision. We all have our priorities."
msgstr "Видимо, я слишком многого просил... Что ж, я не стану хуже думать о вас из-за отказа. У каждого свои приоритеты."

#. ja: 冒険者！？　た、助かった……。<br>すまない、あんたの手を貸してほしいんだ。
#. de: Ein<if $gn4>e Abenteurerin<else> Abenteurer</if>! Du musst mir helfen!
#. fr: Je vous en prie,  <if $gn4>aventurière<else>aventurier</if>. Je n'ai pas beaucoup de temps. Ils sont tout près... Ils peuvent me trouver d'un instant à l'autre<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Who, you ask? The wolves, who else? Can you not hear them? The rumble of their growl, the incessant pattering of their feet, and the howls... Those bloodcurdling howls... A pack has been on my trail since I wounded my leg in an iron trap intended for those very beasts. Oh, the irony of it all!
#. column 58: I have used what little strength I have left to make it this far, but the wound has begun to ache, and I do not believe I can outrun the pack any longer. Please, I beg of you. Beat the wolves back just long enough that I might make it to Camp Dragonhead and the succor behind her walls.
#. column 59: Escort the injured knight?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then you have damned me to death's cold grip...
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:129:0:56"
msgid "Please, good adventurer. I haven't much time. <i>They</i> are so close now... It is only a matter of time before they find me."
msgstr "Прошу вас, добрый искатель приключений. У меня мало времени. <i>Они</i> уже совсем близко... Рано или поздно они меня найдут."

#. ja: 口に出すのも恥ずかしいが、偵察中に遭難しちまってな。<br>おまけにウルフどもに見つかっちまってさぁ、<br>この雪ン中をさんざんっぱら、追いかけ回される始末よ。
#. de: Es ist beschämend für mich als Ritter aus dem Hause Fortemps, doch ich wurde von Wölfen angefallen und übel zugerichtet. Ich habe versucht sie zu vertreiben, aber langsam verlassen mich die Kräfte.
#. fr: Qui ça<nbsp>? Eh bien, les loups<nbsp>! Vous ne les entendez pas<nbsp>? Leurs grognements, le bruit de leurs pattes et leurs hurlements... Ils me glacent le sang... Cette meute est à mes trousses depuis que j'ai marché sur un piège à loups. Quelle ironie...
#. column 56: Please, good adventurer. I haven't much time. <i>They</i> are so close now... It is only a matter of time before they find me.
#. column 58: I have used what little strength I have left to make it this far, but the wound has begun to ache, and I do not believe I can outrun the pack any longer. Please, I beg of you. Beat the wolves back just long enough that I might make it to Camp Dragonhead and the succor behind her walls.
#. column 59: Escort the injured knight?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then you have damned me to death's cold grip...
msgctxt "FateEvent:129:0:57"
msgid "Who, you ask? The wolves, who else? Can you not hear them? The rumble of their growl, the incessant pattering of their feet, and the howls... Those bloodcurdling howls... A pack has been on my trail since I wounded my leg in an iron trap intended for those very beasts. Oh, the irony of it all!"
msgstr "Кто, спрашиваете? Волки, кто же ещё? Разве не слышите? Их рычание, топот лап и вой... От этого воя кровь стынет в жилах... Стая преследует меня с тех пор, как я угодил ногой в железный капкан, поставленный на этих самых зверей. Вот уж ирония!"

#. ja: なんとか頑張って追っ払おうにも、<br>逃げ回ったからクタクタで、それもままならねぇ……。<br>なぁあんた、少し手伝っちゃくれないか？
#. de: Wenn du mich in die Nähe des Camps geleiten könntest ...? Den Rest schaffe ich dann.
#. fr: J'ai réussi à arriver jusqu'ici, mais ma blessure me fait ter<shy>ri<shy>ble<shy>ment souffrir et je suis à bout de forces. Je vous en supplie, escortez-moi jusqu'au camp de la Tête du dragon.
#. column 56: Please, good adventurer. I haven't much time. <i>They</i> are so close now... It is only a matter of time before they find me.
#. column 57: Who, you ask? The wolves, who else? Can you not hear them? The rumble of their growl, the incessant pattering of their feet, and the howls... Those bloodcurdling howls... A pack has been on my trail since I wounded my leg in an iron trap intended for those very beasts. Oh, the irony of it all!
#. column 59: Escort the injured knight?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then you have damned me to death's cold grip...
msgctxt "FateEvent:129:0:58"
msgid "I have used what little strength I have left to make it this far, but the wound has begun to ache, and I do not believe I can outrun the pack any longer. Please, I beg of you. Beat the wolves back just long enough that I might make it to Camp Dragonhead and the succor behind her walls."
msgstr "На последних силах я добрался сюда, но рана уже даёт о себе знать. Боюсь, от стаи мне больше не убежать. Прошу, задержите волков, пока я не доберусь до Лагеря Драконьей Головы и не окажусь за его стенами."

#. ja: 手を貸しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Beschützt du den Ritter vor den Wölfen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Escorter le chevalier blessé<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Please, good adventurer. I haven't much time. <i>They</i> are so close now... It is only a matter of time before they find me.
#. column 57: Who, you ask? The wolves, who else? Can you not hear them? The rumble of their growl, the incessant pattering of their feet, and the howls... Those bloodcurdling howls... A pack has been on my trail since I wounded my leg in an iron trap intended for those very beasts. Oh, the irony of it all!
#. column 58: I have used what little strength I have left to make it this far, but the wound has begun to ache, and I do not believe I can outrun the pack any longer. Please, I beg of you. Beat the wolves back just long enough that I might make it to Camp Dragonhead and the succor behind her walls.
#. column 62: Then you have damned me to death's cold grip...
