msgctxt "FateEvent:129:0:59"
msgid "Escort the injured knight?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Сопроводить раненого рыцаря?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: そうかい、じゃあしょうがねぇな……。<br>わかったよ、もう少しここで休んでから、<br>自分でなんとかしてみるさ。
#. de: Ah ... Aber du hast Recht. Ein Fortemps muss sich selbst verteidigen können. Das befiehlt die Ritterehre.
#. fr: Vous me condamnez à une mort certaine...
#. column 56: Please, good adventurer. I haven't much time. <i>They</i> are so close now... It is only a matter of time before they find me.
#. column 57: Who, you ask? The wolves, who else? Can you not hear them? The rumble of their growl, the incessant pattering of their feet, and the howls... Those bloodcurdling howls... A pack has been on my trail since I wounded my leg in an iron trap intended for those very beasts. Oh, the irony of it all!
#. column 58: I have used what little strength I have left to make it this far, but the wound has begun to ache, and I do not believe I can outrun the pack any longer. Please, I beg of you. Beat the wolves back just long enough that I might make it to Camp Dragonhead and the succor behind her walls.
#. column 59: Escort the injured knight?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:129:0:62"
msgid "Then you have damned me to death's cold grip..."
msgstr "Значит, ты обрекаешь меня на холодные объятия смерти..."

#. ja: 我々は氷壁調査隊だ。<br>冒険者よ、丁度いいところに現れてくれた。<br>少し、我々の話を聞いてはもらえないだろうか？
#. de: Wir untersuchen die Schneekleid-Felswand. Und da werden wir auch feststecken, wenn du uns nicht hilfst.
#. fr: Un<if $gn4>e aventurière<else> aventurier</if> avec de la bouteille<nbsp>! Nous sommes des naturalistes et nous faisons partie du groupe d'exploration de Manteneige. Nous avons besoin d'aide pour une tâche qui nous dépasse com<shy>plè<shy>te<shy>ment.
#. column 57: Giants. Large ones. The naturalists and I tried to reason with them as we would any other man, and at first we thought we had made some progress─the creatures agreed to let us pass if we answered their riddles. The questions were insanely simple, as one would expect from uneducated brutes, but their giant logic made the riddles impossible to answer correctly.
#. column 58: What is giant and stomps on tiny man's head? A giant, right? No. A giant's <i>foot</i>. A giant's foot! Have you ever heard anything so absurd? So yes. Here we are, stuck between a rock and a party of rock-brained lummoxes. I would be in your debt if you were to teach those cretins a lesson.<br>I will make it worth your while.
#. column 59: Heed the party's request?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Giant's <i>foot</i> my arse... Perhaps if I ask again, they will give me another chance...and this time we shall be prepared!
#. macro: <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if $gn4>her<else>him</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:130:0:56"
msgid "An adventurer! And one with <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> wits about <if $gn4>her<else>him</if>, it would seem. We are with the expeditionary party up at Snowcloak and could use a hand, for we find ourselves in a predicament that my charges' years of study in the scholasticate did not quite prepare them for."
msgstr "Искатель приключений! Да ещё и, похоже, <if $gn4>с головой на плечах<else>с головой на плечах</if>. Мы из экспедиции на Снежном Покрове, и нам нужна помощь. Моих подопечных годы учёбы в семинарии к такому не готовили."

#. ja: 実はこの先でジャイアント族が待ち構えていてな、<br>我々のキャンプに戻れなくて困っているのだ。
#. de: Einige Riesen haben uns den Weg abgeschnitten. Sie lauern uns auf und hindern uns an der Rückkehr ins sichere Camp.
#. fr: Des géants... J'ai essayé de les raisonner. J'ai même cru que nous avions trouvé une solution lorsqu'ils m'ont proposé de nous laisser passer si je parvenais à répondre à leurs énigmes. C'était un jeu d'enfant, car ce ne sont que des brutes sans éducation, mais leur logique est telle qu'ils ont refusé toutes nos réponses.
#. column 56: An adventurer! And one with <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> wits about <if $gn4>her<else>him</if>, it would seem. We are with the expeditionary party up at Snowcloak and could use a hand, for we find ourselves in a predicament that my charges' years of study in the scholasticate did not quite prepare them for.
#. column 58: What is giant and stomps on tiny man's head? A giant, right? No. A giant's <i>foot</i>. A giant's foot! Have you ever heard anything so absurd? So yes. Here we are, stuck between a rock and a party of rock-brained lummoxes. I would be in your debt if you were to teach those cretins a lesson.<br>I will make it worth your while.
#. column 59: Heed the party's request?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Giant's <i>foot</i> my arse... Perhaps if I ask again, they will give me another chance...and this time we shall be prepared!
msgctxt "FateEvent:130:0:57"
msgid "Giants. Large ones. The naturalists and I tried to reason with them as we would any other man, and at first we thought we had made some progress─the creatures agreed to let us pass if we answered their riddles. The questions were insanely simple, as one would expect from uneducated brutes, but their giant logic made the riddles impossible to answer correctly."
msgstr "Гиганты. Самые настоящие здоровяки. Мы с естествоиспытателями попытались договориться с ними как с обычными людьми. Сперва показалось, что дело ладится: твари согласились пропустить нас, если мы отгадаем их загадки. Загадки были до безумия простые — чего ещё ждать от необразованных громил? Но гигантская логика сделала их неразрешимыми."

#. ja: 氷壁調査隊は、その名の通り調査が主任務、<br>ジャイアント族を倒せるほどの戦力は保有していない。<br>そこで冒険者よ、君の力を貸してくれないだろうか？
#. de: Wir sind Forscher, keine Kämpfer! Gegen diese Monstren haben wir keine Chance. Kannst du uns nicht deinen starken Arm leihen?
#. fr: Qu'est-ce qui est géant et écrase les petits hommes<nbsp>? Un géant, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>? Eh bien non, c'est le pied d'un géant<nbsp>! Le pied d'un géant, par<shy>fai<shy>te<shy>ment<nbsp>! On n'a jamais entendu une chose aussi absurde<nbsp>! Bref, nous voilà coincés à cause de ces stupides géants. Si vous acceptiez de leur donner une bonne leçon, je veillerais à ce que votre récompense soit à la hauteur.
#. column 56: An adventurer! And one with <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> wits about <if $gn4>her<else>him</if>, it would seem. We are with the expeditionary party up at Snowcloak and could use a hand, for we find ourselves in a predicament that my charges' years of study in the scholasticate did not quite prepare them for.
#. column 57: Giants. Large ones. The naturalists and I tried to reason with them as we would any other man, and at first we thought we had made some progress─the creatures agreed to let us pass if we answered their riddles. The questions were insanely simple, as one would expect from uneducated brutes, but their giant logic made the riddles impossible to answer correctly.
#. column 59: Heed the party's request?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Giant's <i>foot</i> my arse... Perhaps if I ask again, they will give me another chance...and this time we shall be prepared!
