#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:130:0:59"
msgid "Heed the party's request?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь экспедиции?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: そうか……いや、君を責めはせぬ。<br>しかし、ならばどうしたものか。<br>一度引き返し、援軍を請うべきだろうか……？
#. de: Nein? Sollen wir mit unseren Eispickeln kämpfen?! Was muss man im Dienste der Wissenschaft nicht alles tun!
#. fr: Le pied d'un géant... C'est vraiment pas le pied. Ils me donneront peut-être une nouvelle chance si je leur demande. Et cette fois, nous serons prêts, mes hommes et moi<nbsp>!
#. column 56: An adventurer! And one with <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> wits about <if $gn4>her<else>him</if>, it would seem. We are with the expeditionary party up at Snowcloak and could use a hand, for we find ourselves in a predicament that my charges' years of study in the scholasticate did not quite prepare them for.
#. column 57: Giants. Large ones. The naturalists and I tried to reason with them as we would any other man, and at first we thought we had made some progress─the creatures agreed to let us pass if we answered their riddles. The questions were insanely simple, as one would expect from uneducated brutes, but their giant logic made the riddles impossible to answer correctly.
#. column 58: What is giant and stomps on tiny man's head? A giant, right? No. A giant's <i>foot</i>. A giant's foot! Have you ever heard anything so absurd? So yes. Here we are, stuck between a rock and a party of rock-brained lummoxes. I would be in your debt if you were to teach those cretins a lesson.<br>I will make it worth your while.
#. column 59: Heed the party's request?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:130:0:62"
msgid "Giant's <i>foot</i> my arse... Perhaps if I ask again, they will give me another chance...and this time we shall be prepared!"
msgstr "Ногу гиганта им в <i>задницу</i>... Может, если попрошу ещё раз, они дадут мне второй шанс... и на этот раз мы будем готовы!"

#. ja: 冒険者よ、我々に協力する気はないか？<br>我々は、ここより東の「アドネール占星台」を守護する、<br>デュランデル家の者だ。
#. de: Oh, <if $gn4>eine ausgeruhte Abenteurerin<else>ein ausgeruhter Abenteurer</if>! Stoß doch zu uns!
#. fr: Ravi de faire votre con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ce, <if $gn4>aventurière<else>aventurier</if>. Nous sommes des chevaliers au service de la famille Durendaire qui protégeons l'Observatoire, à l'est d'ici.
#. column 57: We make our way there now in response to an urgent report claiming that a band of giants has descended from the Nail─most likely in search of fire or food─and are heading directly for the walled encampment.
#. column 58: We have been trained to fend off attacks as these, but are not so foolish as to turn down any help that might present itself. What say you? Join us and add another verse to that song the bards will one day sing of your deeds?
msgctxt "FateEvent:131:0:56"
msgid "Well met, brave adventurer. We are knights of House Durendaire tasked with guarding the Observatorium to the east."
msgstr "Приветствую, <if $gn4>отважную искательницу<else>отважного искателя</if> приключений. Мы — рыцари дома Дюрандэр, охраняем обсерваторий к востоку отсюда."

#. ja: 現在、我らが守護するかの地に向かって、<br>ジャイアント族が移動中である。<br>至急、きゃつらへの迎撃作戦を展開せねばならん。
#. de: Wir haben eine interessante Mission zu erfüllen. Riesen sind auf dem Weg hierher, und wir werden sie aufhalten.
#. fr: Nous avons été envoyés ici, car un groupe de géants en provenance de L'Épée se dirigerait en ce moment même vers le camp fortifié.
#. column 56: Well met, brave adventurer. We are knights of House Durendaire tasked with guarding the Observatorium to the east.
#. column 58: We have been trained to fend off attacks as these, but are not so foolish as to turn down any help that might present itself. What say you? Join us and add another verse to that song the bards will one day sing of your deeds?
msgctxt "FateEvent:131:0:57"
msgid "We make our way there now in response to an urgent report claiming that a band of giants has descended from the Nail─most likely in search of fire or food─and are heading directly for the walled encampment."
msgstr "По срочному донесению, отряды гигантов спустились с Иглы — скорее всего, в поисках огня или пищи — и направляются прямо к укреплённому лагерю. Мы уже выдвигаемся туда."

#. ja: 我々にとってきゃつらの相手は手慣れたものだが……<br>万が一の遅れを取ることがあるやもしれぬ。<br>勝利を盤石にするため、汝らの力を貸してくれ！
#. de: Sie haben es auf das Observatorium abgesehen, aber so weit kommen sie nicht. Los, schließ dich uns an!
#. fr: Nous sommes entraînés, mais nous ne sommes pas du genre à refuser l'aide qui s'offre à nous. Qu'en dites-vous<nbsp>? Voulez-vous nous rejoindre et tenter d'apparaître un jour dans les chants et les légendes<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Well met, brave adventurer. We are knights of House Durendaire tasked with guarding the Observatorium to the east.
#. column 57: We make our way there now in response to an urgent report claiming that a band of giants has descended from the Nail─most likely in search of fire or food─and are heading directly for the walled encampment.
msgctxt "FateEvent:131:0:58"
msgid "We have been trained to fend off attacks as these, but are not so foolish as to turn down any help that might present itself. What say you? Join us and add another verse to that song the bards will one day sing of your deeds?"
msgstr "Нас обучали отражать подобные атаки, но мы не станем отказываться от помощи. Что скажешь? Присоединишься к нам и добавишь ещё одну строчку в песню бардов о твоих подвигах?"

#. ja: そこの人……冒険者よね？<br>冒険者同士、あたしに協力してくれないかしら？
#. de: Oh, <if $gn4>eine Kollegin<else>ein Kollege</if>! Sag, kannst du mir nicht kurz zur Hand gehen?
#. fr: Je vous demande pardon. J'ai eu les yeux plus gros que le ventre et j'aurais besoin de l'aide d'un<if $gn4>e collègue aventurière<else> collègue aventurier</if>.
#. column 57: I accepted a levequest to gather up abandoned supplies from the ruins of Camp Revenant's Toll thinking all I would have to do is run in, collect the items, and sneak out. Little did I know the place would be crawling with hungry gigantoads...
#. column 58: How about this─I give you half of the levequest reward in exchange for ridding the area of the nixes? Alright, fifty-one percent, <i>and</i> I'll do the collecting. Do we have an accord?
#. column 59: Do the adventurer's dirty work?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Is that any way to treat a fellow adventurer? What if the tables were turned? What if <i>you</i> were stuck somewhere, arms bloodied and bruised from battling countless beasts, and needed someone to lend you a hand gathering abandoned equipment? Well, you wouldn't find any help from me!
#. macro: <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:132:0:56"
msgid "I beg your pardon, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>. I seem to have bitten off a tad more than I can chew and could use a helping hand from a fellow adventurer."
msgstr "Прошу прощения, <if $gn4>миледи<else>милорд</if>. Похоже, я взялась не за своё дело и не отказалась бы от помощи товарища по приключениям."

#. ja: ギルドの仕事で、遺品の回収に来たんだけど……<br>ほら、そこにニクスが居座ってるでしょ？<br>作業できないのよね、困ったことに。
#. de: Ich hab da von der Gilde so einen blöden Auftrag angenommen, weißt du - Überreste einsammeln. Und da hinten sitzen lauter Nöcken und wollen an <i>meine</i> Überreste ...
#. fr: J'ai accepté un mandat visant à récupérer des effets personnels dans les ruines du camp dévasté. Je pensais que je n'aurais qu'à entrer, récupérer les affaires, et repartir... Mais l'endroit grouille de crapauds géants assoiffés de sang.
#. column 56: I beg your pardon, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>. I seem to have bitten off a tad more than I can chew and could use a helping hand from a fellow adventurer.
#. column 58: How about this─I give you half of the levequest reward in exchange for ridding the area of the nixes? Alright, fifty-one percent, <i>and</i> I'll do the collecting. Do we have an accord?
#. column 59: Do the adventurer's dirty work?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Is that any way to treat a fellow adventurer? What if the tables were turned? What if <i>you</i> were stuck somewhere, arms bloodied and bruised from battling countless beasts, and needed someone to lend you a hand gathering abandoned equipment? Well, you wouldn't find any help from me!
msgctxt "FateEvent:132:0:57"
msgid "I accepted a levequest to gather up abandoned supplies from the ruins of Camp Revenant's Toll thinking all I would have to do is run in, collect the items, and sneak out. Little did I know the place would be crawling with hungry gigantoads..."
msgstr "Я взяла заказ: нужно было собрать оставшиеся припасы из руин лагеря «Звон ревенантов». Думала, забегу, соберу вещи и тихонько улизну. А там, оказывается, полно голодных гигантских жаб..."

#. ja: かといって実力で排除しようにも、<br>ちょっとあたしの手には余る相手で……。<br>そこで、あなたの力を借りたいのよ。
#. de: Du warst doch auch mal ein Neuling als Abenteurer, oder? Bitte hilf mir! Mit einem Nöck werde ich garantiert nicht fertig.
#. fr: Je vous offre la moitié de la récompense pour le mandat si vous éliminez les nix qui errent dans le coin. <br>... Bon, très bien, 51% et je m'occupe de ramasser les objets perdus. D'accord<nbsp>?
#. column 56: I beg your pardon, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>. I seem to have bitten off a tad more than I can chew and could use a helping hand from a fellow adventurer.
#. column 57: I accepted a levequest to gather up abandoned supplies from the ruins of Camp Revenant's Toll thinking all I would have to do is run in, collect the items, and sneak out. Little did I know the place would be crawling with hungry gigantoads...
#. column 59: Do the adventurer's dirty work?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Is that any way to treat a fellow adventurer? What if the tables were turned? What if <i>you</i> were stuck somewhere, arms bloodied and bruised from battling countless beasts, and needed someone to lend you a hand gathering abandoned equipment? Well, you wouldn't find any help from me!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:132:0:58"
msgid "How about this─I give you half of the levequest reward in exchange for ridding the area of the nixes? Alright, fifty-one percent, <i>and</i> I'll do the collecting. Do we have an accord?"
msgstr "Давай так: я отдам тебе половину награды за заказ, а ты очистишь место от никсов. Ладно, пятьдесят один процент, <i>и</i> собирать буду я. По рукам?"

#. ja: 手を貸しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Bist du solidarisch?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Faire le sale boulot de l'aventurière<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: I beg your pardon, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>. I seem to have bitten off a tad more than I can chew and could use a helping hand from a fellow adventurer.
#. column 57: I accepted a levequest to gather up abandoned supplies from the ruins of Camp Revenant's Toll thinking all I would have to do is run in, collect the items, and sneak out. Little did I know the place would be crawling with hungry gigantoads...
#. column 58: How about this─I give you half of the levequest reward in exchange for ridding the area of the nixes? Alright, fifty-one percent, <i>and</i> I'll do the collecting. Do we have an accord?
#. column 62: Is that any way to treat a fellow adventurer? What if the tables were turned? What if <i>you</i> were stuck somewhere, arms bloodied and bruised from battling countless beasts, and needed someone to lend you a hand gathering abandoned equipment? Well, you wouldn't find any help from me!
