msgctxt "FateEvent:132:0:59"
msgid "Do the adventurer's dirty work?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь авантюристке с грязной работой?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ……冷たいのねぇ。<br>じゃあいいわ、もう頼まないから。<br>その代わり、あなたに何かあっても……助けないからね！
#. de: Oh, du bist also schon was Besseres? Dann vergiss es, ich hab dich nie gefragt. Hmpf!
#. fr: Est-ce une façon de traiter une consœur<nbsp>? Et si les rôles étaient inversés<nbsp>? Si c'était vous qui étiez coincé<if $gn4>e</if> quelque part, las<if $gn4>se</if> d'affronter d'innombrables créatures, et que vous aviez besoin d'aide pour récupérer des objets<nbsp>? Eh bien, sachez que je ne vous aiderais pas<nbsp>!
#. column 56: I beg your pardon, <if $gn4>ma'am<else>sir</if>. I seem to have bitten off a tad more than I can chew and could use a helping hand from a fellow adventurer.
#. column 57: I accepted a levequest to gather up abandoned supplies from the ruins of Camp Revenant's Toll thinking all I would have to do is run in, collect the items, and sneak out. Little did I know the place would be crawling with hungry gigantoads...
#. column 58: How about this─I give you half of the levequest reward in exchange for ridding the area of the nixes? Alright, fifty-one percent, <i>and</i> I'll do the collecting. Do we have an accord?
#. column 59: Do the adventurer's dirty work?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:132:0:62"
msgid "Is that any way to treat a fellow adventurer? What if the tables were turned? What if <i>you</i> were stuck somewhere, arms bloodied and bruised from battling countless beasts, and needed someone to lend you a hand gathering abandoned equipment? Well, you wouldn't find any help from me!"
msgstr "Разве так обращаются с товарищем-авантюристом? А если бы мы поменялись местами? Если бы это <i>ты</i> оказался где-то в ловушке, весь в ссадинах и крови после бесчисленных битв со зверьём, и попросил помочь собрать брошенное снаряжение? Ну уж нет, от меня помощи не дождёшься!"

#. ja: さあ、任せたわよ！<br>ガツーンと、やっちゃってッ！！
#. de: Los los los, mach die Viecher schon fertig!
#. fr: Je vous les laisse<nbsp>! J'attendrai que la voie soit libre pour récupérer les objets. Je... je ne voudrais surtout pas vous gêner.
#. column 57: Oh, and don't worry about those nixes outside the camp. I don't think they will be giving us any trouble.
msgctxt "FateEvent:133:0:56"
msgid "They're all yours! I'll wait until the coast is clear before collecting the items. I, uh, wouldn't want to get in your way."
msgstr "Теперь они твои! Подожду, пока всё утихнет, а потом соберу вещи. Я... э-э... не хочу тебе мешать."

#. ja: あ、やるのはキャンプの中のだけでいいからね？<br>外にいるヤツは、放っておいて構わないわ。
#. de: Nur die im Camp musst du erledigen, klar? Die da draußen kümmern uns nicht.
#. fr: Oh, et ne faites pas attention aux nix qui rôdent en dehors du camp. Je ne pense pas qu'ils nous posent problème.
#. column 56: They're all yours! I'll wait until the coast is clear before collecting the items. I, uh, wouldn't want to get in your way.
msgctxt "FateEvent:133:0:57"
msgid "Oh, and don't worry about those nixes outside the camp. I don't think they will be giving us any trouble."
msgstr "А, и не волнуйся насчёт никсов за пределами лагеря. Думаю, они нам не помешают."

#. ja: この周辺で、帝国軍が使う魔導兵器の残骸が<br>見つかったらしくてね……探しに来たんだ。<br>敵の兵器を研究することは、戦略の初歩の初歩だろ？
#. de: Weißt du, was hier in der Gegend rumliegt? Jede Menge Wrackteile von Magitek-Maschinen.
#. fr: Bonjour<nbsp>! J'ai entendu dire qu'un engin magitek avait pris feu non loin d'ici. Je venais voir si je ne pouvais pas en récupérer quelques pièces pour les étudier à la guilde.
#. column 57: Why would I do that, you ask? I believe a wise man once said, “Know thy enemy.” Or...was it “know thine enemy”? I was never that good with letters. No, engineering has always been my strong suit, and I reckoned if I could pore over the parts, I might be able to figure out how they worked.
#. column 58: And if we know how it is them machines run, then we'll be that much closer to knowing how they can be destroyed, if you catch my drift. Now, if I only had some kind soul to help me. \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 59: Help the draughtsman collect engine parts?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: That's the spirit! You have the makings of an engineer yourself, you know. They say the trade's ninety percent inspiration and ninety percent perspiration. Collect me those parts, and you'll be halfway there!
#. column 62: Not interested, eh? Then what<i>ever</i> am I to do with all this gil weighing down my britches? \<wink> \<wink>
msgctxt "FateEvent:134:0:56"
msgid "Well met! I hear tell there was some magitek contraption what caught aflame near these parts. I came looking to see if I couldn't take a few of the scraps back to the guild to study."
msgstr "Приветствую! Слыхал, неподалёку сгорела какая-то магитехническая штуковина. Я пришёл посмотреть, нельзя ли унести несколько обломков в гильдию на изучение."

#. ja: 今回は、連中の使う魔導兵器の核心、<br>「青燐機関の部品」を入手するまたとない好機……<br>って意気込んでたんだけど、これがなかなか大変でさ。
#. de: Damit können wir eine Menge über die garleische Technologie rausfinden. Magitek-Motorenbau! Erdseim-Antrieb! Verstehst du?
#. fr: Pour quoi faire<nbsp>? Il me semble qu'un sage a dit autrefois<nbsp>: “Connais ton ennemi.” Je pense qu'en étudiant les pièces qui les composent, je pourrai découvrir comment ils fonctionnent.
#. column 56: Well met! I hear tell there was some magitek contraption what caught aflame near these parts. I came looking to see if I couldn't take a few of the scraps back to the guild to study.
#. column 58: And if we know how it is them machines run, then we'll be that much closer to knowing how they can be destroyed, if you catch my drift. Now, if I only had some kind soul to help me. \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 59: Help the draughtsman collect engine parts?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: That's the spirit! You have the makings of an engineer yourself, you know. They say the trade's ninety percent inspiration and ninety percent perspiration. Collect me those parts, and you'll be halfway there!
#. column 62: Not interested, eh? Then what<i>ever</i> am I to do with all this gil weighing down my britches? \<wink> \<wink>
msgctxt "FateEvent:134:0:57"
msgid "Why would I do that, you ask? I believe a wise man once said, “Know thy enemy.” Or...was it “know thine enemy”? I was never that good with letters. No, engineering has always been my strong suit, and I reckoned if I could pore over the parts, I might be able to figure out how they worked."
msgstr "Зачем, спрашиваешь? Кажется, один мудрец сказал: «Знай своего врага». Или... «знай врага своего»? С грамотой у меня всегда было туго. Нет, в инженерном деле я силён. Думал, разберу детали и пойму, как всё это работает."

#. ja: そこでだ、部品の回収に力を貸してくれないかい？<br>部品は落ちている兵器の残骸を調べるか……<br>まだ動いている奴をやっつければ、手に入るヨ。
#. de: Wir brauchen Bauteile der Erdseim-Motoren. Woher, das ist einerlei. Birg welche aus den Wrackteilen oder zerstör ein paar aktive Magitek-Maschinen. Ein paar laufen hier nämlich noch rum!
#. fr: Quand nous saurons comment ces machines marchent, nous saurons également comment les détruire. Si seulement j'avais quelqu'un pour m'aider...
#. column 56: Well met! I hear tell there was some magitek contraption what caught aflame near these parts. I came looking to see if I couldn't take a few of the scraps back to the guild to study.
#. column 57: Why would I do that, you ask? I believe a wise man once said, “Know thy enemy.” Or...was it “know thine enemy”? I was never that good with letters. No, engineering has always been my strong suit, and I reckoned if I could pore over the parts, I might be able to figure out how they worked.
#. column 59: Help the draughtsman collect engine parts?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: That's the spirit! You have the makings of an engineer yourself, you know. They say the trade's ninety percent inspiration and ninety percent perspiration. Collect me those parts, and you'll be halfway there!
#. column 62: Not interested, eh? Then what<i>ever</i> am I to do with all this gil weighing down my britches? \<wink> \<wink>
msgctxt "FateEvent:134:0:58"
msgid "And if we know how it is them machines run, then we'll be that much closer to knowing how they can be destroyed, if you catch my drift. Now, if I only had some kind soul to help me. \\<wink> \\<wink>"
msgstr "А если узнаем, как работают эти машины, то поймём и как их уничтожить. Ну, найдись же добрая душа, которая мне поможет. <i>Хе-хе!</i> <i>Хе-хе!</i>"

#. ja: 手を貸しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Hilfst du beim Sammeln?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider le dessinateur à récupérer des pièces de l'engin<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Well met! I hear tell there was some magitek contraption what caught aflame near these parts. I came looking to see if I couldn't take a few of the scraps back to the guild to study.
#. column 57: Why would I do that, you ask? I believe a wise man once said, “Know thy enemy.” Or...was it “know thine enemy”? I was never that good with letters. No, engineering has always been my strong suit, and I reckoned if I could pore over the parts, I might be able to figure out how they worked.
#. column 58: And if we know how it is them machines run, then we'll be that much closer to knowing how they can be destroyed, if you catch my drift. Now, if I only had some kind soul to help me. \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 60: That's the spirit! You have the makings of an engineer yourself, you know. They say the trade's ninety percent inspiration and ninety percent perspiration. Collect me those parts, and you'll be halfway there!
#. column 62: Not interested, eh? Then what<i>ever</i> am I to do with all this gil weighing down my britches? \<wink> \<wink>
