msgctxt "FateEvent:134:0:59"
msgid "Help the draughtsman collect engine parts?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь чертёжнику собрать детали двигателя?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: すばらしいよ、君ィ！<br>君の献身は、必ずや正当に報われるはずだ！
#. de: Ausgezeichnet! Du weißt, worauf's beim Technologiediebstahl ankommt!
#. fr: Formidable<nbsp>! Vous êtes de l'étoffe des ingénieurs, croyez-moi. Ce métier, c'est 99% d'inspiration et 99% de transpiration, comme on dit. Récupérez ces pièces pour moi et vous serez sur la bonne voie.
#. column 56: Well met! I hear tell there was some magitek contraption what caught aflame near these parts. I came looking to see if I couldn't take a few of the scraps back to the guild to study.
#. column 57: Why would I do that, you ask? I believe a wise man once said, “Know thy enemy.” Or...was it “know thine enemy”? I was never that good with letters. No, engineering has always been my strong suit, and I reckoned if I could pore over the parts, I might be able to figure out how they worked.
#. column 58: And if we know how it is them machines run, then we'll be that much closer to knowing how they can be destroyed, if you catch my drift. Now, if I only had some kind soul to help me. \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 59: Help the draughtsman collect engine parts?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Not interested, eh? Then what<i>ever</i> am I to do with all this gil weighing down my britches? \<wink> \<wink>
msgctxt "FateEvent:134:0:60"
msgid "That's the spirit! You have the makings of an engineer yourself, you know. They say the trade's ninety percent inspiration and ninety percent perspiration. Collect me those parts, and you'll be halfway there!"
msgstr "Вот это настрой! Знаешь, из тебя вышел бы отличный инженер. Говорят, в этой работе девяносто процентов вдохновения и девяносто процентов пота. Соберёшь для меня детали — и будешь уже на полпути!"

#. ja: クッ……<br>この手の単純労働は僕向きじゃないんだが……。
#. de: Verflucht. Hoffentlich kommt doch noch einer, der mir die schweren Teile zusammenträgt.
#. fr: Cela ne vous intéresse pas<nbsp>? Que diable vais-je donc pouvoir faire de tous ces gils qui m'encombrent<nbsp>? J'espérais que vous m'aideriez à alléger ma bourse...
#. column 56: Well met! I hear tell there was some magitek contraption what caught aflame near these parts. I came looking to see if I couldn't take a few of the scraps back to the guild to study.
#. column 57: Why would I do that, you ask? I believe a wise man once said, “Know thy enemy.” Or...was it “know thine enemy”? I was never that good with letters. No, engineering has always been my strong suit, and I reckoned if I could pore over the parts, I might be able to figure out how they worked.
#. column 58: And if we know how it is them machines run, then we'll be that much closer to knowing how they can be destroyed, if you catch my drift. Now, if I only had some kind soul to help me. \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 59: Help the draughtsman collect engine parts?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: That's the spirit! You have the makings of an engineer yourself, you know. They say the trade's ninety percent inspiration and ninety percent perspiration. Collect me those parts, and you'll be halfway there!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:134:0:62"
msgid "Not interested, eh? Then what<i>ever</i> am I to do with all this gil weighing down my britches? \\<wink> \\<wink>"
msgstr "Неинтересно, значит? И что же мне теперь <i>делать-то</i> со всеми этими гилами, что оттягивают штаны? <i>Хе-хе!</i> <i>Хе-хе!</i>"

#. ja: ええと……主器がこっちで、補器がこっち。<br>この管があっちに繋がって……と、ゴメンゴメン。<br>で、青燐機関の部品は集められたのかい？
#. de: Mal sehen ... hier ist die Hauptkanone ... und die Reserve. Und die Zuleitung hier ... <br>Oh, 'tschuldige. Hast du Motorbauteile gefunden?
#. fr: Alors, si je mets cette fiche ronde dans ce trou carré... Oh<nbsp>! Vous m'apportez d'autres pièces<nbsp>? Approchez<nbsp>! N'ayez pas peur<nbsp>! Montrez-moi ça<nbsp>!
#. column 60: Ah, more pieces to the puzzle. I shall delight in putting them all together! You can find me here if you happen upon anything else.
#. column 62: Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole.
msgctxt "FateEvent:135:0:56"
msgid "So if I put this round peg into this square hole like so... Oh! Are you here with more parts? Come now. Don't be shy. Let me see the beauties."
msgstr "Так, если вставить этот круглый штырь в квадратное отверстие... О! Ты принёс ещё детали? Ну же, не стесняйся. Дай полюбоваться."

#. ja: おお、すばらしい成果だよ君ィ！<br>おかげで、なかなか数が集まってきたさ。<br>でも……まだ数が足りないね、もう少し頼むよ。
#. de: Wow, nicht schlecht! Damit hätten wir genug ... ach, was sag ich! Wir brauchen noch viel mehr Erdseim-Motor-Bauteile!
#. fr: Ah, d'autres pièces du puzzle. Je vais m'amuser comme un fou à tout remettre en place<nbsp>! Si jamais vous en trouvez d'autres, je serai là.
#. column 56: So if I put this round peg into this square hole like so... Oh! Are you here with more parts? Come now. Don't be shy. Let me see the beauties.
#. column 62: Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole.
msgctxt "FateEvent:135:0:60"
msgid "Ah, more pieces to the puzzle. I shall delight in putting them all together! You can find me here if you happen upon anything else."
msgstr "А, новые кусочки головоломки. С удовольствием соберу их воедино! Если найдёшь ещё, я буду здесь."

#. ja: そうか、では頑張ってくれたまえ。
#. de: Gut, dann viel Erfolg.
#. fr: Rien du tout<nbsp>? Eh bien, continuez à chercher et moi je vais essayer de faire rentrer cette satanée fiche dans ce trou.
#. column 56: So if I put this round peg into this square hole like so... Oh! Are you here with more parts? Come now. Don't be shy. Let me see the beauties.
#. column 60: Ah, more pieces to the puzzle. I shall delight in putting them all together! You can find me here if you happen upon anything else.
msgctxt "FateEvent:135:0:62"
msgid "Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole."
msgstr "Ничего, значит? Ну, продолжай поиски. А я пока попробую запихнуть этот проклятый штырь в отверстие."

#. ja: このあたりにある「魔導兵器の残骸」を調べて、<br>「青燐機関の部品」を持ってきてほしいんだ。
#. de: Untersuch die Wracks der Magitek-Maschinen und bring mir Erdseim-Motor-Bauteile.
#. fr: Trouvez cette machine de guerre et démantelez-la. Je vous récompenserai pour toute pièce que vous m'apporterez.
msgctxt "FateEvent:136:0:56"
msgid "Find that war machine and tear it limb from limb. I'll gladly pay for any piece you bring back."
msgstr "Найди ту боевую машину и разбери её на части. За любую деталь, что принесёшь, я щедро заплачу."

#. ja: いいねいいね、これだけ部品が集まれば、<br>ガレマール帝国の核心技術とて、丸裸になったも同然！
#. de: Sehr schön! Du hast es echt drauf. Jetzt liegen die Geheimnisse der Garlear so offen vor uns wie ein offenes Buch.
#. fr: Avec toutes ces pièces, j'arriverai peut-être à remonter cet engin. Si seulement j'arrivais à comprendre comment faire rentrer cette fiche dans ce trou...
#. column 57: Perhaps there is still a square peg out there somewhere...or perhaps a round hole. Either way, I suppose I still have some time before I start the return journey to the guild. If you have no other pressing matters to attend to... \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 60: Excellent! Not quite the peg I was hoping for, but I'm certain I can find a hole for it.
#. column 62: Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole.
msgctxt "FateEvent:137:0:56"
msgid "With this many parts, I might even be able to reconstruct an entire engine! If I can only figure out how to get that damnable peg into that square hole..."
msgstr "С таким количеством деталей я, пожалуй, смогу собрать целый двигатель! Вот бы ещё понять, как запихнуть этот проклятый штырь в квадратное отверстие..."

#. ja: とはいえ資料となる部品は、いくらあっても困らないんだ。<br>まだ持ってるなら、撤収前までに渡してくれると助かる。<br>もう間もなく、青燐研究所に帰還するんでね。
#. de: Wenn du noch mehr Bauteile hast, immer her damit. Wer weiß, was noch Aufschlussreiches dabei ist? Aber denk dran, dass wir bald ins Erdseim-Labor zurückmüssen.
#. fr: Il y a peut-être une fiche carrée quelque part... ou bien un trou rond. Enfin, je ne rentre pas tout de suite à la guilde. Si vous n'avez rien de mieux à faire, je ne bouge pas d'ici...
#. column 56: With this many parts, I might even be able to reconstruct an entire engine! If I can only figure out how to get that damnable peg into that square hole...
#. column 60: Excellent! Not quite the peg I was hoping for, but I'm certain I can find a hole for it.
#. column 62: Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole.
msgctxt "FateEvent:137:0:57"
msgid "Perhaps there is still a square peg out there somewhere...or perhaps a round hole. Either way, I suppose I still have some time before I start the return journey to the guild. If you have no other pressing matters to attend to... \\<wink> \\<wink>"
msgstr "Может, где-то ещё найдётся квадратный колышек... или круглое отверстие. В любом случае до возвращения в гильдию ещё есть время. Если у вас нет дел поважнее... <i>Хе-хе!</i> <i>Хе-хе!</i>"

#. ja: よしよし、実にすばらしい。<br>また見つけたら、持ってきてくれ。
#. de: Ah, sehr gut. Fast unbeschädigt! Von denen kannst du mir noch mehr bringen.
#. fr: Excellent<nbsp>! Ce n'est pas la fiche que je cherche, mais je pense pouvoir trouver le trou qui lui correspond.
#. column 56: With this many parts, I might even be able to reconstruct an entire engine! If I can only figure out how to get that damnable peg into that square hole...
#. column 57: Perhaps there is still a square peg out there somewhere...or perhaps a round hole. Either way, I suppose I still have some time before I start the return journey to the guild. If you have no other pressing matters to attend to... \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 62: Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole.
msgctxt "FateEvent:137:0:60"
msgid "Excellent! Not quite the peg I was hoping for, but I'm certain I can find a hole for it."
msgstr "Прекрасно! Не совсем тот штырь, что я искал, но уж отверстие для него я найду."

#. ja: そうか、わかった。<br>もし見つけたら、すぐに持ってきてくれるかな？
#. de: Aha, na gut. Wenn du doch noch auf was stößt, bring es gleich zu mir.
#. fr: Rien du tout<nbsp>? Eh bien, continuez à chercher et moi je vais essayer de faire rentrer cette satanée fiche dans ce trou.
#. column 56: With this many parts, I might even be able to reconstruct an entire engine! If I can only figure out how to get that damnable peg into that square hole...
#. column 57: Perhaps there is still a square peg out there somewhere...or perhaps a round hole. Either way, I suppose I still have some time before I start the return journey to the guild. If you have no other pressing matters to attend to... \<wink> \<wink>
#. column 60: Excellent! Not quite the peg I was hoping for, but I'm certain I can find a hole for it.
msgctxt "FateEvent:137:0:62"
msgid "Nothing, eh? Well, you keep searching. I'll keep trying to fit this Twelve-damned peg into this hole."
msgstr "Ничего, значит? Ну, продолжай поиски. А я пока попробую запихнуть этот проклятый штырь в отверстие."

#. ja: 青燐機関の部品、必要な数は集まったよ。<br>あとは青燐研究所に帰って、これを解析してみるだけさ。
#. de: Wir haben genug Erdseim-Maschinen-Bauteile zusammen. Jetzt bringen wir die fette Beute ins Erdseim-Labor!
#. fr: Je dois pouvoir fabriquer une fiche carrée, mais c'est beaucoup moins amusant...
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:138:0:56"
msgid "I suppose I could always <i>make</i> a square peg, but where's the fun in that?"
msgstr "Я, конечно, мог бы <i>сделать</i> квадратный штырь, но где тогда веселье?"

#. ja: あたしぃ、ゴーレムの発生について調査するためにぃ、<br>ゴーレムやスプリガンが持ってるって話のぉ、<br>「石兵のソウルストーン」を集めてるんですぅ。
#. de: Psst, ich verrat dir was. Ich bin dabei, hinter das Geheimnis der Golem-Beseelung zu kommen.
#. fr: Bonjour<nbsp>! Vous êtes un<if $gn4>e aventurière<else> aventurier</if><nbsp>? Mes frères et sœurs du Temple de la Sérénité m'ont dit qu'avec un peu de patience, un<if $gn4>e aventurière<else> aventurier</if> finirait bien par passer par ici. Vous êtes bien un<if $gn4>e aventurière<else> aventurier</if>, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>?
#. column 57: My name is...er...not important. That is what my brothers at the Fane always tell me, anyway. Until I prove my worth to the guild, I am but a leaf on a tree, nameless and one of many. But that will all change when I complete this task!
#. column 58: <i>If</i>, that is, I complete this task... You see, I need to collect golem soulstones so that my brothers might study them...but I can barely cast Stone, let alone a spell that will pacify one of those unholy creatures. Now you, on the other hand, appear as if you have seen a few more battles than I. Would you help a poor conjurer earn her name?
#. column 59: Collect soulstones in the conjurer's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Many thanks! I shall be waiting for you here.
#. column 62: My brothers at the Fane told me some would turn me down. But I shall not let it discourage me! I will earn my name if I have to stand here for an eternity!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:139:0:56"
msgid "Hello there! Are you an adventurer? My brothers and sisters at the Fane told me if I waited long enough an adventurer would wander by soon enough. You <i>are</i> an adventurer, aren't you?"
msgstr "Привет! Ты искатель приключений? Братья и сёстры из нашего храма сказали, что если подождать, то мимо обязательно пройдёт искатель приключений. Ты ведь <i>точно</i> искатель приключений?"

#. ja: でもでもぉ、このあたりの魔物は強くってぇ……<br>あたしの力じゃ歯が立たないんですぅ。
#. de: Dafür untersuche ich Golem-Seelensteine, die das Herz und Zentrum der steinernen Krieger bilden.
#. fr: Je me nomme... euh... c'est sans importance. Enfin, c'est ce que me disent mes frères du Temple de la Sérénité, en tout cas. Tant que je n'aurai pas prouvé ma valeur à la guilde, je ne serai qu'une feuille de l'arbre, anonyme et indiscernable des autres. Mais si j'arrive à terminer cette tâche, ce sera différent.
#. column 56: Hello there! Are you an adventurer? My brothers and sisters at the Fane told me if I waited long enough an adventurer would wander by soon enough. You <i>are</i> an adventurer, aren't you?
#. column 58: <i>If</i>, that is, I complete this task... You see, I need to collect golem soulstones so that my brothers might study them...but I can barely cast Stone, let alone a spell that will pacify one of those unholy creatures. Now you, on the other hand, appear as if you have seen a few more battles than I. Would you help a poor conjurer earn her name?
#. column 59: Collect soulstones in the conjurer's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Many thanks! I shall be waiting for you here.
#. column 62: My brothers at the Fane told me some would turn me down. But I shall not let it discourage me! I will earn my name if I have to stand here for an eternity!
msgctxt "FateEvent:139:0:57"
msgid "My name is...er...not important. That is what my brothers at the Fane always tell me, anyway. Until I prove my worth to the guild, I am but a leaf on a tree, nameless and one of many. But that will all change when I complete this task!"
msgstr "Меня зовут... э-э... неважно. Братья в храме всегда так говорят. Пока я не докажу свою ценность гильдии, я всего лишь один листок среди многих, без имени. Но всё изменится, когда я выполню это задание!"

#. ja: あたしの代わりにぃ、冒険者さんがぁ、<br>「石兵のソウルストーン」を集めてくれませんかぁ？
#. de: Tongolems tragen solche Steine manchmal mit sich, sie spüren darin wohl den leisen Nachhall des verloschenen Lebens ...<br>Sag, hilfst du mir beim Sammeln?
#. fr: Je dois récupérer des pierres d'âme de golem pour que mes frères les étudient, mais je ne suis pas douée pour la magie, alors je suis incapable de lancer un sort pour apaiser ces maudites créatures. Vous voulez bien aider une pauvre élé<shy>men<shy>ta<shy>lis<shy>te à se faire un nom<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Hello there! Are you an adventurer? My brothers and sisters at the Fane told me if I waited long enough an adventurer would wander by soon enough. You <i>are</i> an adventurer, aren't you?
#. column 57: My name is...er...not important. That is what my brothers at the Fane always tell me, anyway. Until I prove my worth to the guild, I am but a leaf on a tree, nameless and one of many. But that will all change when I complete this task!
#. column 59: Collect soulstones in the conjurer's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Many thanks! I shall be waiting for you here.
#. column 62: My brothers at the Fane told me some would turn me down. But I shall not let it discourage me! I will earn my name if I have to stand here for an eternity!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:139:0:58"
msgid "<i>If</i>, that is, I complete this task... You see, I need to collect golem soulstones so that my brothers might study them...but I can barely cast Stone, let alone a spell that will pacify one of those unholy creatures. Now you, on the other hand, appear as if you have seen a few more battles than I. Would you help a poor conjurer earn her name?"
msgstr "<i>Если</i>, конечно, я выполню это задание... Понимаешь, мне нужно собрать души големов, чтобы братья могли их изучить... Но я едва умею творить заклинание Камня, не говоря уж о том, чтобы усмирить этих нечестивых тварей. А ты, похоже, повидал куда больше сражений, чем я. Поможешь бедному чародею заслужить имя?"

#. ja: 調査を手伝いますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Willst du Seelensteine sammeln?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Récupérer des pierres d'âme pour l'élé<shy>men<shy>ta<shy>lis<shy>te<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
