msgid "Collect soulstones in the conjurer's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Собрать камни душ за чародея?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ありがとうございますぅ。<br>よろしくお願いしますねぇ。
#. de: Ich wusste doch, dass das Geheimnis des Lebens niemanden unberührt lässt! Vielen Dank!
#. fr: Merci infiniment. Je ne bouge pas d'ici.
#. column 56: Hello there! Are you an adventurer? My brothers and sisters at the Fane told me if I waited long enough an adventurer would wander by soon enough. You <i>are</i> an adventurer, aren't you?
#. column 57: My name is...er...not important. That is what my brothers at the Fane always tell me, anyway. Until I prove my worth to the guild, I am but a leaf on a tree, nameless and one of many. But that will all change when I complete this task!
#. column 58: <i>If</i>, that is, I complete this task... You see, I need to collect golem soulstones so that my brothers might study them...but I can barely cast Stone, let alone a spell that will pacify one of those unholy creatures. Now you, on the other hand, appear as if you have seen a few more battles than I. Would you help a poor conjurer earn her name?
#. column 59: Collect soulstones in the conjurer's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: My brothers at the Fane told me some would turn me down. But I shall not let it discourage me! I will earn my name if I have to stand here for an eternity!
msgctxt "FateEvent:139:0:60"
msgid "Many thanks! I shall be waiting for you here."
msgstr "Большое спасибо! Буду ждать тебя здесь."

#. ja: そうですかぁ……。<br>わかりましたぁ、他の人にお願いしますよぅ。
#. de: Was? Interessiert dich denn gar nicht, was einen Golem im Innersten zusammenhält?
#. fr: Mes frères du Temple de la Sérénité m'avaient bien dit que ce ne serait pas facile. Mais je ne me laisse pas abattre<nbsp>! Je me ferai un nom, même si ça me prend l'éternité.
#. column 56: Hello there! Are you an adventurer? My brothers and sisters at the Fane told me if I waited long enough an adventurer would wander by soon enough. You <i>are</i> an adventurer, aren't you?
#. column 57: My name is...er...not important. That is what my brothers at the Fane always tell me, anyway. Until I prove my worth to the guild, I am but a leaf on a tree, nameless and one of many. But that will all change when I complete this task!
#. column 58: <i>If</i>, that is, I complete this task... You see, I need to collect golem soulstones so that my brothers might study them...but I can barely cast Stone, let alone a spell that will pacify one of those unholy creatures. Now you, on the other hand, appear as if you have seen a few more battles than I. Would you help a poor conjurer earn her name?
#. column 59: Collect soulstones in the conjurer's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Many thanks! I shall be waiting for you here.
msgctxt "FateEvent:139:0:62"
msgid "My brothers at the Fane told me some would turn me down. But I shall not let it discourage me! I will earn my name if I have to stand here for an eternity!"
msgstr "Братья в храме говорили, что мне могут отказать. Но я не сдамся! Я добьюсь своего, даже если придётся простоять тут целую вечность!"

#. ja: あっ、鉱石を持ってきてくれたんですかぁ？
#. de: Oh, du hast mir Steine gebracht?
#. fr: Avez-vous des pierres d'âme<nbsp>?
#. column 60: Hah hah! Just wait, my brothers! A few more stones and my name shall be mine again!
#. column 62: Are you certain? That bulge there in your pouch seems the exact shape and size of a golem soulstone... Or perhaps I'm merely mistaken.
msgctxt "FateEvent:140:0:56"
msgid "Have you any soulstones?"
msgstr "У тебя найдутся камни души?"

#. ja: 助かりますぅ。<br>もっといっぱい欲しいので、よろしくですぅ！
#. de: Vielen Dank, das hilft mir schon mal einen Schritt weiter. Aber bring mir noch mehr!
#. fr: Ha ha<nbsp>! Attendez un peu, mes frères<nbsp>! Encore quelques pierres et on m'appellera à nouveau par mon prénom<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Have you any soulstones?
#. column 62: Are you certain? That bulge there in your pouch seems the exact shape and size of a golem soulstone... Or perhaps I'm merely mistaken.
msgctxt "FateEvent:140:0:60"
msgid "Hah hah! Just wait, my brothers! A few more stones and my name shall be mine again!"
msgstr "Ха-ха! Вот подождите, братья! Ещё немного камней — и моё имя снова станет моим!"

#. ja: そうですかぁ。<br>じゃあ、がんばってくださいねぇ。<br>待ってますよぉ。
#. de: Nichts gefunden?  Seelensteine sehen ganz anders aus als gewöhnliche. Schau doch noch mal genau!
#. fr: Vraiment<nbsp>? Cette bosse dans votre poche fait la même taille qu'une pierre d'âme de golem... Enfin, je peux me tromper.
#. column 56: Have you any soulstones?
#. column 60: Hah hah! Just wait, my brothers! A few more stones and my name shall be mine again!
msgctxt "FateEvent:140:0:62"
msgid "Are you certain? That bulge there in your pouch seems the exact shape and size of a golem soulstone... Or perhaps I'm merely mistaken."
msgstr "Точно? Вон в сумке у тебя выпуклость точь-в-точь по размеру камня души голема... Или мне только кажется."

#. ja: ゴーレムの発生について調査するためぇ、<br>魔物が持つ「石兵のソウルストーン」集めてますぅ。<br>見つけたらぁ……あたしまで持ってきてくださぁい。
#. de: Ich benötige Golem-Seelensteine, um die magischen Zusammenhänge bei der Golem-Beseelung verstehen zu lernen. Hilf mir und bring mir welche!
#. fr: Les environs grouillent de golems. Quel est l'intérêt de donner vie à autant de ces créatures<nbsp>? Je vais y réfléchir le temps que vous récupériez leurs pierres d'âme.
msgctxt "FateEvent:141:0:56"
msgid "The area is simply crawling with golems. What purpose would anyone have breathing life into so many of these creatures? I suppose I shall ponder on that while you go and collect me their soulstones."
msgstr "В этих краях големов просто полно. Зачем кому-то оживлять столько этих созданий? Пожалуй, подумаю об этом, пока ты будешь собирать их камни души."

#. ja: 必要な量は集まりましたぁ、どうもですぅ。<br>でもでもぉ、いっぱいある分には困らないのでぇ……<br>もっとあったら、持ってきちゃってくださぁい。
#. de: Damit habe ich wohl genug. Puh, das wird ein Schwertransport. Falls du noch welche mit dir rumträgst, nehme ich sie aber gerne.
#. fr: Adelle<nbsp>! Vous entendez ça, mes frères<nbsp>? Je me nomme Adelle<nbsp>! Avec deux L. Non, mettez-en trois<nbsp>! Adellle<nbsp>! Hahaha<nbsp>! Et si l'aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if> me rapporte d'autres pierres d'âme, j'ajouterai peut-être même un autre D.
msgctxt "FateEvent:142:0:56"
msgid "Adelle! Do you hear that, my brothers!? My name is Adelle! With two Ls! No, make it three! Adellle! Hah hah hah! And if this adventurer brings more soulstones, I might just add another D while I'm at it!"
msgstr "Аделль! Слышите, братья?! Меня зовут Аделль! С двумя «л»! Нет, лучше с тремя! Аделлль! Ха-ха-ха! А если этот искатель приключений принесёт ещё камней души, я, пожалуй, добавлю к имени ещё одну «д»."

#. ja: おかげさまで、必要量は集まってますぅ。<br>でもぉ、資料の鉱石はいくらあってもいいのでぇ、<br>まだまだ受け取りますよぉ。
#. de: Ausgezeichnet! Mehr als genug Golemmaterial! Damit finde ich garantiert alles über diese Steinwesen raus. Wenn du noch Steine hast, gib sie mir jetzt.
#. fr: Adelle<nbsp>! Vous entendez ça, mes frères<nbsp>? Je me nomme Adelle<nbsp>! Avec deux L. Non, mettez-en trois<nbsp>! Adellle<nbsp>! Hahaha<nbsp>! Et si l'aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if> me rapporte d'autres pierres d'âme, j'ajouterai peut-être même un autre D.
#. column 60: More soulstones? Oh, you thought I was <i>serious</i> just now? Well, I suppose a few more could not hurt. I won't be adding any more Ds to my name, mind you.
#. column 62: Addellle! It just rolls off the tongue, does it not?
msgctxt "FateEvent:143:0:56"
msgid "Adelle! Do you hear that, my brothers!? My name is Adelle! With two Ls! No, make it three! Adellle! Hah hah hah! And if this adventurer brings more soulstones, I might just add another D while I'm at it!"
msgstr "Аделль! Слышите, братья?! Меня зовут Аделль! С двумя «л»! Нет, лучше с тремя! Аделлль! Ха-ха-ха! А если этот искатель приключений принесёт ещё камней души, я, пожалуй, добавлю к имени ещё одну «д»."

#. ja: ありがとうございますぅ。<br>必要な量は足りてますけど、いただきますねぇ。<br>調査の精度が上がりますからぁ。
#. de: Vielen Dank. Ich habe zwar schon mehr Steine als ich tragen kann, aber ich nehme gerne, was du noch hast.
#. fr: D'autres pierres d'âme<nbsp>? Oh, vous croyiez que j'étais sérieuse<nbsp>? Eh bien, je les prends quand même, mais je ne compte pas ajouter de D à mon prénom.
#. column 56: Adelle! Do you hear that, my brothers!? My name is Adelle! With two Ls! No, make it three! Adellle! Hah hah hah! And if this adventurer brings more soulstones, I might just add another D while I'm at it!
#. column 62: Addellle! It just rolls off the tongue, does it not?
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:143:0:60"
msgid "More soulstones? Oh, you thought I was <i>serious</i> just now? Well, I suppose a few more could not hurt. I won't be adding any more Ds to my name, mind you."
msgstr "Ещё камни души? А, ты подумал, что я <i>серьёзно</i>? Ну, ещё несколько не повредят. Только новых «д» в имени я добавлять не собираюсь."

#. ja: そうですかぁ……。<br>でも、必要量は集まっているのでぇ、大丈夫ですぅ。
#. de: Na, kein Problem. Ich habe ja ohnehin schon genug.
#. fr: Addellle<nbsp>! Ça roule sur la langue, vous ne trouvez pas<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Adelle! Do you hear that, my brothers!? My name is Adelle! With two Ls! No, make it three! Adellle! Hah hah hah! And if this adventurer brings more soulstones, I might just add another D while I'm at it!
#. column 60: More soulstones? Oh, you thought I was <i>serious</i> just now? Well, I suppose a few more could not hurt. I won't be adding any more Ds to my name, mind you.
msgctxt "FateEvent:143:0:62"
msgid "Addellle! It just rolls off the tongue, does it not?"
msgstr "Аделлль! Как звучит, а?"

#. ja: 凶悪なドラゴン族、黄竜「スヴァラ」を知ってるか？<br>そいつが今、「スチールヴィジル」方面に向かっていると、<br>アドネール占星台の観測で判明したんだ。
#. de: Hast du schon von dem grausamen gelben Drachen Svara gehört? Er fliegt gerade in Richtung Stählerne Wacht ...
#. fr: Vous avez entendu parler du dragon Svara<nbsp>? Évidemment que oui. Qui n'a jamais entendu ce maudit nom<nbsp>? Enfin, d'après l'Observatoire, cette vile créature se dirigerait vers le Vigile d'Acier.
#. column 57: We engineers must needs make it back to the Vigil afore Svara does, so that we might ready Bertha─our very own fire-belching cannon. 'Tis the only thing outside the fist of the Fury Herself that'll penetrate the dragon's stone hide.
#. column 58: There's only one problem─if this is aught like every other battle with Svara, the dragon'll have its very own horde of foot soldiers in tow, and my men aren't trained or equipped to deal with the lot of them. Might I ask that you join me for the march to the Vigil?
#. column 59: Protect the engineer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:144:0:56"
msgid "You heard of the dragon Svara? 'Course you have. Ain't a man alive what hasn't heard spoke that curse of a name. Well, word from the Observatorium has it that the foul creature is headed for the Steel Vigil."
msgstr "Слышали о драконе Сваре? Конечно, слышали. Да кто ж не слыхал проклятого имени этой твари! Так вот, в обсерватории выяснили: мерзкая тварь направляется к Стальной страже."

#. ja: 俺たち工作兵は一刻も早く、<br>奴らを迎撃するため、対竜カノン砲を設置しなきゃならん。
#. de: Wir arbeiten fieberhaft an  der Verstärkung der Abwehr. Wir wollen die Bestie mit einer Haubitze abschießen, das ist unsere einzige Chance.
#. fr: Nous devons atteindre cet endroit avant Svara pour préparer nos canons anti-dragon. C'est la seule arme qui peut percer la peau des dragons.
#. column 56: You heard of the dragon Svara? 'Course you have. Ain't a man alive what hasn't heard spoke that curse of a name. Well, word from the Observatorium has it that the foul creature is headed for the Steel Vigil.
#. column 58: There's only one problem─if this is aught like every other battle with Svara, the dragon'll have its very own horde of foot soldiers in tow, and my men aren't trained or equipped to deal with the lot of them. Might I ask that you join me for the march to the Vigil?
#. column 59: Protect the engineer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:144:0:57"
msgid "We engineers must needs make it back to the Vigil afore Svara does, so that we might ready Bertha─our very own fire-belching cannon. 'Tis the only thing outside the fist of the Fury Herself that'll penetrate the dragon's stone hide."
msgstr "Нам, инженерам, нужно добраться до Стальной Стражи раньше Свары и подготовить Берту — нашу огнедышащую пушку. Только она, кроме кулака самой Фурии, способна пробить каменную шкуру дракона."

#. ja: だが、奴らの眷属による妨害が予想される……。<br>冒険者よ、あんたの力で設置作業が終わるまで、<br>俺たち工作兵部隊を守ってくれないか！？
#. de: Allerdings wird Svara sicher nicht alleine kommen. Abenteurer<if $gn4>in</if>, kannst du uns die Biester vom Leib halten, bis wir die Kanone installiert haben?
#. fr: Le seul problème, c'est qu'à chaque combat contre Svara, il faut également affronter sa horde de fidèles, et mes hommes ne sont pas équipés pour cela. Puis-je vous demander de nous accompagner au Vigile<nbsp>?
#. column 56: You heard of the dragon Svara? 'Course you have. Ain't a man alive what hasn't heard spoke that curse of a name. Well, word from the Observatorium has it that the foul creature is headed for the Steel Vigil.
#. column 57: We engineers must needs make it back to the Vigil afore Svara does, so that we might ready Bertha─our very own fire-belching cannon. 'Tis the only thing outside the fist of the Fury Herself that'll penetrate the dragon's stone hide.
#. column 59: Protect the engineer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:144:0:58"
msgid "There's only one problem─if this is aught like every other battle with Svara, the dragon'll have its very own horde of foot soldiers in tow, and my men aren't trained or equipped to deal with the lot of them. Might I ask that you join me for the march to the Vigil?"
msgstr "Есть одна загвоздка: если всё будет как в прошлых битвах со Сварой, дракон явится со своей ордой приспешников. Мои люди не обучены и не снаряжены для боя с ними. Не сопроводишь нас до Стальной Стражи?"

#. ja: 護衛を引き受けますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Hilfst du bei der Verteidigung?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Protéger les ingénieurs<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: You heard of the dragon Svara? 'Course you have. Ain't a man alive what hasn't heard spoke that curse of a name. Well, word from the Observatorium has it that the foul creature is headed for the Steel Vigil.
#. column 57: We engineers must needs make it back to the Vigil afore Svara does, so that we might ready Bertha─our very own fire-belching cannon. 'Tis the only thing outside the fist of the Fury Herself that'll penetrate the dragon's stone hide.
#. column 58: There's only one problem─if this is aught like every other battle with Svara, the dragon'll have its very own horde of foot soldiers in tow, and my men aren't trained or equipped to deal with the lot of them. Might I ask that you join me for the march to the Vigil?
