msgctxt "FateEvent:145:0:59"
msgid "Garrote the gigas?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Распугать гигов?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ですよね～。<br>そんな奇特な方そうそういるもんじゃ<br>ないですよね～。
#. de: Ja, verstehe. Wer würde schon sein Leben für jemand anderen aufs Spiel setzen?
#. fr: Les découvertes d'un mois complet réduites en poussière... Nos confrères de la Trouvaille vont être très déçus...
#. column 56: The gigas! They're everywhere and they won't. Stop. Smashing. Our. Things!
#. column 57: We were on our way back to Ishgard to share this moon's findings with the Holy See when from out of nowhere a band of scantily clad muscle-bound thugs appeared waving their massive weapons, running hither and thither, crushing crates left and right.
#. column 58: It was all my companions and I could do to steal away to safety with whatever we could carry. We are too tuckered to attempt to garrote them by ourselves, and would be more than grateful to <if $gn4>she<else>he</if> who might assist us in driving off the gigas.
#. column 59: Garrote the gigas?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:145:0:62"
msgid "\\<sigh> A whole moon's findings... Gone... The Sons will be devastated..."
msgstr "<i>Эх...</i> Все открытия за целый месяц... пропали... Сыны будут в отчаянии..."

#. ja: イシュガルドにおいて、この「聖ダナフェンの落涙」は、<br>「聖水」の湧く聖なる泉として知られています。
#. de: Wie wär's mit einer Phiole „Sankt Daniffens Tränen“, Abenteurer<if $gn4>in</if>? Das Wasser, das wahre Wunder wirkt!<br>Hast du denn noch nie davon gehört?!
#. fr: Cette eau sacrée, surnommée “larmes de Daniffen”, est utilisée dans un grand nombre de rites sacrés à Ishgard.
#. column 57: 'Tis my business to bottle the water and deliver it to the Holy See. That is...'tis my business to do so when the spring is not teeming with angry water sprites. I can offer a small stipend to any soul brave enough to push their way past the sprites and fill these here phials with tears.
msgctxt "FateEvent:146:0:56"
msgid "Water collected from the Weeping Saint─or Daniffen's Tears as it is more commonly referred to─is used by the church in myriad holy rites."
msgstr "Воду из Плачущего святого — его чаще называют Слёзами Даниффена — церковь использует во множестве священных обрядов."

#. ja: 私も「聖水」を求めてやってきたのですが、<br>突然、危険なウォータースプライトが沸いてしまって……<br>どうか私の代わりに、「聖水」を集めてくれませんか？
#. de: Umso besser. Ich will das Mittel nämlich groß rausbringen und hier kann man es gratis abfüllen! Leider kann ich nicht ran, weil alles voller Wasser-Exergone ist. Willst du nicht für mich schöpfen gehen? Du wirkst so wehrhaft.
#. fr: Je suis venu ici pour collecter de l'eau, mais le problème, c'est que la source grouille d'élémentaires d'eau en colère. J'aurais besoin que quelqu'un trompe la vigilance de ces créatures pour remplir ces fioles de larmes, en échange d'une modeste récompense.
#. column 56: Water collected from the Weeping Saint─or Daniffen's Tears as it is more commonly referred to─is used by the church in myriad holy rites.
msgctxt "FateEvent:146:0:57"
msgid "'Tis my business to bottle the water and deliver it to the Holy See. That is...'tis my business to do so when the spring is not teeming with angry water sprites. I can offer a small stipend to any soul brave enough to push their way past the sprites and fill these here phials with tears."
msgstr "Моё дело — набрать эту воду в бутылки и доставить её в Священный престол. То есть... я бы этим и занимался, если бы источник не кишел разъярёнными водяными спрайтами. Готов заплатить тому, кто не побоится пробраться мимо них и наполнить эти флаконы слезами."

#. ja: あの、「聖水」を持ってきてくれたのでしょうか？
#. de: Hast du schon Wasser für mich abgefüllt?
#. fr: Avez-vous récupéré de l'eau sacrée<nbsp>?
#. column 60: Yes! This is very good, but my client will not be satisfied with any less than what was promised. If you can bring more, I will purchase it off you as I did this delivery.
#. column 62: Have you come for the tears as well? Many pilgrims trace the steps of Saint Daniffen's journey through Coerthas to this place─the place where he met his end at the hands of the Betrayer. But I needn't tell you that if it is true you are a pilgrim yourself.
msgctxt "FateEvent:147:0:56"
msgid "Have you collected any tears?"
msgstr "Нашёл слёзы?"

#. ja: そ……そうです、これです！<br>ああ、これがもっとあれば、助かるのですが……。
#. de: Aah, das ist es! Welch heiliges Schimmern! Mehr, Abenteurer<if $gn4>in</if>, bring mir mehr!
#. fr: Oui<nbsp>! C'est exactement ça, mais il n'y en a pas encore assez. Si vous pouviez en récolter davantage, je vous la rachèterai avec plaisir.
#. column 56: Have you collected any tears?
#. column 62: Have you come for the tears as well? Many pilgrims trace the steps of Saint Daniffen's journey through Coerthas to this place─the place where he met his end at the hands of the Betrayer. But I needn't tell you that if it is true you are a pilgrim yourself.
msgctxt "FateEvent:147:0:60"
msgid "Yes! This is very good, but my client will not be satisfied with any less than what was promised. If you can bring more, I will purchase it off you as I did this delivery."
msgstr "Да! Именно то, что нужно. Но заказчица обещала больше. Если принесёшь ещё, куплю их у тебя, как и эту партию."

#. ja: そうですか……あの、冒険者の方？<br>もしかして、あなたも「聖水」を求めて、<br>ここまでいらっしゃったとかなのでしょうか？
#. de: Du ... hast es doch nicht etwa für dich selbst behalten?!
#. fr: Vous êtes là pour rapporter de l'eau, vous aussi<nbsp>? De nombreux pèlerins marchent sur les traces de Saint Daniffen entre le Coerthas et cet endroit, où il a perdu la vie à cause du traître. Mais pas besoin de vous ennuyer avec cela<nbsp>; vous savez déjà tout cela si vous êtes un<if $gn4>e pèlerine<else> pèlerin</if>.
#. column 56: Have you collected any tears?
#. column 60: Yes! This is very good, but my client will not be satisfied with any less than what was promised. If you can bring more, I will purchase it off you as I did this delivery.
msgctxt "FateEvent:147:0:62"
msgid "Have you come for the tears as well? Many pilgrims trace the steps of Saint Daniffen's journey through Coerthas to this place─the place where he met his end at the hands of the Betrayer. But I needn't tell you that if it is true you are a pilgrim yourself."
msgstr "Ты тоже пришёл за слезами? Многие пилигримы идут по следам святого Даниффена через Коэртас к месту, где его убил Предатель. Но если ты и сам пилигрим, мне незачем тебе это объяснять."

#. ja: これだけあれば、式典で注文された量には事足ります。<br>とはいえ、予備もいくらかは必要ですので……<br>まだ「聖水」をお持ちなら、ぜひ私にお譲りください。<br>
#. de: Damit habe ich genug für alle Kunden bei der Zeremonie. Und dabei fällt mir ein, dass ich noch eine Menge vorbereiten muss. Ich wäre dir also dankbar, wenn du für mich weiterschöpfst - als Reserve.
#. fr: Il doit y en avoir assez pour les prochains rites. Mon client sera content<nbsp>! Mais si vous m'en rapportez encore, il me l'achètera sûrement pour d'autres occasions.
msgctxt "FateEvent:148:0:56"
msgid "I believe I have more than enough now for my client, but I will not avert my eyes from opportunity when she is staring me right in the face. The Holy See is a big place. I'm certain I can locate a cardinal or bishop who is in need of my services."
msgstr "Думаю, для моей заказчицы уже достаточно. Но упускать возможность, которая сама идёт в руки, я не стану. Священный престол велик — наверняка найдётся кардинал или епископ, которому понадобятся мои услуги."

#. ja: すでに「聖水」は必要量集まったのですが、<br>何があるかわかりませんし、余分に用意したいのです。<br>まだ「聖水」をお持ちでしたら、いただきますよ？
#. de: Ich habe zwar schon genug von Sankt Daniffens Tränen, aber ein bisschen mehr könnte ich noch tragen. Bring mir so viel du nur schöpfen kannst!
#. fr: Je pense en savoir suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment pour mon client, mais je ne peux quand même pas refuser une telle opportunité. Ishgard est une grande ville. Je pense pouvoir y trouver un cardinal ou un évêque qui aura besoin de mes services.
#. column 60: Yes, I believe I already have a prospective buyer in mind. Many thanks, adventurer. May the Fury give you strength.
#. column 62: Have you come for the tears as well? Many pilgrims trace the steps of Saint Daniffen's journey through Coerthas to this place─the place where he met his end at the hands of the Betrayer. But I needn't tell you that if it is true you are a pilgrim yourself.
msgctxt "FateEvent:149:0:56"
msgid "I believe I have more than enough now for my client, but I will not avert my eyes from opportunity when she is staring me right in the face. The Holy See is a big place. I'm certain I can locate a cardinal or bishop who is in need of my services."
msgstr "Думаю, для моей заказчицы уже достаточно. Но упускать возможность, которая сама идёт в руки, я не стану. Священный престол велик — наверняка найдётся кардинал или епископ, которому понадобятся мои услуги."

#. ja: ありがとうございます。<br>あなたは、かような善行を為される方です。<br>必ずや神のご加護がありますよ。
#. de: Vielen herzlichen Dank. Sankt Daniffen wird dir deine guten Taten hundertfach vergelten.
#. fr: Oui, je pense avoir un acheteur potentiel. Mille mercis, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if><nbsp>! Puisse les Dieux vous protéger.
#. column 56: I believe I have more than enough now for my client, but I will not avert my eyes from opportunity when she is staring me right in the face. The Holy See is a big place. I'm certain I can locate a cardinal or bishop who is in need of my services.
#. column 62: Have you come for the tears as well? Many pilgrims trace the steps of Saint Daniffen's journey through Coerthas to this place─the place where he met his end at the hands of the Betrayer. But I needn't tell you that if it is true you are a pilgrim yourself.
msgctxt "FateEvent:149:0:60"
msgid "Yes, I believe I already have a prospective buyer in mind. Many thanks, adventurer. May the Fury give you strength."
msgstr "Да, кажется, я уже знаю, кому их продать. Большое спасибо, искатель приключений. Да укрепит тебя Фурия."

#. ja: そうですか……。<br>あの、もしかして……あなたご自身も、<br>式典に「聖水」を持っていかれるおつもりなのですか？
#. de: Gar nichts? Das ist höchst verdächtig ... Wehe, wenn ich dich bei der Zeremonie als Konkurrenten wiedertreffe!
#. fr: Vous êtes là pour les larmes, vous aussi<nbsp>? De nombreux pèlerins marchent sur les pas de Saint Daniffen entre Coerthas et cet endroit, là où il a perdu la vie à cause du Traître. Mais pas besoin de vous ennuyer<nbsp>; vous savez déjà tout cela si vous êtes un<if $gn4>e pèlerine<else> pèlerin</if>.
#. column 56: I believe I have more than enough now for my client, but I will not avert my eyes from opportunity when she is staring me right in the face. The Holy See is a big place. I'm certain I can locate a cardinal or bishop who is in need of my services.
#. column 60: Yes, I believe I already have a prospective buyer in mind. Many thanks, adventurer. May the Fury give you strength.
msgctxt "FateEvent:149:0:62"
msgid "Have you come for the tears as well? Many pilgrims trace the steps of Saint Daniffen's journey through Coerthas to this place─the place where he met his end at the hands of the Betrayer. But I needn't tell you that if it is true you are a pilgrim yourself."
msgstr "Ты тоже пришёл за слезами? Многие пилигримы идут по следам святого Даниффена через Коэртас к месту, где его убил Предатель. Но если ты и сам пилигрим, мне незачем тебе это объяснять."

#. ja: そこの冒険者の人、力を貸してもらえないかな？<br>自分、ここの青燐精製所の技師なんだけど……<br>あんたみたいな冒険者サンに、頼みたいことあんのさ。
#. de: Oh, wie gerufen. Ein freiwilliger Helfer. Geh mir doch mal kurz zur Hand, ja?
#. fr: Tel un chevalier en armure étincelante sorti tout droit des temps jadis, vous avez traversé la brume bleue sur votre fidèle destrier pour venir en aide à un pauvre homme dans le besoin.
#. column 57: Oh, I apologize. My colleagues tell me I have a tendency to wax dramaturgical when it comes to asking someone for their aid. I am but a humble draughtsman, toiling in this terrible place to hammer out a meager existence for me and my wretched wife.
#. column 58: Oh, there I go again. Alright, here's the rub─we at the processing plant require earth cores to maintain the stability of the raw ceruleum piped in from the mines. As we are but mere engineers, we must look to adventurers to obtain those cores. So, what say you?
#. column 59: Slay earth sprites for their cores?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Huzzah! You have my undying thanks, friend!
#. column 62: Oh, woe betide the young man who merely wallowed in a mire of his own sorrow as he watched his knight saunter slowly off into the setting sun!
msgctxt "FateEvent:150:0:56"
msgid "Like a knight in shining armor, from a long time ago, you have ridden forth from the blue mists on your gallant steed; come to help a poor man crippled by his inane inability to help himself!"
msgstr "Словно рыцарь в сверкающих доспехах из давних времён, ты прискакал на благородном скакуне сквозь синюю мглу — спасти беднягу, который сам себе помочь не в силах!"

#. ja: ここでやってる青燐水の精製には触媒として、<br>「アーススプライトの核」を使用しているんだけどね……<br>あいにく、うっかりと在庫を切らしちゃった。
#. de: Ich bin von der Amajina AG und muss eine Riesenmenge Erd-Exergon-Kerne auftreiben. Die technischen Details erspar ich dir, aber wir brauchen sie als Katalysator bei der Erdseim-Raffinierung.
#. fr: Ah, mes excuses. Mes collègues me disent que j'ai une certaine tendance aux élans dramatiques quand j'ai besoin d'aide. Je ne suis qu'un simple ingénieur venu ici pour mener une vie paisible avec ma femme.
#. column 56: Like a knight in shining armor, from a long time ago, you have ridden forth from the blue mists on your gallant steed; come to help a poor man crippled by his inane inability to help himself!
#. column 58: Oh, there I go again. Alright, here's the rub─we at the processing plant require earth cores to maintain the stability of the raw ceruleum piped in from the mines. As we are but mere engineers, we must look to adventurers to obtain those cores. So, what say you?
#. column 59: Slay earth sprites for their cores?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Huzzah! You have my undying thanks, friend!
#. column 62: Oh, woe betide the young man who merely wallowed in a mire of his own sorrow as he watched his knight saunter slowly off into the setting sun!
msgctxt "FateEvent:150:0:57"
msgid "Oh, I apologize. My colleagues tell me I have a tendency to wax dramaturgical when it comes to asking someone for their aid. I am but a humble draughtsman, toiling in this terrible place to hammer out a meager existence for me and my wretched wife."
msgstr "Ах, простите. Коллеги говорят, что, когда прошу о помощи, я порой впадаю в излишний драматизм. Я всего лишь скромный чертёжник, вкалываю в этом ужасном месте, чтобы кое-как прокормить себя и свою несчастную жену."

#. ja: それで周辺の「アーススプライト」から調達できんかと、<br>思ってみたりもしたんだが……自分、戦闘はからっきしで。<br>冒険者サン、自分の代わりに集めてくれないかな？
#. de: Ich hab mich nie gefragt, wo die Kerne herkommen, aber wahrscheinlich von Erd-Exergonen, oder? Leider bin ich bin aber nicht Krieger genug, um selbst welche zu entkernen. Aber für dich ist das sicher ein Leichtes, was? Besorg mir doch meinen Katalysator und du leistest einen wertvollen Beitrag zur Erdseim-Versorgung Eorzeas.
#. fr: Oh, je m'épanche à nouveau. Bref, l'usine de céruleum veut des noyaux d'élémentaire de terre pour stabiliser le céruleum extrait dans les mines. Nous ne sommes que des ingénieurs, alors nous demandons aux aventuriers de nous fournir ces noyaux. Qu'en dites-vous<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Like a knight in shining armor, from a long time ago, you have ridden forth from the blue mists on your gallant steed; come to help a poor man crippled by his inane inability to help himself!
#. column 57: Oh, I apologize. My colleagues tell me I have a tendency to wax dramaturgical when it comes to asking someone for their aid. I am but a humble draughtsman, toiling in this terrible place to hammer out a meager existence for me and my wretched wife.
#. column 59: Slay earth sprites for their cores?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Huzzah! You have my undying thanks, friend!
#. column 62: Oh, woe betide the young man who merely wallowed in a mire of his own sorrow as he watched his knight saunter slowly off into the setting sun!
msgctxt "FateEvent:150:0:58"
msgid "Oh, there I go again. Alright, here's the rub─we at the processing plant require earth cores to maintain the stability of the raw ceruleum piped in from the mines. As we are but mere engineers, we must look to adventurers to obtain those cores. So, what say you?"
msgstr "Вот, опять я за своё. Ладно, дело такое: для устойчивой работы завода нам нужны ядра земли — они стабилизируют сырой церулеум, который поступает из шахт. Мы, простые инженеры, сами их не добудем, вот и обращаемся к искателям приключений. Ну что скажешь?"

#. ja: 力を貸しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Erfüllst du den Bedarf des Konstrukteurs?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Tuer des élémentaires de terre pour obtenir leurs noyaux<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Like a knight in shining armor, from a long time ago, you have ridden forth from the blue mists on your gallant steed; come to help a poor man crippled by his inane inability to help himself!
#. column 57: Oh, I apologize. My colleagues tell me I have a tendency to wax dramaturgical when it comes to asking someone for their aid. I am but a humble draughtsman, toiling in this terrible place to hammer out a meager existence for me and my wretched wife.
#. column 58: Oh, there I go again. Alright, here's the rub─we at the processing plant require earth cores to maintain the stability of the raw ceruleum piped in from the mines. As we are but mere engineers, we must look to adventurers to obtain those cores. So, what say you?
#. column 60: Huzzah! You have my undying thanks, friend!
#. column 62: Oh, woe betide the young man who merely wallowed in a mire of his own sorrow as he watched his knight saunter slowly off into the setting sun!
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:150:0:59"
msgid "Slay earth sprites for their cores?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Убить земляных спрайтов и забрать их ядра?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 力を貸してくれるんかい！？<br>いやぁ、助かる助かる、あーりがとぉー！<br>「アーススプライトの核」、よろしく頼むよ！
#. de: Im Ernst? Dann danke ich dir schon mal. Erd-Exergone, nichts anderes, verstanden?
#. fr: Formidable<nbsp>! Merci infiniment<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Like a knight in shining armor, from a long time ago, you have ridden forth from the blue mists on your gallant steed; come to help a poor man crippled by his inane inability to help himself!
#. column 57: Oh, I apologize. My colleagues tell me I have a tendency to wax dramaturgical when it comes to asking someone for their aid. I am but a humble draughtsman, toiling in this terrible place to hammer out a meager existence for me and my wretched wife.
#. column 58: Oh, there I go again. Alright, here's the rub─we at the processing plant require earth cores to maintain the stability of the raw ceruleum piped in from the mines. As we are but mere engineers, we must look to adventurers to obtain those cores. So, what say you?
#. column 59: Slay earth sprites for their cores?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Oh, woe betide the young man who merely wallowed in a mire of his own sorrow as he watched his knight saunter slowly off into the setting sun!
msgctxt "FateEvent:150:0:60"
msgid "Huzzah! You have my undying thanks, friend!"
msgstr "Ура! Друг, век не забуду твою помощь!"

#. ja: んむっ……そっかぁ、わかった。<br>無理には頼まないよ、他の人を当たってみるさ。
#. de: Ah. Na, da kann man nichts machen. Ich überleg mir schon noch was.
#. fr: Oh, pauvre de moi. La tristesse m'envahit alors que mon chevalier s'éloigne lentement dans le soleil couchant<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Like a knight in shining armor, from a long time ago, you have ridden forth from the blue mists on your gallant steed; come to help a poor man crippled by his inane inability to help himself!
#. column 57: Oh, I apologize. My colleagues tell me I have a tendency to wax dramaturgical when it comes to asking someone for their aid. I am but a humble draughtsman, toiling in this terrible place to hammer out a meager existence for me and my wretched wife.
#. column 58: Oh, there I go again. Alright, here's the rub─we at the processing plant require earth cores to maintain the stability of the raw ceruleum piped in from the mines. As we are but mere engineers, we must look to adventurers to obtain those cores. So, what say you?
#. column 59: Slay earth sprites for their cores?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Huzzah! You have my undying thanks, friend!
msgctxt "FateEvent:150:0:62"
msgid "Oh, woe betide the young man who merely wallowed in a mire of his own sorrow as he watched his knight saunter slowly off into the setting sun!"
msgstr "Ах, горе мне! Молодой человек лишь погрузился в пучину печали, глядя, как его рыцарь медленно удаляется навстречу закату!"

#. ja: 頼んだのは「アーススプライトの核」だ。<br>青燐水を精製するとき、触媒に使うシロモノでね。<br>よろしく頼むよ、冒険者サン。
#. de: Erd-Exergon-Kerne, bitte. In Massen. Und schnell, sonst steht die Erdseim-Produktion.
#. fr: On peut généralement trouver des noyaux d'élémentaires à Brumebleue, des restes d'élémentaires disparus il y a longtemps. Mais si nous attendions patiemment qu'un nombre suffisant d'élémentaires meurent de façon naturelle pour se procurer leurs noyaux, nous serions morts et enterrés avant d'avoir ce dont on a besoin. Non, il n'y a qu'un moyen, s'en procurer sur des élémentaires vivants.
#. column 57: The cores you collect will be used to fortify the foundations of the processing plant and suppress any vibrations that may come from the nearby fighting─vibrations that could cause an unstable piece of raw ceruleum to ignite, and bring the entire mountain crashing down upon us.
#. column 58: But enough of the chitchat. I shall be waiting here for your triumphant return.
msgctxt "FateEvent:151:0:56"
msgid "Earth cores can ofttimes be found lying about Bluefog─the final remnants of some long-dead sprite. However, if we were to wait for enough sprites to perish of natural causes before collecting their cores, we would both be old and grey before obtaining a sufficient amount to work with. No, the quickest way to the cores is by taking them from the live sprites."
msgstr "Ядра земли нередко попадаются в Синей мгле — это остатки давно погибших спрайтов. Но если ждать, пока спрайтов наберётся достаточно и они умрут своей смертью, мы с вами состаримся, прежде чем соберём нужное количество. Нет, быстрее всего добыть ядра у живых спрайтов."

#. ja: 「アーススプライトの核」は、<br>近くにいる「アーススプライト」を倒しても手に入るし、<br>落ちてるのを集めてくれてもいい、どっちも一緒のもんだ。
#. de: Erleg doch ein paar Erd-Exergone, um an die Kerne zu gelangen. Sammeln müsste man sie aber eigentlich auch können, ist ja nichts weiter als erdelementare Energie.
#. fr: Les noyaux récupérés permettront de renforcer les fondations de l'usine de céruleum et de réduire les vibrations des combats alentour, vibrations qui pourraient causer la combustion d'un morceau de céruleum instable et faire s'effondrer toute la montagne.
#. column 56: Earth cores can ofttimes be found lying about Bluefog─the final remnants of some long-dead sprite. However, if we were to wait for enough sprites to perish of natural causes before collecting their cores, we would both be old and grey before obtaining a sufficient amount to work with. No, the quickest way to the cores is by taking them from the live sprites.
#. column 58: But enough of the chitchat. I shall be waiting here for your triumphant return.
msgctxt "FateEvent:151:0:57"
msgid "The cores you collect will be used to fortify the foundations of the processing plant and suppress any vibrations that may come from the nearby fighting─vibrations that could cause an unstable piece of raw ceruleum to ignite, and bring the entire mountain crashing down upon us."
msgstr "Собранные ядра укрепят основание завода и приглушат вибрацию от боёв поблизости. Иначе сырой церулеум может вспыхнуть, а вместе с ним обрушится и вся гора."

#. ja: ともかく、数がいるんだよ。<br>たっくさん頼むぜ。
#. de: Wie du es machst, ist mir gleich. Hauptsache, du lieferst mir viel.
#. fr: Mais assez parlé. Je vous attendrai ici.
#. column 56: Earth cores can ofttimes be found lying about Bluefog─the final remnants of some long-dead sprite. However, if we were to wait for enough sprites to perish of natural causes before collecting their cores, we would both be old and grey before obtaining a sufficient amount to work with. No, the quickest way to the cores is by taking them from the live sprites.
#. column 57: The cores you collect will be used to fortify the foundations of the processing plant and suppress any vibrations that may come from the nearby fighting─vibrations that could cause an unstable piece of raw ceruleum to ignite, and bring the entire mountain crashing down upon us.
msgctxt "FateEvent:151:0:58"
msgid "But enough of the chitchat. I shall be waiting here for your triumphant return."
msgstr "Ну, хватит болтать. Буду ждать твоего триумфального возвращения."

#. ja: どうしたい冒険者サン、<br>「アーススプライトの核」を持ってきてくれたんかい？
#. de: Bringst du mir Erd-Exergon-Kerne?
#. fr: Avez-vous trouvé d'autres noyaux<nbsp>?
#. column 60: Huzzah, huzzah! 'Twas fate that brought us together. 'Twas cores that strengthened our bonds! 'Tis <i>more</i> cores that will <i>further</i> strengthen our bonds!
#. column 62: You would not think of keeping those cores for yourself now, would you? What good is an earth core to an adventurer other than to sell and line <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> pockets with gil?
msgctxt "FateEvent:152:0:56"
msgid "Well then, have you found any cores yet?"
msgstr "Ну что, ядра нашёл?"

#. ja: そうそう、これだよこれ！<br>この「アーススプライトの核」が必要だったのさ。<br>んじゃ、まだまだ要るんで、どんどん持ってきてくれな！
#. de: Sehr schön. Rein und hervorragend als Katalysator geeignet. Bring mir noch mehr davon!
#. fr: C'est formidable<nbsp>! Le destin vous a mis<if $gn4>e</if> sur ma route<nbsp>! Ces noyaux nous ont rapprochés<nbsp>! Avec d'autres noyaux, nous serions encore plus proches<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Well then, have you found any cores yet?
#. column 62: You would not think of keeping those cores for yourself now, would you? What good is an earth core to an adventurer other than to sell and line <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> pockets with gil?
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:152:0:60"
msgid "Huzzah, huzzah! 'Twas fate that brought us together. 'Twas cores that strengthened our bonds! 'Tis <i>more</i> cores that will <i>further</i> strengthen our bonds!"
msgstr "Ура, ура! Судьба свела нас вместе. Ядра укрепили нашу дружбу! А ещё больше ядер укрепят её <i>ещё</i> <i>сильнее</i>!"

#. ja: いいかい冒険者サン、「アーススプライトの核」だ。<br>こいつを自分のところまで、バンバン持ってきてくれっ！
#. de: Schau nicht in die Luft, ich brauche erdenergiegeladene Kerne! Erd-Exergone musst du dafür ausquetschen. Alles klar?
#. fr: Vous ne voulez pas garder ces noyaux pour vous, quand même<nbsp>? À quoi pourrait bien vous servir un noyau d'élémentaire à part à vous enrichir<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Well then, have you found any cores yet?
#. column 60: Huzzah, huzzah! 'Twas fate that brought us together. 'Twas cores that strengthened our bonds! 'Tis <i>more</i> cores that will <i>further</i> strengthen our bonds!
#. macro: <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:152:0:62"
msgid "You would not think of keeping those cores for yourself now, would you? What good is an earth core to an adventurer other than to sell and line <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> pockets with gil?"
msgstr "Ты ведь не собираешься оставить себе эти ядра? Что авантюристу делать с ядром земли, кроме как продать и набить <if $gn4>карманы<else>карманы</if> гил?"

#. ja: そこの冒険者さん。<br>もしかして「キャンプ・ドラゴンヘッド」まで<br>向かうとかだったりしませんか？
#. de: He! Bist du vielleicht auch nach Camp Drachenkopf unterwegs?
#. fr: Pardonnez-moi, mais iriez-vous par hasard vers le camp de la Tête du dragon<nbsp>? Si c'est le cas, j'ai une proposition à vous faire.
#. column 57: I am an astrologian employed at the Observatorium. I must hurry these readings to a courier in the camp so that he might deliver them to the archbishop.
#. column 58: Usually, a knight of House Durendaire would accompany me, but those stationed at the Observatorium had to make for the Nail to intercept a band of crazed giants come down from the mountain to raid our kitchens and steal our women. And therefore, I must ask you to accompany me.
#. column 59: Escort the astrologian to Camp Dragonhead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: I might have expected as much from an unbeliever. The Holy See is wise to keep its gates shut to the likes of you.
msgctxt "FateEvent:153:0:56"
msgid "Pardon me, but might you be headed north towards Camp Dragonhead? If you are, I have a proposition."
msgstr "Простите, вы случайно не направляетесь на север, в Лагерь Драконьей Головы? Если да, у меня есть к вам предложение."

#. ja: 実は北の「キャンプ・ドラゴンヘッド」まで<br>星読みの結果を至急伝える必要がありまして……。<br>星読みの結果ですか？それは極秘事項で……。
#. de: Ich habe Dokumente von größter Wichtigkeit dort abzuliefern. Eine astrologische Deutung, deren Tragwei... Ähem. Mehr darf ich dazu nicht sagen.
#. fr: Je suis un astrologue de l'Observatoire. Je dois confier ces résultats à un messager pour qu'il les apporte à l'archevêque.
#. column 56: Pardon me, but might you be headed north towards Camp Dragonhead? If you are, I have a proposition.
#. column 58: Usually, a knight of House Durendaire would accompany me, but those stationed at the Observatorium had to make for the Nail to intercept a band of crazed giants come down from the mountain to raid our kitchens and steal our women. And therefore, I must ask you to accompany me.
#. column 59: Escort the astrologian to Camp Dragonhead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: I might have expected as much from an unbeliever. The Holy See is wise to keep its gates shut to the likes of you.
msgctxt "FateEvent:153:0:57"
msgid "I am an astrologian employed at the Observatorium. I must hurry these readings to a courier in the camp so that he might deliver them to the archbishop."
msgstr "Я астролог из обсерватории. Нужно срочно доставить эти расчёты курьеру в лагерь, чтобы он передал их архиепископу."

#. ja: 普段であればお付きのものが同行してくれるのですが、<br>急なことでみな出払っていて…。<br>道中私の身をお守り頂けないでしょうか。
#. de: Ich hätte mir selbst<shy>verständ<shy>lich eine Eskorte mitnehmen sollen, aber ich bin sofort losgestürzt, angesichts der bevorst... Öhöm. Jedenfalls brauche<br>ich - und meine Botschaft! - dringend deinen Schutz.
#. fr: En temps normal, j'aurais dû être accompagné d'un chevalier au service de la maison Durendaire, mais ceux affectés à l'Observatoire ont dû se rendre à L'Épée pour une in<shy>ter<shy>ven<shy>tion. J'aimerais donc vous demander de m'accompagner.
#. column 56: Pardon me, but might you be headed north towards Camp Dragonhead? If you are, I have a proposition.
#. column 57: I am an astrologian employed at the Observatorium. I must hurry these readings to a courier in the camp so that he might deliver them to the archbishop.
#. column 59: Escort the astrologian to Camp Dragonhead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: I might have expected as much from an unbeliever. The Holy See is wise to keep its gates shut to the likes of you.
msgctxt "FateEvent:153:0:58"
msgid "Usually, a knight of House Durendaire would accompany me, but those stationed at the Observatorium had to make for the Nail to intercept a band of crazed giants come down from the mountain to raid our kitchens and steal our women. And therefore, I must ask you to accompany me."
msgstr "Обычно меня сопровождает рыцарь дома Дюрандэр, но тех, кто служит в обсерватории, отправили к Гвоздю перехватить стаю обезумевших гигантов. Они спустились с горы грабить наши кухни и воровать наших женщин. Так что придётся попросить вас меня сопровождать."

#. ja: 護衛してあげますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Eskortierst du den Astrologen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Escorter l'astrologue<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Pardon me, but might you be headed north towards Camp Dragonhead? If you are, I have a proposition.
#. column 57: I am an astrologian employed at the Observatorium. I must hurry these readings to a courier in the camp so that he might deliver them to the archbishop.
#. column 58: Usually, a knight of House Durendaire would accompany me, but those stationed at the Observatorium had to make for the Nail to intercept a band of crazed giants come down from the mountain to raid our kitchens and steal our women. And therefore, I must ask you to accompany me.
#. column 62: I might have expected as much from an unbeliever. The Holy See is wise to keep its gates shut to the likes of you.
