msgctxt "FateEvent:168:0:59"
msgid "Aid the recruit?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь новобранцу?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: そうですか……申し訳ない、無理を言いました。<br>確かに、これだけの敵を相手することは簡単ではない……<br>勝算なき戦を、軽々にできるはずありませんよね。
#. de: Das kannst du doch nicht zulassen!<br>Aber ich gebe zu, es ist kein leichtes Unterfangen.
#. fr: Alors, nous procéderons sans vous. Telle est notre destinée.
#. column 56: A scout has just returned bearing ill tidings. A party of Amalj'aa and their tempered slaves have begun a summoning rite nearby. Do you know what that means, fool? Ifrit! The hells-damned primal could be here breathing fire down our necks any moment!
#. column 57: While I do not doubt my unit would fight bravely if it came to battle with the Lord of the Inferno, I fear we would be overmatched and their deaths would be for naught. However, those Amalj'aa who conduct the rites, they we may be able to handle.
#. column 58: With some help...of course. If we can engage the lizards and the tempered and distract them long enough to destroy the glowing cresset used in the rites, we may be able to thwart their plans and drive them back to Zahar'ak. Will you join us?
#. column 59: Aid the recruit?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:168:0:62"
msgid "Then we shall do the deed without you. Such is our duty, such is our destiny."
msgstr "Тогда справимся и без тебя. Таков наш долг, такова наша судьба."

#. ja: アマルジャ族のテンパードたちが行っている、<br>蛮神イフリートを崇め奉る儀式を止めてください！
#. de: Die fanatischen Ifrit-Anhänger haben mit der Zeremonie begonnen! Du musst sie aufhalten!
#. fr: Nous devons im<shy>mé<shy>dia<shy>te<shy>ment mettre fin aux rites d'invocation<nbsp>!
#. column 57: The only way to do so is to locate the glowing cresset used in the dark ceremony, and the quickest way to locate it is by gutting the Amalj'aa who devise to use the unholy vessel.
#. column 58: But keep your eyes open for the tempered. Despite their outward appearances, they are no longer like us. They have been ripped of their souls and will throw themselves on a blade without hesitation if it means to protect their fiery masters. Deal with them, but only if you must.
msgctxt "FateEvent:169:0:56"
msgid "We must stop the summoning rites at once!"
msgstr "Нужно немедленно остановить обряд призыва!"

#. ja: 儀式を取り仕切っている、<br>アマルジャ族の祭司と警備兵を倒すんです。<br>そうすれば、奴らの祭器が見つかるはず……！
#. de: Beseitige die Priester und Wachen, damit wir nach dem Zentralobjekt der Zeremonie suchen können.
#. fr: Pour cela, une seule solution<nbsp>: forcer les  Amalj'aa qui ont prévu d'utiliser ce récipient impie à nous révéler où se trouve le crasset flamboyant.
#. column 56: We must stop the summoning rites at once!
#. column 58: But keep your eyes open for the tempered. Despite their outward appearances, they are no longer like us. They have been ripped of their souls and will throw themselves on a blade without hesitation if it means to protect their fiery masters. Deal with them, but only if you must.
msgctxt "FateEvent:169:0:57"
msgid "The only way to do so is to locate the glowing cresset used in the dark ceremony, and the quickest way to locate it is by gutting the Amalj'aa who devise to use the unholy vessel."
msgstr "Для этого надо найти светящийся жертвенник, который используют в этом тёмном обряде. Быстрее всего мы его отыщем, если выпотрошим амалджаа, замысливших воспользоваться нечестивым сосудом."

#. ja: 周りのテンパードたちの抵抗もあるでしょうが、<br>全てをこの地より排除してください！<br>くれぐれも、お気をつけて！
#. de: Sie werden sich zur Wehr setzen, so viel ist klar. Und die Kräfte von Besessenen sind nicht zu unter<shy>schätzen!
#. fr: Mais méfiez-vous des subjugués. Même s'ils le cachent bien, ils ne sont plus les mêmes. Ils ont été débarrassés de leur âme et n'hésiteront pas à se jeter sur votre lame pour protéger leurs maîtres. Éliminez-les uniquement s'ils ne vous laissent pas d'autre choix.
#. column 56: We must stop the summoning rites at once!
#. column 57: The only way to do so is to locate the glowing cresset used in the dark ceremony, and the quickest way to locate it is by gutting the Amalj'aa who devise to use the unholy vessel.
msgctxt "FateEvent:169:0:58"
msgid "But keep your eyes open for the tempered. Despite their outward appearances, they are no longer like us. They have been ripped of their souls and will throw themselves on a blade without hesitation if it means to protect their fiery masters. Deal with them, but only if you must."
msgstr "Но смотрите в оба: порабощённые будут сопротивляться. Хоть с виду они и не отличаются от нас, души у них вырваны, и они без колебаний бросятся на клинок, лишь бы защитить своих огненных повелителей. Разбирайтесь с ними, только если придётся."

#. ja: おお、なんてたくましそうな冒険者さんだ。<br>ひとつ、その素敵な腕を貸してくれませんか？
#. de: Ah, ein Prachtexemplar von <if $gn4>einer Abenteurerin<else>einem Abenteurer</if>! Willst du deine herausragenden Fä<shy>hig<shy>kei<shy>ten nicht für einen guten Zweck einsetzen?
#. fr: Ah<nbsp>! Vous, vous avez une tête à avoir de la force dans les bras. Vous pourriez me donner un coup de main<nbsp>?
#. column 57: The cart with today's shipment of sour red was overturned just as she left from Wineport. If it were simply restacking crates, I wouldn't bother asking an outsider for help, but my boy who rode ahead to corral the bolted cart birds spotted a band of buccaneers headed this direction.
#. column 58: I haven't the means to defend meself or the crates, and the Wineport militia is too drunk to be of any help. So I must put the fate of my cargo in your hands.
#. column 59: Protect the wine from the buccaneers?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then I'll be forced to abandon my wine...and my livelihood... Forgive me, son...
msgctxt "FateEvent:170:0:56"
msgid "An adventurer! And just in the nick of time! Can you lend a man a hand?"
msgstr "Вот это приключенец! И как раз вовремя! Не поможешь?"

#. ja: 荷馬車が、積荷のワインを落としているのに気づかず<br>さっさと行ってしまったんです。
#. de: Ein Frachtwagen hat einen Teil seiner Ladung verloren, ohne es zu merken. Edelster Wein, und eine stattliche Menge dazu!
#. fr: J'ai perdu des caisses de mon chargement en cours de route, et je viens seulement de m'en apercevoir.
#. column 56: An adventurer! And just in the nick of time! Can you lend a man a hand?
#. column 58: I haven't the means to defend meself or the crates, and the Wineport militia is too drunk to be of any help. So I must put the fate of my cargo in your hands.
#. column 59: Protect the wine from the buccaneers?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then I'll be forced to abandon my wine...and my livelihood... Forgive me, son...
msgctxt "FateEvent:170:0:57"
msgid "The cart with today's shipment of sour red was overturned just as she left from Wineport. If it were simply restacking crates, I wouldn't bother asking an outsider for help, but my boy who rode ahead to corral the bolted cart birds spotted a band of buccaneers headed this direction."
msgstr "Повозка с сегодняшней партией кислого красного вина опрокинулась сразу после выезда из Вайнпорта. Если бы надо было просто собрать ящики, я бы не стал просить чужака о помощи. Но мой сын, который поскакал догонять сбежавших тягловых птиц, заметил, что сюда направляются пираты."

#. ja: 上等なワインですので、拾い集めて、<br>ワインポートへ運びたいんですが……<br>私の細腕じゃ、とてもとても運べそうにないもので……
#. de: Die Flaschen sind gut verpackt und heil geblieben. Wir haben sie aufgesammelt und bringen sie nach Weinhafen. Aber mit meinen schwachen Händen könnte ich nicht mal eine Kiste aufheben, wenn sie vom Wagen fällt ...
#. fr: C'est du vin de grande qualité, alors je dois absolument récupérer ces caisses pour les livrer à Port-aux-Vins, mais je ne suis pas sûr d'y arriver seul.
#. column 56: An adventurer! And just in the nick of time! Can you lend a man a hand?
#. column 57: The cart with today's shipment of sour red was overturned just as she left from Wineport. If it were simply restacking crates, I wouldn't bother asking an outsider for help, but my boy who rode ahead to corral the bolted cart birds spotted a band of buccaneers headed this direction.
#. column 59: Protect the wine from the buccaneers?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then I'll be forced to abandon my wine...and my livelihood... Forgive me, son...
msgctxt "FateEvent:170:0:58"
msgid "I haven't the means to defend meself or the crates, and the Wineport militia is too drunk to be of any help. So I must put the fate of my cargo in your hands."
msgstr "Мне не защитить ни себя, ни ящики, а ополченцы Вайнпорта слишком пьяны, чтобы помочь. Так что теперь судьба груза в ваших руках."

#. ja: 運んであげますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Hilfst du dem Händler beim Transport?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aidez l'homme à récupérer ses caisses de vin<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: An adventurer! And just in the nick of time! Can you lend a man a hand?
#. column 57: The cart with today's shipment of sour red was overturned just as she left from Wineport. If it were simply restacking crates, I wouldn't bother asking an outsider for help, but my boy who rode ahead to corral the bolted cart birds spotted a band of buccaneers headed this direction.
#. column 58: I haven't the means to defend meself or the crates, and the Wineport militia is too drunk to be of any help. So I must put the fate of my cargo in your hands.
#. column 62: Then I'll be forced to abandon my wine...and my livelihood... Forgive me, son...
