msgctxt "FateEvent:184:0:59"
msgid "Collect poison spores for the Wood Wailer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Собрать ядовитые споры для лесного стража?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 引き受けてくれるか……！。<br>「毒キノコの胞子」はこの周辺で採れる……らしい。<br>くれぐれも頼む、任せたからな？
#. de: Vielen Dank! Du hilfst dem Klageregiment enorm! Die Sporen sind hier in der Gegend in Massen zu finden.
#. fr: Eh bien, quelle surprise<nbsp>! Vous n'avez pas idée à quel point mon discours effraie les aventuriers, en général. Mais assez parlé, les spores n'attendent pas<nbsp>!
#. column 56: A good Wood Wailer knows that the best way to cure a poison is to use the poison itself. It matters little that I do not know how <i>exactly</i> a poison can be its own antidote, only that I know it is. And that is why I'm a good Wood Wailer. Or so I've been told.
#. column 57: A good Wood Wailer <i>also</i> knows that if he can get someone else to collect the poison to create that antidote, there is less chance for him to actually be poisoned in the first place.
#. column 58: Not that I want <i>you</i> to get poisoned. No. I just want you to collect poison spores. You would only get poisoned if you were careless anyway. Or unlucky.
#. column 59: Collect poison spores for the Wood Wailer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Somehow I knew you were going to say that. Was it the pep talk? Should I not have mentioned the poison?
msgctxt "FateEvent:184:0:60"
msgid "Well, that was...unexpected. You wouldn't imagine how many adventurers are turned off by my little pep talk. But enough chitchat, eh? The spores await!"
msgstr "Вот это да... не ожидал! И не представляете, сколько авантюристов отпугивает моя небольшая ободряющая речь. Ладно, хватит болтать. Споры сами себя не соберут!"

#. ja: そうか……残念だが仕方ない。<br>ほかの者をあたるとしよう。
#. de: Schade. Aber es ist ja nicht so, dass wir auf deine Hilfe angewiesen wären.
#. fr: Au fond de moi, je savais que vous alliez refuser. Est-ce à cause de mon petit topo<nbsp>? Peut-être que j'aurais dû éviter de parler de poison...
#. column 56: A good Wood Wailer knows that the best way to cure a poison is to use the poison itself. It matters little that I do not know how <i>exactly</i> a poison can be its own antidote, only that I know it is. And that is why I'm a good Wood Wailer. Or so I've been told.
#. column 57: A good Wood Wailer <i>also</i> knows that if he can get someone else to collect the poison to create that antidote, there is less chance for him to actually be poisoned in the first place.
#. column 58: Not that I want <i>you</i> to get poisoned. No. I just want you to collect poison spores. You would only get poisoned if you were careless anyway. Or unlucky.
#. column 59: Collect poison spores for the Wood Wailer?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Well, that was...unexpected. You wouldn't imagine how many adventurers are turned off by my little pep talk. But enough chitchat, eh? The spores await!
msgctxt "FateEvent:184:0:62"
msgid "Somehow I knew you were going to say that. Was it the pep talk? Should I not have mentioned the poison?"
msgstr "Почему-то я так и знал, что ты откажешься. Это моя речь тебя отпугнула? Не надо было про яд упоминать?"

#. ja: 「毒キノコの胞子」に強心作用が本当にあるのかだと？<br>……そんなこと、一介の現場の者にはわからぬよ。<br>私だって、上から集めて来いと命令されただけなのだ。
#. de: Wie? Ob Giftpilze wirklich heilen können? Frag mich doch nicht so was! Ich bin auf Weisung von oben hier. Die Forschung machen die Leute im Labor.
#. fr: Je peux vous dire que j'en ai fait, des corvées de ramassage de poison, depuis que j'ai rejoint les vigiles sombres. Une fois, alors qu'on nous avait ordonné de collecter des spores, un serpent s'est glissé dans mon pantalon et m'a mordu les... <br>Au fait, vous n'avez pas des spores à ramasser au lieu de discuter<nbsp>?
msgctxt "FateEvent:185:0:56"
msgid "I have taken my share of antidotes since joining the Wailers. There was that time I was sitting in the grass picking daisies when a garter snake slithered right up my bodice and bit me in the─ Wait, shouldn't you be collecting spores?"
msgstr "С тех пор как я вступил в лесные стражи, я столько раз принимал противоядие! Помню, как сидел в траве, собирал ромашки, а тут змея заползла прямо мне за пазуху и укусила в... Погоди, а тебе не пора споры собирать?"

#. ja: 「毒キノコの胞子」を見つけたか？
#. de: Hast du Giftpilz-Sporen gefunden?
#. fr: Vous semblez en bonne santé. Apparemment, le poison ne vous a pas affecté<if $gn4>e</if> de manière durable. Alors, avez-vous récupéré mes spores<nbsp>?
#. column 60: Ah yes. You don't mind if I have you slip those directly in my bag here, do you? I wouldn't want to accidentally get any on me and become─\<gasp>─poisoned. Thank you.
#. column 61: You wouldn't...ah...happen to have any more, would you?
#. column 62: No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?
msgctxt "FateEvent:186:0:56"
msgid "You look well enough. The poison doesn't seem to be doing any lasting damage. So, then. Have you collected any spores?"
msgstr "Выглядите вполне здоровым. Похоже, яд не нанёс непоправимого вреда. Ну что, нашли споры?"

#. ja: うーん、これでいい……のだろうか？<br>いやすまない、恥ずかしながら私は実物を見たことがない。<br>上から聞いた話のかぎりでは、大丈夫だと思うが……。
#. de: Das ... ist doch schon mal eine gute Ausbeute. Glaube ich. Falls es die richtigen Pilze sind. Ich schick sie mal ans Labor. Sammle nur weiter!
#. fr: Parfait. Vous voulez bien les mettre directement dans mon sac<nbsp>? J'aimerais éviter de m'empoisonner, si possible.
#. column 56: You look well enough. The poison doesn't seem to be doing any lasting damage. So, then. Have you collected any spores?
#. column 61: You wouldn't...ah...happen to have any more, would you?
#. column 62: No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?
msgctxt "FateEvent:186:0:60"
msgid "Ah yes. You don't mind if I have you slip those directly in my bag here, do you? I wouldn't want to accidentally get any on me and become─\\<gasp>─poisoned. Thank you."
msgstr "Да, верно. Вы не против, если я попрошу вас положить их прямо в мою сумку? Не хотелось бы случайно задеть их и... <i>Ах!</i> отравиться. Спасибо."

#. ja: いや、きっとこれでいいのだろう、いいに違いない！<br>君、もっと集めてきてくれないか！！
#. de: Ja, die sehen ganz in Ordnung aus. Wahrscheinlich die richtige Sorte. Aber bring mir zur Sicherheit noch mehr!
#. fr: Vous n'en auriez pas d'autre sur vous, par hasard<nbsp>?
#. column 56: You look well enough. The poison doesn't seem to be doing any lasting damage. So, then. Have you collected any spores?
#. column 60: Ah yes. You don't mind if I have you slip those directly in my bag here, do you? I wouldn't want to accidentally get any on me and become─\<gasp>─poisoned. Thank you.
#. column 62: No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?
msgctxt "FateEvent:186:0:61"
msgid "You wouldn't...ah...happen to have any more, would you?"
msgstr "А ещё... э-э... споры у вас случайно не остались?"

#. ja: む……そうか、持ってきたのではないのか。<br>「毒キノコの胞子」は、身体にいいものではないと聞く。<br>見つけたら、早めに私に渡した方が安全ではないか？
#. de: War das alles? Wenn du noch Giftpilz-Sporen mit dir herumträgst, gib sie mir lieber - zu viel davon einzuatmen ist sicher nicht gesund.
#. fr: Pas de spores<nbsp>? Et que vois-je là, dans votre main<nbsp>? J'ai oublié de vous dire que le poison entrait dans la composition de l'antidote, mais que seul, il ne guérissait rien. Vous êtes sûr<if $gn4>e</if> que vous ne voulez pas me les donner, pour votre propre bien<nbsp>?
#. column 56: You look well enough. The poison doesn't seem to be doing any lasting damage. So, then. Have you collected any spores?
#. column 60: Ah yes. You don't mind if I have you slip those directly in my bag here, do you? I wouldn't want to accidentally get any on me and become─\<gasp>─poisoned. Thank you.
#. column 61: You wouldn't...ah...happen to have any more, would you?
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:186:0:62"
msgid "No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?"
msgstr "Нет спор? Тогда что это у вас на руках, позвольте узнать? Уже проникает в кровь! Кажется, я забыл сказать: яд нужен, чтобы <i>изготовить</i> противоядие. Сам по себе он не лечит. Точно не хотите отдать его мне?"

#. ja: きっとこれだけあれば充分だろう！<br>私はそろそろ部隊に戻らなければならないので、<br>まだ「毒キノコの胞子」があったら早めに持ってきてくれ！
#. de: Das müsste doch reichen! Bei all den Pilzen sind sicher welche mit dem richtigen Wirkstoff dabei.<br>Obwohl - noch etwas mehr schadet sicher nicht.
#. fr: Oui, cela devrait suffire pour préparer l'antidote. J'en aurai peut-être une bouteille, cette fois<nbsp>! J'éviterai douze secondes de souffrance la prochaine fois que je tomberai sur un fungus égaré.
msgctxt "FateEvent:187:0:56"
msgid "Yes, this should be more than enough to prepare the antidote. I may get a whole bottle this time! No more twelve seconds of suffering when I step on that next stray funguar."
msgstr "Да, этого должно хватить на противоядие. Может, в этот раз целую бутылку наберу! Больше никаких двенадцати секунд мучений, если наступлю на очередного грибка."

#. ja: おお、「毒キノコの胞子」を<br>持ってきてくれたのか、冒険者よ！
#. de: Aha, frische Giftpilz-Sporen. Jetzt nur nicht zu tief einatmen ...
#. fr: Quel cœur à l'ouvrage<nbsp>! J'imagine que je peux vous débarrasser de quelques spores de plus. C'est le moins que je puisse faire vu le temps que vous avez passé à les récupérer.
#. column 60: Yes. Remember, directly into the bag─and gently. The last thing I need is a cloud of spores corrupting my lungs. Thank you.
#. column 62: No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?
msgctxt "FateEvent:188:0:56"
msgid "Aren't we the eager one? I suppose I could take more spores. It is the least I can do after you spent all the time and effort in gathering them."
msgstr "Вот это усердие! Ну что ж, могу принять ещё спор. Меньшее, что я могу сделать после того, сколько сил и времени вы потратили на сбор."

#. ja: うむ、「毒キノコの胞子」に相違ないな。<br>まだ少し時間がある、持ってきてくれるのならば、<br>受け取るのでよろしく頼むぞ。
#. de: Das sind eindeutig Sporen. Gut. Wenn du noch Zeit hast, kannst du gern noch mehr bringen.
#. fr: Oui. Comme toujours, directement dans le sac. En douceur... Voilà. Je n'ai pas envie que ces spores endommagent mes poumons. Je vous remercie.
#. column 56: Aren't we the eager one? I suppose I could take more spores. It is the least I can do after you spent all the time and effort in gathering them.
#. column 62: No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?
msgctxt "FateEvent:188:0:60"
msgid "Yes. Remember, directly into the bag─and gently. The last thing I need is a cloud of spores corrupting my lungs. Thank you."
msgstr "Да. Только помните: прямо в сумку — и осторожно. Меньше всего мне хочется вдохнуть облако спор. Спасибо."

#. ja: 「毒キノコの胞子」を渡してくれるのではないのか？<br>まぁ……君が持っていたというのなら、止めはしない。<br>だが、取り扱いにだけは、十分気を付けてくれよ。
#. de: Ist nur meine Meinung, aber an deiner Stelle würd ich Giftpilz-Sporen nicht zu lange in der Tasche rumtragen. Gib sie mir lieber, wenn du noch welche hast.
#. fr: Pas de spores<nbsp>? Et que vois-je là, dans votre main<nbsp>? Gardez-les si vous voulez, mais il ne faudra pas venir pleurer quand vous aurez les mains pleines de cloques purulentes. Vous êtes sûr<if $gn4>e</if> que vous ne voulez pas me les donner<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Aren't we the eager one? I suppose I could take more spores. It is the least I can do after you spent all the time and effort in gathering them.
#. column 60: Yes. Remember, directly into the bag─and gently. The last thing I need is a cloud of spores corrupting my lungs. Thank you.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:188:0:62"
msgid "No spores? Then what is that, exactly, on your hands, seeping into your humours as we speak? Perhaps I forgot to mention, poison is used to <i>make</i> the antidote. It is not the antidote itself. Are you certain you do not wish to hand it over?"
msgstr "Нет спор? Тогда что это у вас на руках, позвольте узнать? Уже проникает в кровь! Кажется, я забыл сказать: яд нужен, чтобы <i>изготовить</i> противоядие. Сам по себе он не лечит. Точно не хотите отдать его мне?"

#. ja: ごきげんいかがかな、冒険者さん。<br>レインキャッチャーという植物を知っているかい？<br>この辺りに生えてる、器のような赤い花の植物さ。
#. de: Wie geht's, wie steht's, Abenteurer<if $gn4>in</if>? Darf ich dir von einer famosen Pflanze vorschwärmen, dem Regenfänger? Rote Blüte, bienenbezaubernder Duft!
#. fr: Si je puis me permettre, je ne suis qu'un pauvre habitant de Port-aux-Vins chargé de m'occuper des vignes.
#. column 57: However, truth be told, 'tis not I what does the bulk o' the work, but the wood's goodly bees. Still, I must find all manner of ways to lure the flyin' faeries up to the vines. O'er the seasons, I's found that raincatcher nectar does a right job.
#. column 58: If it weren't for them bloody pink devils, I'd already have the sweet stuff up on the vines, but a man of me age ain't built to weather a beak to the gut. Might I ask <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> to collect the nectar in me stead? Me master will pay handsomely.
#. column 59: Collect raincatcher nectar?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks and a thousand more! I'll wait here for the nectar while you give them colibri what's comin' to 'em!
#. column 62: Me master won't be pleased, and I know not how many more lashin's me back can take...
#. macro: <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:189:0:56"
msgid "If I may, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. I's but a Wineport housebond, tasked with tendin' the vines."
msgstr "Если позволите, госпожа. Я всего лишь работник виноградника в Вайнпорте."

#. ja: こいつ花の蜜が、<br>蜜蜂を寄せつけるのに最適でね！<br>ブドウ畑の受粉のために、利用したいんだ。
#. de: Ihr Nektar ist unheimlich attraktiv für Bienen, was man von Weinblüten nicht gerade behaupten kann. Die fliegenden Helferlein sollen aber die Weinblüten befruchten, und deswegen wollen wir sie ihnen mit Regenfänger-Nektar schmackhaft machen.
#. fr: Cependant, pour être honnête, ce n'est pas moi qui fais le plus gros du travail, mais les  gentilles abeilles des bois. Je dois déborder d'ingéniosité pour attirer ces petites fées volantes dans les vignes. Avec le temps, j'ai découvert que le miel de cueillepluie fonctionnait plutôt bien.
#. column 56: If I may, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. I's but a Wineport housebond, tasked with tendin' the vines.
#. column 58: If it weren't for them bloody pink devils, I'd already have the sweet stuff up on the vines, but a man of me age ain't built to weather a beak to the gut. Might I ask <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> to collect the nectar in me stead? Me master will pay handsomely.
#. column 59: Collect raincatcher nectar?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks and a thousand more! I'll wait here for the nectar while you give them colibri what's comin' to 'em!
#. column 62: Me master won't be pleased, and I know not how many more lashin's me back can take...
msgctxt "FateEvent:189:0:57"
msgid "However, truth be told, 'tis not I what does the bulk o' the work, but the wood's goodly bees. Still, I must find all manner of ways to lure the flyin' faeries up to the vines. O'er the seasons, I's found that raincatcher nectar does a right job."
msgstr "Правду сказать, основную работу делают добрые лесные пчёлки. А мне приходится придумывать, как заманить этих летающих фей на виноградник. За годы я понял, что нектар дожделовов отлично подходит."

#. ja: ただ、コリブリも蜜を狙ってるもんで、<br>蜜集めがはかどらなくて。<br>よかったら蜜集めを手伝ってくれないか？
#. de: Dabei gibt es aber einen Haken. Der Nektar lockt nicht nur Bienen, sondern auch Kolibris an. Mit denen will ich mich nicht anlegen! Kannst du nicht den Nektar für mich sammeln?
#. fr: Sans ces petits démons roses que sont les colibris, j'en aurais déjà appliqué sur les vignes. Mais un homme de mon âge n'est plus assez rapide pour éviter les coups de bec. Puis-je vous demander de récupérer ce miel pour moi<nbsp>? Mon maître vous paiera rubis sur l'ongle.
#. column 56: If I may, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. I's but a Wineport housebond, tasked with tendin' the vines.
#. column 57: However, truth be told, 'tis not I what does the bulk o' the work, but the wood's goodly bees. Still, I must find all manner of ways to lure the flyin' faeries up to the vines. O'er the seasons, I's found that raincatcher nectar does a right job.
#. column 59: Collect raincatcher nectar?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: A thousand thanks and a thousand more! I'll wait here for the nectar while you give them colibri what's comin' to 'em!
#. column 62: Me master won't be pleased, and I know not how many more lashin's me back can take...
#. macro: <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:189:0:58"
msgid "If it weren't for them bloody pink devils, I'd already have the sweet stuff up on the vines, but a man of me age ain't built to weather a beak to the gut. Might I ask <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> to collect the nectar in me stead? Me master will pay handsomely."
msgstr "Будь моя воля, я бы уже развесил сладкий нектар на лозах, да только эти проклятые розовые демоны-калибри клюются. В моём-то возрасте не пережить удара клювом в живот. Не соберёт ли <if $gn4>миледи<else>милорд</if> нектар за меня? Хозяин щедро заплатит."

#. ja: 「レインキャッチャーの蜜」を集めてあげますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Willst du Regenfänger-Nektar für den Winzer sammeln?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Récupérer du miel de cueillepluie<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: If I may, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. I's but a Wineport housebond, tasked with tendin' the vines.
#. column 57: However, truth be told, 'tis not I what does the bulk o' the work, but the wood's goodly bees. Still, I must find all manner of ways to lure the flyin' faeries up to the vines. O'er the seasons, I's found that raincatcher nectar does a right job.
#. column 58: If it weren't for them bloody pink devils, I'd already have the sweet stuff up on the vines, but a man of me age ain't built to weather a beak to the gut. Might I ask <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> to collect the nectar in me stead? Me master will pay handsomely.
#. column 60: A thousand thanks and a thousand more! I'll wait here for the nectar while you give them colibri what's comin' to 'em!
#. column 62: Me master won't be pleased, and I know not how many more lashin's me back can take...
