msgctxt "FateEvent:243:0:59"
msgid "Escort the moogle to Zenith?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Проводить мугла до Зенита?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 残念だけど、仕方ないくぽ。<br>くぽぽ……こわいこわいくぽ……。
#. de: O weh, kupo! Wenn die bösen Drachen mich auffressen, bist du schuld, kupo!
#. fr: Oh, je vois, kuppo... J'ai pourtant tellement peur tout seul, kuppo...
#. column 56: Those good-for-naught pom-clods! They said they'd be here by now, kupo!
#. column 57: If the ancient covenant says <i>all</i> moogles of Moghome must tend to the holy tower, why is it always yours-kupo-truly who finds himself stuck wiping down the walls by his lonesome?
#. column 58: \<sigh> You wouldn't happen to be on your way to Zenith, would you? I've drawn the small nut and now must take one in the pom to see my ungrateful brothers remain in Hraesvelgr's good graces. Problem is, I don't think I can make it there on my own, kupo.
#. column 59: Escort the moogle to Zenith?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:243:0:62"
msgid "Mog it! If Hraesvelgr wants to come down from the lofty heavens and raze Moghome, let him! At least I'll never have to wipe a wall again."
msgstr "Да пропади оно всё! Если Хресвельгр хочет спуститься с небес и разнести Могдом — пусть! Зато больше не придётся вытирать стены."

#. ja: ね、ねぇ……あなたって、<br>ヴィゾーヴニル様のお知り合いだよね？<br>お願い、助けてほしいんだ！
#. de: Du bist <if $gn4>eine Freundin<else>ein Freund</if> von Vidofnir, nicht wahr? Dann musst du mir helfen!
#. fr: Dis-moi, humain<if $gn4>e</if>, tu connais Vidofnir, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>?<nbsp>... Dans ce cas, j'aimerais te demander un service.
#. column 57: Mine uncle, known by your people as Galar of the Second Sun, ever loyal servant of Hraesvelgr, is beset by minions of Nidhogg.
#. column 58: I ask with humble heart that you lend him your strength, for without aid, I do not believe he will survive much longer, and I am too young and weak to alter the tide of battle.
#. column 59: Save Galar?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then you have condemned him to death... Perhaps Vidofnir was mistaken...
#. macro: <if $gn4>Daughter<else>Son</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:244:0:56"
msgid "<if $gn4>Daughter<else>Son</if> of the Land, you are here in our realm at the blessing of Vidofnir, which means there is good within you."
msgstr "<if $gn4>Дочь<else>Сын</if> Земли, ты здесь по благословению Видофнир. Значит, в тебе есть добро."

#. ja: 邪竜の眷属たちに襲われて……<br>僕を逃がすために、おじさんが残って戦ってるんだ。<br>ここまで逃げてきたけど、やっぱりおじさんが心配で……。
#. de: Mein Onkel und ich wurden von Nidhoggs Horde angegriffen. Damit ich fliehen konnte, hat mein Onkel die Drachen in einen Kampf verwickelt. Aber alleine ist er ihnen nicht gewachsen!
#. fr: Mon oncle et moi avons été attaqués par ces sauvages qui sont sous les ordres de Nidhogg. Il est d'ailleurs resté en retrait pour me permettre de m'enfuir. Mais j'ai peur pour lui...
#. column 56: <if $gn4>Daughter<else>Son</if> of the Land, you are here in our realm at the blessing of Vidofnir, which means there is good within you.
#. column 58: I ask with humble heart that you lend him your strength, for without aid, I do not believe he will survive much longer, and I am too young and weak to alter the tide of battle.
#. column 59: Save Galar?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then you have condemned him to death... Perhaps Vidofnir was mistaken...
msgctxt "FateEvent:244:0:57"
msgid "Mine uncle, known by your people as Galar of the Second Sun, ever loyal servant of Hraesvelgr, is beset by minions of Nidhogg."
msgstr "Мой дядя, которого ваш народ знает как Галара Второго Солнца, верный слуга Хресвельгра, окружён приспешниками Нидхёгга."

#. ja: だからお願い！<br>僕のおじさん……「ガラール」を助けて！
#. de: Mein Onkel heißt Galar! Bitte lass ihn nicht im Stich!
#. fr: Accepterais-tu d'aller aider mon oncle<nbsp>? Il s'appelle Galar...
#. column 56: <if $gn4>Daughter<else>Son</if> of the Land, you are here in our realm at the blessing of Vidofnir, which means there is good within you.
#. column 57: Mine uncle, known by your people as Galar of the Second Sun, ever loyal servant of Hraesvelgr, is beset by minions of Nidhogg.
#. column 59: Save Galar?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then you have condemned him to death... Perhaps Vidofnir was mistaken...
msgctxt "FateEvent:244:0:58"
msgid "I ask with humble heart that you lend him your strength, for without aid, I do not believe he will survive much longer, and I am too young and weak to alter the tide of battle."
msgstr "От всего сердца прошу помочь ему. Без поддержки он долго не продержится, а я слишком юн и слаб, чтобы переломить ход битвы."

#. ja: 助けてあげますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Dem Onkel des Drachenjungen helfen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider l'oncle de ce dragonnet<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: <if $gn4>Daughter<else>Son</if> of the Land, you are here in our realm at the blessing of Vidofnir, which means there is good within you.
#. column 57: Mine uncle, known by your people as Galar of the Second Sun, ever loyal servant of Hraesvelgr, is beset by minions of Nidhogg.
#. column 58: I ask with humble heart that you lend him your strength, for without aid, I do not believe he will survive much longer, and I am too young and weak to alter the tide of battle.
#. column 62: Then you have condemned him to death... Perhaps Vidofnir was mistaken...
