msgid "Why, you have outdone yourself, good adventurer! House Haillenarte is in your debt!"
msgstr "Вот это вы постарались, добрый искатель приключений! Дом Хайленарт у вас в долгу!"

#. ja: この資源は、いくらあっても困りません。<br>また収集されましたら、お届けくださいね！
#. de: Wenn Ihr mir noch mehr Scherben bringen wollt, sage ich nicht nein. Je mehr, desto besser!
#. fr: Revenez me voir quand vous aurez accumulé davantage d'éclats. Plus il y en a, mieux c'est<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Every shard will bring House Haillenarte closer to solving the mystery surrounding these remarkable items. Your contribution is much appreciated.
#. column 60: Why, you have outdone yourself, good adventurer! House Haillenarte is in your debt!
msgctxt "FateEvent:330:0:62"
msgid "Still, the High Count's generosity knows no bounds when it comes to rewarding service in his name. Have you more shards, further riches await."
msgstr "Граф щедро награждает тех, кто служит ему. Нашли ещё осколки? За новые находки получите ещё больше."

#. ja: 聞いておくれよ！<br>田植えに備えて「稲の苗」を運んでいたら、<br>泥棒ナマズオが、力尽くで奪おうとしてきたんだ！
#. de: Da ist man nichts Böses ahnend auf dem Weg zur Aussaat und wird auf einmal von Namazuo bedroht. Die Diebe haben es auf unsere Reissetzlinge abgesehen. Ist das zu fassen?
#. fr: Aide-moi, s'il te plaît<nbsp>! J'allais planter mon riz quand des Namazu sont arrivés pour me chaparder mes graines<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Traps, nets, patrols day and night...and still those damnable Namazu are able to slither into our village and rob us of our very livelihoods! I've had enough! This means <i>war</i>! Not only will we retrieve the seedlings they stole, we will make sure they never can again!
#. column 58: To war?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Good! Because you can't have a war without someone able to fight, and us poor, humble villagers are far from able when it comes to slitting throats and taking names. You, on the other hand, <i>you</i> look as if you've sent a good plenty of deserving souls to the afterlife. I'll be waiting here for the seedlings!
#. column 62: So it's like that, is it? You're going to leave us here to starve? I suppose we only have ourselves to blame...but it's a lot easier on the heart blaming an uncharitable stranger!
msgctxt "FateEvent:331:0:56"
msgid "How could this have happened! Tell me! TELL ME!"
msgstr "Да как же так вышло?! Скажи мне! СКАЖИ!"

#. ja: 苗がなけりゃ、来年には餓死者が出かねない！<br>旅人さん、後生だから、泥棒ナマズオを懲らしめて、<br>「稲の苗」を取り返してくれないかい？
#. de: Ohne die Ernte werden wir nächstes Jahr schlimmen Hunger leiden! Ich bitte dich, schlag die Namazuo in die Flucht und rette unsere Setzlinge!
#. fr: Si je ne plante pas ces graines, je mourrai de faim l'année prochaine<nbsp>! Je t'en prie, <if $gn4>voyageuse<else>voyageur</if><nbsp>! Peux-tu récupérer mes graines de riz<nbsp>!?
#. column 56: How could this have happened! Tell me! TELL ME!
#. column 58: To war?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Good! Because you can't have a war without someone able to fight, and us poor, humble villagers are far from able when it comes to slitting throats and taking names. You, on the other hand, <i>you</i> look as if you've sent a good plenty of deserving souls to the afterlife. I'll be waiting here for the seedlings!
#. column 62: So it's like that, is it? You're going to leave us here to starve? I suppose we only have ourselves to blame...but it's a lot easier on the heart blaming an uncharitable stranger!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:331:0:57"
msgid "Traps, nets, patrols day and night...and still those damnable Namazu are able to slither into our village and rob us of our very livelihoods! I've had enough! This means <i>war</i>! Not only will we retrieve the seedlings they stole, we will make sure they never can again!"
msgstr "Ловушки, сети, дозоры день и ночь... а проклятые намазу всё равно пробираются в деревню и грабят нас до нитки! С меня хватит! Это значит <i>война</i>! Мы вернём украденную рассаду и сделаем так, чтобы такого больше не повторилось!"

#. ja: 稲の苗を取り返す？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Der Bäuerin helfen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider la paysanne<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: How could this have happened! Tell me! TELL ME!
#. column 57: Traps, nets, patrols day and night...and still those damnable Namazu are able to slither into our village and rob us of our very livelihoods! I've had enough! This means <i>war</i>! Not only will we retrieve the seedlings they stole, we will make sure they never can again!
#. column 60: Good! Because you can't have a war without someone able to fight, and us poor, humble villagers are far from able when it comes to slitting throats and taking names. You, on the other hand, <i>you</i> look as if you've sent a good plenty of deserving souls to the afterlife. I'll be waiting here for the seedlings!
#. column 62: So it's like that, is it? You're going to leave us here to starve? I suppose we only have ourselves to blame...but it's a lot easier on the heart blaming an uncharitable stranger!
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
