#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:331:0:58"
msgid "To war?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "На войну?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 本当かい！？　そいつは助かるよ！<br>泥棒ナマズオを懲らしめながら、散らばっている、<br>「稲の苗」も集めて、持って来ておくれ！
#. de: Wirklich? Tausend Dank! Erteil diesen Langfingern eine Lektion und bring mir alle Setzlinge, die du findest!
#. fr: Tu veux bien<nbsp>!? Sois béni<if $gn4>e</if><nbsp>! Mets une bonne raclée à ces garnements et rapporte-moi mes graines, s'il te plaît<nbsp>!
#. column 56: How could this have happened! Tell me! TELL ME!
#. column 57: Traps, nets, patrols day and night...and still those damnable Namazu are able to slither into our village and rob us of our very livelihoods! I've had enough! This means <i>war</i>! Not only will we retrieve the seedlings they stole, we will make sure they never can again!
#. column 58: To war?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: So it's like that, is it? You're going to leave us here to starve? I suppose we only have ourselves to blame...but it's a lot easier on the heart blaming an uncharitable stranger!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:331:0:60"
msgid "Good! Because you can't have a war without someone able to fight, and us poor, humble villagers are far from able when it comes to slitting throats and taking names. You, on the other hand, <i>you</i> look as if you've sent a good plenty of deserving souls to the afterlife. I'll be waiting here for the seedlings!"
msgstr "Вот именно! На войне без бойца никуда. А мы, бедные деревенские жители, в перерезании глоток и расправе не мастера. А вот ты... <i>ты</i> похож на того, кто отправил на тот свет немало достойных. Буду ждать рассаду здесь!"

#. ja: ナマズオに苗を奪われた、私が悪いってことだね。<br>そうかい……今年ぶんの米を食い終わったら、<br>身投げでも考えるとするよ……。
#. de: Ich kann dich zu nichts zwingen. Aber denk daran, was auf dem Spiel steht!
#. fr: C'est vrai que c'est ma faute, je n'aurais pas dû les laisser me voler mes graines si facilement... Je mangerai le peu de riz qu'il me reste, et arrivée l'année prochaine... J'irai peut-être me jeter du haut d'une falaise, qui sait<nbsp>?
#. column 56: How could this have happened! Tell me! TELL ME!
#. column 57: Traps, nets, patrols day and night...and still those damnable Namazu are able to slither into our village and rob us of our very livelihoods! I've had enough! This means <i>war</i>! Not only will we retrieve the seedlings they stole, we will make sure they never can again!
#. column 58: To war?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Good! Because you can't have a war without someone able to fight, and us poor, humble villagers are far from able when it comes to slitting throats and taking names. You, on the other hand, <i>you</i> look as if you've sent a good plenty of deserving souls to the afterlife. I'll be waiting here for the seedlings!
msgctxt "FateEvent:331:0:62"
msgid "So it's like that, is it? You're going to leave us here to starve? I suppose we only have ourselves to blame...but it's a lot easier on the heart blaming an uncharitable stranger!"
msgstr "Значит, вот как? Оставишь нас голодать? Наверное, сами виноваты... но куда легче обвинить бессердечного чужака!"

#. ja: シュー……最低限の数は取り戻せた。<br>だが、「奪われた装飾具」は、まだあるはず……。<br>もしも取り戻せたなら、持って来てくれ。
#. de: Danke, das issst ein Anfang. Aber noch habe ich nicht alle Ssschmuckstücke zurück.
#. fr: Vous en avez déjà récupéré pas mal, mais je suis sûre qu'il y en avait d'autres. Si jamais vous les retrouvez, merci de me les apporter<nbsp>! Ssss...
msgctxt "FateEvent:332:0:56"
msgid "You have been mossst generousss with your time, kind stranger. Several of my creations still lie in the handsss of the accursssed Qalyana, but I have already asked overmuch, and could not think of burdening you further...unlesss, that is, you do not mind..."
msgstr "Ты очень помог<if $gn4>ла</if>, добрый незнакомец. Несколько моих украшений всё ещё у проклятых калиана, но я и так слишком многого просил... Не хочу больше тебя обременять... если только ты сам не против..."

#. ja: 冒険者さん、ちょうどいいところに……。<br>矢尻の材料になる「鋭い石片」を集めるのを、<br>手伝ってはもらえませんか？
#. de: Meine Tante meinte, dass ihr Abenteurer anderen helfen würdet. Würdest du <i>mir</i> vielleicht helfen, Steinsplitter für Pfeilspitzen zu sammeln?
#. fr: Vous alors, on peut dire que vous tombez à pic<nbsp>! J'ai besoin de pierres aiguisées pour fabriquer des pointes de flèches, ça vous dé<shy>rrran<shy>ge<shy>rait de m'aider à en ramasser<nbsp>?
#. column 57: Help the M tribe youth?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: You will? I... I... It's just...my aunt... She's never... Oh, thank you, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>! There are sharp stones all about these hills, but the best ones can be found inside the dhara's dust-devils.
#. column 62: I knew it. My aunt is always lying...when she's not giving me lashings.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:333:0:56"
msgid "My aunt tells me that adventurers are supposed to help people. Would you help <i>me</i> collect sharp stones to make arrowheads?"
msgstr "Тётя говорит, что искатели приключений должны помогать людям. Поможешь <i>мне</i> собрать острые камни для наконечников стрел?"

#. ja: メ族の少女を手伝う？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Dem Mädchen der M helfen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider la jeune M<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: My aunt tells me that adventurers are supposed to help people. Would you help <i>me</i> collect sharp stones to make arrowheads?
#. column 60: You will? I... I... It's just...my aunt... She's never... Oh, thank you, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>! There are sharp stones all about these hills, but the best ones can be found inside the dhara's dust-devils.
#. column 62: I knew it. My aunt is always lying...when she's not giving me lashings.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:333:0:57"
msgid "Help the M tribe youth?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь юному представителю племени М?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ありがとうございます！<br>「鋭い石片」は、この辺りに落ちていますし、<br>ハイランド・ダラを倒しても手に入りますよ。
#. de: Wirklich? Oh ... Ich weiß gar nicht ...! Es ist nur ... Meine Tante ... Du weißt ja gar nicht, wie dankbar ich dir bin, <if $gn4>liebe Abenteurerin<else>lieber Abenteurer</if>!
#. fr: Merrrci<nbsp>! On peut en trouver par terre dans les environs, ou en vainquant ces satanés dharas...
#. column 56: My aunt tells me that adventurers are supposed to help people. Would you help <i>me</i> collect sharp stones to make arrowheads?
#. column 57: Help the M tribe youth?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: I knew it. My aunt is always lying...when she's not giving me lashings.
#. macro: <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:333:0:60"
msgid "You will? I... I... It's just...my aunt... She's never... Oh, thank you, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>! There are sharp stones all about these hills, but the best ones can be found inside the dhara's dust-devils."
msgstr "Правда? Я... я... Просто... тётя... Она никогда... Ой, спасибо, добрый <if $gn4>госпожа<else>сударь</if>! Острые камни валяются по всему холму, но лучшие можно найти внутри пыльных вихрей дхара."

#. ja: そうですか……<br>もし気が変わったら声をかけてくださいね
#. de: Ich wusste es. Meine Tante lügt ständig ... wenn sie mir nicht gerade eine Tracht Prügel verpasst.
#. fr: Ah bon<nbsp>? Dommage, on se serait pourrrtant bien <if $gn4>amusées<else>amusés</if><nbsp>!
#. column 56: My aunt tells me that adventurers are supposed to help people. Would you help <i>me</i> collect sharp stones to make arrowheads?
#. column 57: Help the M tribe youth?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: You will? I... I... It's just...my aunt... She's never... Oh, thank you, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>! There are sharp stones all about these hills, but the best ones can be found inside the dhara's dust-devils.
msgctxt "FateEvent:333:0:62"
msgid "I knew it. My aunt is always lying...when she's not giving me lashings."
msgstr "Я так и знала. Тётя всё время врёт... если только не хлещет меня."

#. ja: 「鋭い石片」は集まりましたか？<br>お持ちでしたら受け取りますよ。
#. de: Hast du ein paar Steinsplitter gefunden?
#. fr: Vous avez trrrouvé des pierres aiguisées<nbsp>?
#. column 57: Hand the youth the stones you have collected?
#. column 60: Ow! When I said sharp stones, you truly listened! Many thanks, kind adventurer. You have saved me a lashing!
#. column 62: My aunt will be furious if I return with this few stones... But then, when isn't she furious?
msgctxt "FateEvent:334:0:56"
msgid "Have you had any luck? The hills are thick with dhara this day and I'm afraid they'll find me if I leave this spot."
msgstr "Удалось что-нибудь найти? Сегодня на холмах полно дхара, боюсь, они меня заметят, если я отсюда уйду."

#. ja: 渡しますか？
#. de: Dem Mädchen deinen Fund übergeben?
#. fr: Remettre les objets<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Have you had any luck? The hills are thick with dhara this day and I'm afraid they'll find me if I leave this spot.
#. column 60: Ow! When I said sharp stones, you truly listened! Many thanks, kind adventurer. You have saved me a lashing!
#. column 62: My aunt will be furious if I return with this few stones... But then, when isn't she furious?
msgctxt "FateEvent:334:0:57"
msgid "Hand the youth the stones you have collected?"
msgstr "Отдать собранные камни юной девушке?"

#. ja: ありがとうございます！<br>この辺りの石は、矢尻を作るのに最適なんです。<br>きっといい狩り用の矢が作れますよ！
#. de: Oh, wunderbar! Die sind hervorragend für Pfeilspitzen geeignet. Danke, du hast mir das Schlimmste erspart.
#. fr: Superrr<nbsp>! Taillées, elles feront de belles pointes de flèches.
#. column 56: Have you had any luck? The hills are thick with dhara this day and I'm afraid they'll find me if I leave this spot.
#. column 57: Hand the youth the stones you have collected?
#. column 62: My aunt will be furious if I return with this few stones... But then, when isn't she furious?
msgctxt "FateEvent:334:0:60"
msgid "Ow! When I said sharp stones, you truly listened! Many thanks, kind adventurer. You have saved me a lashing!"
msgstr "Ай! Когда я сказала «острые камни», ты меня поняла буквально! Спасибо, добрый искатель приключений. Ты спас меня от порки!"

#. ja: そうですか……<br>もし気が変わったら声をかけてくださいね
#. de: Meine Tante wird toben, wenn ich nur mit ein paar Steinen zurückkomme. Na ja, aber das tut sie ja sowieso immer ...
#. fr: Mince... Revenez me voir si vous en trrrouvez<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Have you had any luck? The hills are thick with dhara this day and I'm afraid they'll find me if I leave this spot.
#. column 57: Hand the youth the stones you have collected?
#. column 60: Ow! When I said sharp stones, you truly listened! Many thanks, kind adventurer. You have saved me a lashing!
msgctxt "FateEvent:334:0:62"
msgid "My aunt will be furious if I return with this few stones... But then, when isn't she furious?"
msgstr "Тётя взбесится, если я вернусь с таким малым количеством камней... Хотя когда она не злится?"

#. ja: お、驚いたな……。<br>見回りに来たら、物凄い数の卵を見つけたんだ！<br>間違いない、あれは「ベニツノの卵」だよ！
#. de: Junge, Junge, jetzt haben wir den Eiersalat. Die Hornraben haben's sich vor unserer Haustür gemütlich gemacht.
#. fr: J'en reviens pas... J'ai jamais vu autant d'œufs<nbsp>! C'est de l'œuf de bucorve ça, j'en mets ma main à couper<nbsp>!
#. column 57: If there are as many eggs in the other hornbill nests as the one I just checked, come summer the fields will be aflood with the birds, all honking and squarking till the small hours of night. If you'd be as kind to help me fetch an egg or ten, the village would be in your debt.
#. column 58: Collect eggs for the farmhand?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Your kindness has spared us many a sleepless night, stranger. You'll find the eggs strewn about the paddies, as well as on the hornbills themselves. The females are known to warm their eggs 'neath their wings when hunting.
#. column 62: Beg pardon. 'Twas wrong of me to ask, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:335:0:56"
msgid "Too many... Far, <i>far</i> too many..."
msgstr "Слишком много... Намного <i>слишком</i> много..."

#. ja: あの数の卵が孵ったとしたら……<br>どれだけの鳥害があるか、わかったもんじゃない！<br>よかったら、卵を回収してくれないかい？
#. de: Wenn aus jedem dieser Eier ein Vogel schlüpft, wird man den Himmel vor Federn nicht mehr sehen. Könntest du mir vielleicht helfen, die Eier einzusammeln?
#. fr: Si on les laisse éclore, ils vont ravager le coin. Tu veux bien m'aider à les ramasser<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Too many... Far, <i>far</i> too many...
#. column 58: Collect eggs for the farmhand?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Your kindness has spared us many a sleepless night, stranger. You'll find the eggs strewn about the paddies, as well as on the hornbills themselves. The females are known to warm their eggs 'neath their wings when hunting.
#. column 62: Beg pardon. 'Twas wrong of me to ask, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>.
msgctxt "FateEvent:335:0:57"
msgid "If there are as many eggs in the other hornbill nests as the one I just checked, come summer the fields will be aflood with the birds, all honking and squarking till the small hours of night. If you'd be as kind to help me fetch an egg or ten, the village would be in your debt."
msgstr "Если в остальных гнёздах рогоклювов столько же яиц, сколько в том, что я проверил, к лету птицы заполонят поля и будут горланить до глубокой ночи. Не поможете собрать хотя бы десяток яиц? Вся деревня будет у вас в долгу."

#. ja: 卵を回収する？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Als Eiersammler betätigen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider le paysan<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Too many... Far, <i>far</i> too many...
#. column 57: If there are as many eggs in the other hornbill nests as the one I just checked, come summer the fields will be aflood with the birds, all honking and squarking till the small hours of night. If you'd be as kind to help me fetch an egg or ten, the village would be in your debt.
#. column 60: Your kindness has spared us many a sleepless night, stranger. You'll find the eggs strewn about the paddies, as well as on the hornbills themselves. The females are known to warm their eggs 'neath their wings when hunting.
#. column 62: Beg pardon. 'Twas wrong of me to ask, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>.
