msgctxt "FateEvent:335:0:58"
msgid "Collect eggs for the farmhand?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Собрать яйца для батрака?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 快く引き受けてくれて、感謝するよ！<br>「ベニツノの卵」だが、産み落とされたものはもちろん、<br>親のムニ・ベニツノを倒しても、手に入るはずだぞ！
#. de: Besten Dank! Wenn du schon mal dabei bist, kannst du ja gleich auch ein paar der Elterntiere den Schnabel stopfen.
#. fr: T'es prêt<if $gn4>e</if> à me donner un coup de main<nbsp>? Merci, t'es sympa<nbsp>! Tu peux me rapporter les œufs que tu trouveras par terre, mais aussi ceux que feraient tomber les bucorves. Bonne chance<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Too many... Far, <i>far</i> too many...
#. column 57: If there are as many eggs in the other hornbill nests as the one I just checked, come summer the fields will be aflood with the birds, all honking and squarking till the small hours of night. If you'd be as kind to help me fetch an egg or ten, the village would be in your debt.
#. column 58: Collect eggs for the farmhand?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Beg pardon. 'Twas wrong of me to ask, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>.
msgctxt "FateEvent:335:0:60"
msgid "Your kindness has spared us many a sleepless night, stranger. You'll find the eggs strewn about the paddies, as well as on the hornbills themselves. The females are known to warm their eggs 'neath their wings when hunting."
msgstr "Ваша доброта избавила нас от бессонных ночей, незнакомец. Яйца валяются на рисовых полях, а ещё их можно найти у самих птиц. Самки, говорят, греют яйца под крыльями прямо во время охоты."

#. ja: 仕方あるまい……。<br>ここから石でも投げて、卵を割ってみるか……。<br>いや、そんなことをしたら、親鳥に逆襲されそうだな。
#. de: Oh Mann ... Dann bleibt mir wohl nichts anderes übrig, als von hier mit Steinen auf die Eier zu zielen. Wenn das mal gutgeht ...
#. fr: Ah<nbsp>? Bon bah, pas grave... Je vais balancer des cailloux et... Non, si je fais ça, les parents vont m'ouvrir la caboche à coups de bec...
#. column 56: Too many... Far, <i>far</i> too many...
#. column 57: If there are as many eggs in the other hornbill nests as the one I just checked, come summer the fields will be aflood with the birds, all honking and squarking till the small hours of night. If you'd be as kind to help me fetch an egg or ten, the village would be in your debt.
#. column 58: Collect eggs for the farmhand?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Your kindness has spared us many a sleepless night, stranger. You'll find the eggs strewn about the paddies, as well as on the hornbills themselves. The females are known to warm their eggs 'neath their wings when hunting.
#. macro: <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:335:0:62"
msgid "Beg pardon. 'Twas wrong of me to ask, <if $gn4>milady<else>milord</if>. "
msgstr "Простите. Не стоило мне просить об этом, <if $gn4>сударыня<else>сударь</if>. "

#. ja: 「稲の苗」なら泥棒ナマズオが持っているよ。<br>それに、襲われたときに散らばったものもあるから、<br>拾い集めてくれると、助かるってものさ。
#. de: Die Setzlinge stecken in den Taschen dieser gierigen, diebischen Namazuo. Ich glaube, einige sind ihnen in der Eile auch runtergefallen.
#. fr: J'ai vu les Namazu ramasser mes sacs de graines, mais il y en a qui sont encore à terre, tu peux aussi me rapporter ceux-là. Il me faut de quoi survivre un an, je compte sur toi<nbsp>!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:336:0:56"
msgid "The greedy Namazu made off with far more seedlings than they could carry. As such, some may be lying about the route they used to escape. To reclaim all of them, well... You'll need to find the thieves and <i>ask please</i>."
msgstr "Жадные намазу утащили больше рассады, чем могли унести. Наверняка что-то обронили по дороге. Чтобы вернуть всё, придётся отыскать воров и <i>вежливо попросить</i>."

#. ja: 「鋭い石片」を集めてきてください。<br>この辺りに落ちていますし、<br>ハイランド・ダラを倒しても手に入りますよ。
#. de: Die Steinsplitter liegen entweder hier rum oder befinden sich in den Mägen der Hochland-Dharas. Keine Ahnung, warum die die essen.
#. fr: On peut trouver des pierres aiguisées par terre dans les envirrrons, ou en vainquant ces satanés dharas...
msgctxt "FateEvent:337:0:56"
msgid "There are sharp stones all about these hills, but the best ones can be found inside the dhara's dust-devils."
msgstr "Острые камни валяются по всему холму, но лучшие можно найти внутри пыльных вихрей дхара."

#. ja: 「鋭い石片」は、いくらあっても困りません。<br>お持ちでしたら受け取りますよ。
#. de: Mein Stamm braucht immer Pfeile, und für Pfeile braucht man Pfeilspitzen!
#. fr: Amenez-m'en autant que vous pouvez. Plus j'en ai, mieux c'est<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Hand over the additional stones?
#. column 60: Never before have I known such kindness. My only worry is that if I bring her this many stones, my aunt will think it some manner of treachery... I know, I can hide some of these extras away for next time!
#. column 62: They are quite good stones for making arrowheads. I can see why you'd want to keep them for yourself. It's not like it is <i>you</i> who will be getting twenty lashings when you return home empty-handed...
msgctxt "FateEvent:338:0:56"
msgid "The tribe is always in need of arrows, and you cannot make arrows without sharp stones. Might you have found more?"
msgstr "Нашему племени всегда нужны стрелы, а без острых камней стрел не сделать. Не нашли ещё?"

#. ja: 渡しますか？
#. de: Weitere Steinsplitter übergeben?
#. fr: Remettre les objets<nbsp>?
#. column 56: The tribe is always in need of arrows, and you cannot make arrows without sharp stones. Might you have found more?
#. column 60: Never before have I known such kindness. My only worry is that if I bring her this many stones, my aunt will think it some manner of treachery... I know, I can hide some of these extras away for next time!
#. column 62: They are quite good stones for making arrowheads. I can see why you'd want to keep them for yourself. It's not like it is <i>you</i> who will be getting twenty lashings when you return home empty-handed...
msgctxt "FateEvent:338:0:57"
msgid "Hand over the additional stones?"
msgstr "Отдать ещё камни?"

#. ja: こんなにたくさん集めていただけるなんて！<br>ありがとうございました！
#. de: Das ist wirklich zu großzügig von dir. Meine einzige Sorge ist, dass meine Tante mir vorhalten wird, geschummelt zu haben, wenn ich zu viele Steinsplitter mitbringe. Ich hab's ...! Ich behalte einfach einige fürs nächste Mal!
#. fr: Jamais je n'aurais crrru en avoir autant<nbsp>! Merci beaucoup, <if $gn4>aventurière<else>aventurier</if>.
#. column 56: The tribe is always in need of arrows, and you cannot make arrows without sharp stones. Might you have found more?
#. column 57: Hand over the additional stones?
#. column 62: They are quite good stones for making arrowheads. I can see why you'd want to keep them for yourself. It's not like it is <i>you</i> who will be getting twenty lashings when you return home empty-handed...
msgctxt "FateEvent:338:0:60"
msgid "Never before have I known such kindness. My only worry is that if I bring her this many stones, my aunt will think it some manner of treachery... I know, I can hide some of these extras away for next time!"
msgstr "Никто никогда не был так добр ко мне. Только боюсь: если принесу тёте столько камней, она решит, что я схитрила... А, придумала! Припрячу часть до следующего раза!"

#. ja: あれ、冒険者さんも矢尻を作るんですか？<br>この辺りの「鋭い石片」は、品質がいいですものね！
#. de: Die Steine sind ziemlich gut, um daraus Pfeilspitzen zu machen. Ich verstehe schon, dass du sie behalten möchtest. Du bist es ja auch schließlich nicht, auf den zwanzig Peitschenhiebe warten, wenn du mit zu wenig Steinen zurückkommst.
#. fr: Vous préférez les garder pour vous<nbsp>? Il fallait le dirrre dès le début...
#. column 56: The tribe is always in need of arrows, and you cannot make arrows without sharp stones. Might you have found more?
#. column 57: Hand over the additional stones?
#. column 60: Never before have I known such kindness. My only worry is that if I bring her this many stones, my aunt will think it some manner of treachery... I know, I can hide some of these extras away for next time!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:338:0:62"
msgid "They are quite good stones for making arrowheads. I can see why you'd want to keep them for yourself. It's not like it is <i>you</i> who will be getting twenty lashings when you return home empty-handed..."
msgstr "Камни и правда хороши для наконечников. Понимаю, почему ты хочешь оставить их себе. Не <i>тебе</i> же получать двадцать ударов плетью, если вернёшься домой с пустыми руками..."

#. ja: 「鋭い石片」は、いくらあっても困りません。<br>お持ちでしたら受け取りますよ。
#. de: Mein Stamm braucht immer Pfeile, und für Pfeile braucht man Pfeilspitzen!
#. fr: Continuez à m'apporter des pierres aiguisées, mes sœurs seront fièrrres de moi<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:339:0:56"
msgid "The more arrows you find, the fewer lashes my aunt will give me when I return home. You wouldn't want to see me lashed...would you?"
msgstr "Чем больше найдёшь стрел, тем меньше тётя меня высечет, когда я вернусь. Не хочешь же ты смотреть, как меня порют... да?"

#. ja: シュー……ありがとう、感謝するぞ。<br>しかし、これほどの数の装飾具を盗むとは……<br>カリヤナ派のなんと強欲なことか！
#. de: Vielen Dank! Als ich heute Morgen erwachte, hätte ich nicht gedacht, ssso viel von meinem Schmuck wiederzusehen!
#. fr: Je vous remercie pour votre aide. Je n'arrive pas à croire qu'elles en avaient volé autant<nbsp>! Maudites Qalyanas... Ssss...
#. column 60: I could not asssk any more of you...unlesss, that is, you wish to bloody your blade once more in the name of justice...
#. column 62: Those beads were not carved for you and your ilk. They will bring you no fortune. They will bring you no strength.
msgctxt "FateEvent:340:0:56"
msgid "My thanksss, kind stranger. When I woke this morning I feared I would never see any of my creations again, and yet here you have brought me nearly all that were taken."
msgstr "Спасибо тебе, добрый незнакомец. Проснувшись сегодня, я боялась, что больше никогда не увижу своих творений. А ты вернул почти всё украденное. Шшш..."

#. ja: シュー……かなりの数が取り戻せた。<br>だが、「奪われた装飾具」は、まだあるはず……。<br>もしも取り戻せたなら、持って来てくれ。
#. de: Das ist schon eine ganz beträchtliche Menge. Aber noch nicht allesss. Wenn du mehr Schmuck findest, dann bringe ihn zu mir.
#. fr: Vous en avez déjà récupéré pas mal, mais je suis sûre qu'il y en avait d'autres. Si jamais vous les retrouvez, merci de me les apporter<nbsp>! Ssss...
#. column 56: My thanksss, kind stranger. When I woke this morning I feared I would never see any of my creations again, and yet here you have brought me nearly all that were taken.
#. column 62: Those beads were not carved for you and your ilk. They will bring you no fortune. They will bring you no strength.
msgctxt "FateEvent:340:0:60"
msgid "I could not asssk any more of you...unlesss, that is, you wish to bloody your blade once more in the name of justice..."
msgstr "Ты уже вернул немало. Но украшения ещё остались... Если найдёшь — принеси мне. Шшш..."

#. ja: シュー……疑いたくはないが、<br>その品を持ち逃げする気ではあるまいな？
#. de: Dieser Schmuck wurde nicht für deinesssgleichen gefertigt. Er wird dich nicht reich machen. Und auch nicht ssstärker.
#. fr: Ne me dites pas que vous avez l'intention de vous enfuir avec mes colliers<nbsp>? Ssss...
#. column 56: My thanksss, kind stranger. When I woke this morning I feared I would never see any of my creations again, and yet here you have brought me nearly all that were taken.
#. column 60: I could not asssk any more of you...unlesss, that is, you wish to bloody your blade once more in the name of justice...
msgctxt "FateEvent:340:0:62"
msgid "Those beads were not carved for you and your ilk. They will bring you no fortune. They will bring you no strength."
msgstr "Эти бусы не для таких, как ты. Богатства они тебе не принесут. И силы тоже. Шшш..."

#. ja: 君はアラミゴ解放軍の協力者か？<br>ならば、周辺地域の安全確保のために、<br>巡回に同行してほしいのだが……。
#. de: Du stehst auf Seiten der Be<shy>freiungs<shy>armee? Warum hilfst du dann nicht mit, hier nach dem Rechten zu sehen?
#. fr: Vous êtes <if $gn4>une sympathisante<else>un sympathisant</if> de la résistance mhigoise<nbsp>? Dans ce cas, que diriez-vous de m'accompagner pour ma patrouille de routine<nbsp>?
#. column 57: So, are you with us, or against us?
#. column 58: Are you with them, or against them?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then might I suggest you get your privileged arse out of my homeland afore I gut you with an imperial pike and make you a martyr.
msgctxt "FateEvent:341:0:56"
msgid "You here to aid the Resistance? I know it's not as glamorous as trading blows with an imperial centurion, but the hills need patrolling and I'm short a sentry."
msgstr "Пришёл помочь Сопротивлению? Знаю, патрулировать холмы не так увлекательно, как драться с имперским центурионом, но мне нужен часовой."

#. ja: 実は、同行するはずの仲間が遅れていてね。<br>予定どおりに任務を終えるためにも、そろそろ出発したいのだ。<br>どうだ、やってくれるか？
#. de: Ich wurde anscheinend versetzt und langsam muss ich los. Was sagst du?
#. fr: Je devais être accompagné par un de mes camarades, mais je n'ai pas de nouvelles de lui. Je ne peux pas l'attendre indéfiniment, donc ça m'arrangerait que vous veniez avec moi.
#. column 56: You here to aid the Resistance? I know it's not as glamorous as trading blows with an imperial centurion, but the hills need patrolling and I'm short a sentry.
#. column 58: Are you with them, or against them?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Then might I suggest you get your privileged arse out of my homeland afore I gut you with an imperial pike and make you a martyr.
msgctxt "FateEvent:341:0:57"
msgid "So, are you with us, or against us?"
msgstr "Так ты с нами или против нас?"

#. ja: 巡回に同行する？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Auf Patrouille gehen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider le résistant mhigois<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: You here to aid the Resistance? I know it's not as glamorous as trading blows with an imperial centurion, but the hills need patrolling and I'm short a sentry.
#. column 57: So, are you with us, or against us?
#. column 62: Then might I suggest you get your privileged arse out of my homeland afore I gut you with an imperial pike and make you a martyr.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:341:0:58"
msgid "Are you with them, or against them?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Вы с ними или против них?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: そうか……残念だが、仕方ない。<br>もう少しだけ、仲間の到着をここで待ってみよう……。
#. de: Schade ... Dann werde ich wohl oder übel noch auf die Verstärkung warten müssen.
#. fr: C'est vous qui voyez. Pour ma part, je vais patienter encore un peu...
#. column 56: You here to aid the Resistance? I know it's not as glamorous as trading blows with an imperial centurion, but the hills need patrolling and I'm short a sentry.
#. column 57: So, are you with us, or against us?
#. column 58: Are you with them, or against them?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:341:0:62"
msgid "Then might I suggest you get your privileged arse out of my homeland afore I gut you with an imperial pike and make you a martyr."
msgstr "Тогда убирайся с моей родины, пока я не выпотрошил тебя имперской пикой и не сделал мучеником."

#. ja: シュー……<br>「奪われた装飾具」は、カリヤナ派の拠点に、<br>保管されているはず……見張りに注意してくれよ。
#. de: Die Qalyana horten den Ssschmuck sicher in ihrer Sssiedlung. Sie sind feige und werden ihn gut bewachen. Ich wünsche dir Glück.
#. fr: Les Qalyanas ont sûrement emporté les colliers dans leur base. Faites bien attention aux gardes... Ssss...
msgctxt "FateEvent:342:0:56"
msgid "The Qalyana will have hidden my necklaces somewhere in their settlement. The cowards fear reprisal and will have thusss fortified their guard. May the Lady of the Blisss guide you true."
msgstr "Калиана наверняка спрятали ожерелья в своём поселении. Эти трусы боятся мести и выставили охрану. Пусть Госпожа Блаженства укажет тебе путь. Шшш..."

#. ja: シュー……臆病者のカリヤナ派の連中が、<br>卑怯にも、私が造り上げた装飾具を盗んでいった！<br>手間と魔力をかけて、姉妹のために作ったというのに！
#. de: Verflucht ssseien sie! Allesamt! Den Rücken hab ich mir krumm gemacht, um den Schmuck zu fertigen. Und dann ssstehlen diese elenden Qalyana ihn einfach, während ich ssschlafe!
#. fr: Ces fourbes de Qalyanas m'ont volé les précieux colliers que j'avais fabriqués pour mes sœurs<nbsp>! J'ai passé tellement de temps à travailler dessus... Ssss...
#. column 57: Would that I could retrieve them myssself, yet I am but a carver of beads. You, however, have the look of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of great merit. Might you win back the items in my stead?
#. column 58: Aid the Vira beadmaid?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Unworthy am I of your boundlesss charity. May the Lady of the Blisss guide you true through the Qalyana settlement to where the wicked ones keep my things.
#. column 62: This is a matter for the Vira. I cannot fault you for being unwilling or unable to lend your blade. Please, forgive my presumptuousssnesss.
msgctxt "FateEvent:343:0:56"
msgid "Cravens, they are. Each and every lassst one of them! I toil day and night carving humble necklaces for my sisters, only to have them stolen by loathsssome Qalyana as I sleep!"
msgstr "Трусы! Все до единого! День и ночь я вырезаю скромные ожерелья для сестёр, а проклятые калиана крадут их, пока я сплю! Шшш..."

#. ja: だが、私は職人に過ぎず、力で取り戻すことはできない。<br>ヒトの子の友よ、もしも私を哀れに思うなら、<br>カリヤナ派に「奪われた装飾具」を奪還してきてくれぬか？
#. de: Ich bin eine Juwelierin, keine Kriegerin. Wie soll ich ihn je zurückbekommen? Du sssiehst hingegen aus, als könntest du kämpfen! Hilfst du mir?
#. fr: J'irais bien les chercher moi-même, mais je ne suis qu'une orfèvre qui ne sait pas se battre... Ami<if $gn4>e</if> humain<if $gn4>e</if>, pourriez-vous aller les récupérer à ma place<nbsp>? Ssss...
#. column 56: Cravens, they are. Each and every lassst one of them! I toil day and night carving humble necklaces for my sisters, only to have them stolen by loathsssome Qalyana as I sleep!
#. column 58: Aid the Vira beadmaid?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Unworthy am I of your boundlesss charity. May the Lady of the Blisss guide you true through the Qalyana settlement to where the wicked ones keep my things.
#. column 62: This is a matter for the Vira. I cannot fault you for being unwilling or unable to lend your blade. Please, forgive my presumptuousssnesss.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:343:0:57"
msgid "Would that I could retrieve them myssself, yet I am but a carver of beads. You, however, have the look of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of great merit. Might you win back the items in my stead?"
msgstr "Я бы и сама их вернула, да я всего лишь мастерица бус. А ты, похоже, <if $gn4>женщина<else>мужчина</if> недюжинных достоинств. Не вернёшь ли украшения вместо меня?"

#. ja: ウィルラの職人に手を貸す？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Den Schmuck zurückerbeuten?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider l'orfèvre vira<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Cravens, they are. Each and every lassst one of them! I toil day and night carving humble necklaces for my sisters, only to have them stolen by loathsssome Qalyana as I sleep!
#. column 57: Would that I could retrieve them myssself, yet I am but a carver of beads. You, however, have the look of a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of great merit. Might you win back the items in my stead?
#. column 60: Unworthy am I of your boundlesss charity. May the Lady of the Blisss guide you true through the Qalyana settlement to where the wicked ones keep my things.
#. column 62: This is a matter for the Vira. I cannot fault you for being unwilling or unable to lend your blade. Please, forgive my presumptuousssnesss.
