msgctxt "FateEvent:389:0:57"
msgid "Might you fit the description of “brave warrior”?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Сойдёшь за «храброго воина»?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого FATE: <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 本当かい～？<br>「略奪された宝物」は、紅甲羅たちが持っているか、<br>奴らの溜まり場に置いてあるはずだよぉ～。
#. de: Deine Hilfe ist sehr ...... willkommen. Die Rotpanzer haben die Kostbarkeiten bestimmt schon in ihre Lager geschafft. Wir müssen sie zurückholen, bevor sie in ihre Siedlung zurückkehren. Aber ...... Beeilung!
#. fr: C'est vrai, tu veux bien m'aideeeer<nbsp>? C'est chic de ta paaaart<nbsp>! Tu pourras trouver des coffres par terre chez les Rouges, ou bien en vainquant ces affreuuuux<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Our altars, they have once again been defiled at the hands of the Red. Would that a brave warrior accompany me in my righteous quest to retrieve them.
#. column 57: Might you fit the description of “brave warrior”?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Your answer is...unexpected, yet I will not pass judgment.
msgctxt "FateEvent:389:0:60"
msgid "Your answer is not unexpected, but welcome nonetheless. The Red will have taken the relics they stole to their makeshift camps. We must retrieve the items before the Red return to their stronghold."
msgstr "Не удивлён твоим ответом, но всё же рад ему. Красные, должно быть, утащили похищенные реликвии в свои временные лагеря. Надо вернуть их, пока красные не ушли обратно в свою крепость."

#. ja: そうかい……残念だよぉ……。<br>悲しいなぁ～。
#. de: Deine Antwort ist ...... unerwartet. Aber ich werde nicht über dich urteilen.
#. fr: Ooooh... Bon, je crois qu'il y a des moments où il faut savoir abandonneeeer...
#. column 56: Our altars, they have once again been defiled at the hands of the Red. Would that a brave warrior accompany me in my righteous quest to retrieve them.
#. column 57: Might you fit the description of “brave warrior”?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Your answer is not unexpected, but welcome nonetheless. The Red will have taken the relics they stole to their makeshift camps. We must retrieve the items before the Red return to their stronghold.
msgctxt "FateEvent:389:0:62"
msgid "Your answer is...unexpected, yet I will not pass judgment."
msgstr "Твой ответ... неожиданный. Но судить тебя я не стану."

#. ja: 「略奪された宝物」を、取り戻してくれたのかい～？
#. de: Hast du etwas ...... gefunden?
#. fr: As-tu mis la main sur quelques cooooffres<nbsp>?
#. column 60: Yes... The kami who dwells within this treasure is at ease, but his brethren still lament their fates in the hands of the Red. The search must continue.
#. column 62: The search must continue... The relics must not be left to the whims of the Red.
msgctxt "FateEvent:390:0:56"
msgid "How fares your search?"
msgstr "Как продвигаются поиски?"

#. ja: うわぁ、これだよ、これだよぉ～！<br>まだ数があるはずだから、もっと見つけたら、<br>持って来てねぇ～。
#. de: Ah! Der Kami, der in diesem Kleinod wohnt, hat wieder Frieden gefunden. Doch seine Brüder sind immer noch ...... in Aufruhr.
#. fr: Oh, merci beaucouuuup<nbsp>! Je suis sûr qu'il y en a encore, si tu veux me consacrer encore un peu de ton teeeemps...
#. column 56: How fares your search?
#. column 62: The search must continue... The relics must not be left to the whims of the Red.
msgctxt "FateEvent:390:0:60"
msgid "Yes... The kami who dwells within this treasure is at ease, but his brethren still lament their fates in the hands of the Red. The search must continue."
msgstr "Да... Ками, что обитал в этой реликвии, теперь обрёл покой. Но его братья всё ещё скорбят о том, что пережили в руках красных. Надо продолжать поиски."

#. ja: もう少し、集めて来てくれるのかい～？<br>頼んだよぉ～。
#. de: Suche weiter. Dass die Rotpanzer ihre Hände an unsere Kostbarkeiten gelegt haben, ist ...... unerträglich.
#. fr: Merci de m'apporter les coffres que tu trouveraaaas<nbsp>!
#. column 56: How fares your search?
#. column 60: Yes... The kami who dwells within this treasure is at ease, but his brethren still lament their fates in the hands of the Red. The search must continue.
msgctxt "FateEvent:390:0:62"
msgid "The search must continue... The relics must not be left to the whims of the Red."
msgstr "Поиски нужно продолжать... Нельзя оставлять реликвии на милость красных."

#. ja: 「略奪された宝物」は、紅甲羅たちが持っているか、<br>奴らの溜まり場に置いてあるはずだよぉ～。
#. de: Die Rotpanzer haben die Kostbarkeiten bestimmt schon in ihre Lager geschafft. Wir müssen sie zurückholen, bevor sie in ihre Siedlung zurückkehren. Aber ...... Beeilung!
#. fr: Tu pourras trouver des coffres par terre chez les Rouges, ou bien en vainquant ces affreuuuux<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:391:0:56"
msgid "The Reds will have taken the relics they stole to their makeshift camps. We must retrieve the items before the Red return to their stronghold."
msgstr "Красные, должно быть, утащили похищенные реликвии в свои временные лагеря. Надо вернуть их, пока красные не ушли обратно в свою крепость."

#. ja: 「略奪された宝物」を、取り戻してくれたのかい～？
#. de: Hast du noch mehr gefunden?
#. fr: Où en es-tu, avec ces cooooffres<nbsp>?
#. column 60: It has, and so, too, has it smiled upon the Blues. You have done our people a great service. I shall sing of your kindness to all under the dome. Thank you.
#. column 62: Fortune is does not favor the meek. Yet, you have already done much and more for the Blue, and it is understandable if you are weary from the day's efforts.
msgctxt "FateEvent:392:0:56"
msgid "Has fortune smiled upon you further this day?"
msgstr "Удача улыбнулась тебе ещё раз за день?"

#. ja: これだけ取り戻せれば、十分だぁ～。<br>わざわざ手助けしてくれて、ありがとなぁ～！<br>そろそろ碧のタマミズに帰るとするよぉ～！
#. de: Wie ich sehe, ja. Das Schicksal meint es gut mir dir und mit den Blaupanzern. Wir werden von dir ...... singen.
#. fr: Magnifiiiique<nbsp>! Tu as réussi à en retrouver bien plus que je ne l'espéraiiiis<nbsp>! Mille mercis, <if $gn4>humaiiiine<else>humaiiiin</if>.
#. column 56: Has fortune smiled upon you further this day?
#. column 62: Fortune is does not favor the meek. Yet, you have already done much and more for the Blue, and it is understandable if you are weary from the day's efforts.
msgctxt "FateEvent:392:0:60"
msgid "It has, and so, too, has it smiled upon the Blues. You have done our people a great service. I shall sing of your kindness to all under the dome. Thank you."
msgstr "Да, и нашему народу тоже улыбнулась удача. Ты оказал нам огромную услугу. Я воспою твою доброту под куполом. Спасибо."

#. ja: そろそろ碧のタマミズに帰るとするよぉ～！<br>「略奪された宝物」を持っているなら、<br>早めに渡してくれなぁ～。
#. de: Nicht alle Kostbarkeiten haben ihren Weg zu uns zurückgefunden. Ich hoffe, dass die Kami uns verzeihen.
#. fr: Je vais bientôt devoir rentreeeer... Si tu as des coffres, merci de me les confieeeer<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Has fortune smiled upon you further this day?
#. column 60: It has, and so, too, has it smiled upon the Blues. You have done our people a great service. I shall sing of your kindness to all under the dome. Thank you.
msgctxt "FateEvent:392:0:62"
msgid "Fortune is does not favor the meek. Yet, you have already done much and more for the Blue, and it is understandable if you are weary from the day's efforts."
msgstr "Удача не улыбается тихоням. Но ты и так немало сделал для синих. Пойму, если ты устал за сегодняшний день."

#. ja: そろそろ碧のタマミズに帰るとするよぉ～！<br>「略奪された宝物」を持っているなら、<br>早めに渡してくれなぁ～。
#. de: Ich muss bald zurück, um die Altäre wieder zu schmücken. Wenn du noch mehr Kostbarkeiten finden kannst, beeile dich ...... bitte.
#. fr: Je vais bientôt devoir rentreeeer... Si tu as des coffres, merci de me les confieeeer<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:393:0:56"
msgid "I shall soon return to the dome to restore the altars and sing to my kin your praises. If you have aught else to give, I beg you make haste."
msgstr "Скоро я вернусь под купол, восстановлю алтари и расскажу соплеменникам о твоей доброте. Если у тебя есть ещё что отдать, прошу, поторопись."

#. ja: 羊たちに水を飲ませようとしていたら、<br>屈強な男たちに、無理矢理ここにつれてこられて……。<br>どうかボクを助けておくれよ！
#. de: Gerade als ich meine Schafe zur Tränke führen wollte, wurde ich von hinterhältigen Buduga überfallen und hierher verschleppt. Kannst du mir helfen?
#. fr: Ouah, je l'ai échappé belle... Je promenais mes brebis quand des Buduga armés ont voulu me forcer à les suivre. J'ai réussi à m'enfuir, mais ils sont à ma recherche... S'ils reviennent, tu veux bien t'occuper d'eux<nbsp>?
#. column 57: Rescue the Mol shepherd from the Buduga?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: They're back! May the light of the Dawn Father protect you! May the light of the Dusk Mother, as well! You'll need it!
#. column 62: You can't leave me! I'll make a terrible Buduga!
msgctxt "FateEvent:394:0:56"
msgid "One moment I was leading my herd to water, and the next, I'm on the back of a Budugan horse, my hands and feet bound. I am not a fighter. When my captors return and realize how worthless I am to them, I'll be fed to their pigs...or worse! You must help me!"
msgstr "Я вёл стадо на водопой — и вдруг оказался связанным по рукам и ногам на спине лошади будуга. Я не боец. Когда похитители вернутся и поймут, что я им ни на что не гожусь, они скормят меня свиньям... или сделают что похуже! Прошу, помоги мне!"

#. ja: モル族の羊飼いを助ける？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Willst du den Mol-Schäfer befreien?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider le berger mol<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: One moment I was leading my herd to water, and the next, I'm on the back of a Budugan horse, my hands and feet bound. I am not a fighter. When my captors return and realize how worthless I am to them, I'll be fed to their pigs...or worse! You must help me!
#. column 60: They're back! May the light of the Dawn Father protect you! May the light of the Dusk Mother, as well! You'll need it!
#. column 62: You can't leave me! I'll make a terrible Buduga!
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:394:0:57"
msgid "Rescue the Mol shepherd from the Buduga?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Спасти молского пастуха от будуга?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※ Рекомендуемый уровень для этого FATE: <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: う、うわっ……奴らが戻ってきた！<br>奴らに誘拐されたら、ボクもブドゥガ族にされちゃうよ！<br>た、助けてっ！
#. de: Da sind sie! Sie wollen mich in ihr Lager bringen, um aus mir einen Buguda zu machen. Bitte, hilf mir!
#. fr: ... Oh non, les revoilà<nbsp>! Ne les laisse pas m'enlever, je ne veux pas devenir un Buduga<nbsp>!
#. column 56: One moment I was leading my herd to water, and the next, I'm on the back of a Budugan horse, my hands and feet bound. I am not a fighter. When my captors return and realize how worthless I am to them, I'll be fed to their pigs...or worse! You must help me!
#. column 57: Rescue the Mol shepherd from the Buduga?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: You can't leave me! I'll make a terrible Buduga!
msgctxt "FateEvent:394:0:60"
msgid "They're back! May the light of the Dawn Father protect you! May the light of the Dusk Mother, as well! You'll need it!"
msgstr "Они вернулись! Пусть свет Отца Рассвета хранит тебя! И свет Матери Сумерек тоже! Он тебе понадобится!"

#. ja: そ、そんなぁ……。<br>このまま奴らに誘拐されたら、<br>ボクもブドゥガ族にされちゃうんだよ！？
#. de: Du willst mich den Buguda überlassen? Sie werden mich in ihr Lager verschleppen, um mich zu einem der ihren zu machen.
#. fr: Tu sais qu'ils obligent tous leurs prisonniers à rejoindre leur tribu<nbsp>? Et malgré ça, tu les laisserais m'enlever<nbsp>?
#. column 56: One moment I was leading my herd to water, and the next, I'm on the back of a Budugan horse, my hands and feet bound. I am not a fighter. When my captors return and realize how worthless I am to them, I'll be fed to their pigs...or worse! You must help me!
#. column 57: Rescue the Mol shepherd from the Buduga?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: They're back! May the light of the Dawn Father protect you! May the light of the Dusk Mother, as well! You'll need it!
msgctxt "FateEvent:394:0:62"
msgid "You can't leave me! I'll make a terrible Buduga!"
msgstr "Нельзя же бросать меня! Из меня выйдет никудышный будуга!"

#. ja: 元アラミゴ王家付き書記官、アンセロットがここに記す。<br>宗教行事を禁じた帝国軍の目を盗み、<br>どうにかここにやって来た。
#. de: In den Annalen der Sultane habe ich über diese Begräbnisstätte gelesen und ich wollte sie mit eigenen Augen sehen. Ich musste aufpassen, dass mich niemand entdeckt, denn die Garlear verbieten uns die Ausübung unserer Religion.
#. fr: C'est un message laissé par Anselot, l'ancien scribe de la famille royale mhigoise<nbsp>: “Depuis que l'Empire condamne toute activité ayant trait à la religion, je suis obligé de vivre caché dans ce mausolée...”
#. column 57: “Yet my recent visits to the crypts have left me at a loss for words. With none to tend to them, the once somber halls have fallen into state of utter disrepair. Tombs lie plundered, the bones of kings strewn about and gnawed upon by all manner of foul creatures.”
msgctxt "FateEvent:395:0:56"
msgid "“The Garleans may rule over the royal city, but they will never rule over me. I will continue my duty as royal historian to catalog the deeds of Ala Mhigo's kings, both great and terrible.”"
msgstr "«Гарлеанцы могут править королевским городом, но мной им не править. Я и дальше буду исполнять свой долг королевского историографа и записывать деяния королей Ала Миго — славные и позорные»."

#. ja: 歴代の王家の人々を埋葬した、荘厳なる霊廟……<br>「列王の詩」の様子を確認に来たのだが、こうも荒れているとは！
#. de: Hier ruhen die glorreichen Herrscher von Ala Mhigo, doch zu meinem Schrecken musste ich feststellen, dass ihre Ruhe gestört wird und sich die Grabstätte in einem fürchterlichen Zustand befindet.
#. fr: Le Chant des Rois... Ici reposent les âmes des plus grands monarques d'Ala Mhigo. Quelle tristesse de constater qu'un lieu aussi solennel est aujourd'hui dans un tel état de décrépitude...“
#. column 56: “The Garleans may rule over the royal city, but they will never rule over me. I will continue my duty as royal historian to catalog the deeds of Ala Mhigo's kings, both great and terrible.”
msgctxt "FateEvent:395:0:57"
msgid "“Yet my recent visits to the crypts have left me at a loss for words. With none to tend to them, the once somber halls have fallen into state of utter disrepair. Tombs lie plundered, the bones of kings strewn about and gnawed upon by all manner of foul creatures.”"
msgstr "«Но после недавних визитов в склеп у меня не осталось слов. Некому ухаживать за усыпальницей, и некогда торжественные залы пришли в полное запустение. Гробницы разграблены, кости королей разбросаны и обглоданы всякой мерзостью»."

#. ja: 鎮魂の儀式が途絶えたためか、死霊の姿が散見される。<br>供養に来ないアラミゴの民を恨んでいるのか、<br>いずれも荒れ狂っているようだ。
#. de: Die traditionellen Riten zu Ehren der Toten wurden hier schon lange nicht mehr durchgeführt. Kein Wunder, dass ihre Geister erwachen, getrieben von dem Hass auf die Lebenden.
#. fr: “J'aperçois çà et là des esprits errants, sans doute les âmes de défunts dont la cérémonie funéraire n'a pu être achevée à cause de l'in<shy>ter<shy>dic<shy>tion garlemaldaise. Ils sont prisonniers de ce monde, mus par la rancœur d'avoir été abandonnés par les leurs...
#. column 57: “I endeavored to strengthen the bonds, but my efforts were in vain. The specters have become aware of my presence and now search for me, howling through the chambers. I shall hide behind these monuments until their interest wanes.”
msgctxt "FateEvent:396:0:56"
msgid "“The magicks that once saw the spirits here becalmed are all but faded. Malevolent wraiths walk the grounds unaware that they no longer belong in this realm.”"
msgstr "«Магия, некогда успокаивавшая духов, почти угасла. Злобные призраки бродят по этим местам, не ведая, что им больше нет места в этом мире»."

#. ja: どうにか荒ぶる魂を鎮めようと試みたが、失敗に終わった。<br>悔しいが、ここは身を隠して、やり過ごすしかなさそうだ。
#. de: Ich habe versucht, sie zu besänftigen, aber leider vergebens. Jetzt bleibt mir keine andere Wahl, als mich zu verstecken, bis der Spuk vorbei ist.
#. fr: J'ai bien essayé d'apaiser leurs tourments, en vain... Me voilà contraint de les fuir, de peur que mon âme n'aille grossir leurs rangs...“
#. column 56: “The magicks that once saw the spirits here becalmed are all but faded. Malevolent wraiths walk the grounds unaware that they no longer belong in this realm.”
msgctxt "FateEvent:396:0:57"
msgid "“I endeavored to strengthen the bonds, but my efforts were in vain. The specters have become aware of my presence and now search for me, howling through the chambers. I shall hide behind these monuments until their interest wanes.”"
msgstr "«Я пытался укрепить узы, но безуспешно. Призраки почуяли меня и теперь ищут, воют в залах. Придётся укрыться за этими памятниками, пока они не потеряют ко мне интерес»."

#. ja: 隠れ潜んでいたものの、発見され、襲われ、深手を負った。<br>だが、私のことなど、どうでもいい！
#. de: Die Schatten haben mich entdeckt und verwundet. Ich stehe Todesängste aus, aber ich werde es überleben.
#. fr: “Ma chance a fini par tourner... Je suis grièvement blessé. Si c'est mon destin de périr en ces lieux, qu'il en soit ainsi. Mais avant que je ne rende mon dernier soupir, il faut que je rapporte par écrit l'horreur dont j'ai été témoin...
#. column 57: “I managed to escape a second time, but not without suffering a deep wound to my temple─a wound from which thick blood still oozes, calling to me even more of the wraiths. It will not be long now before they are upon me once again, and this time I fear I will succumb.”
#. column 58: “Yet if I must die, let not my death be for naught. With these, my final words, let me forewarn any who might read them. The corpse of King Manfred the Mad has risen! Ware thee this evil spirit lest you find yourself trapped in a fate worse than mine.”<br>   - Royal Historian, Ancelot the Seventh
msgctxt "FateEvent:397:0:56"
msgid "“I should have known it would be impossible to hide from the undead. They can smell our very lifeblood!”"
msgstr "«Надо было догадаться, что от мертвецов не спрятаться. Они чуют саму нашу кровь!»"

#. ja: 問題は、あの死霊がまとっていた衣だ。<br>あれは「マンフレッド王」のものではなかったか！？<br>
#. de: Viel wichtiger ist, dass diesem Spuk ein Ende bereitet wird. In dem Körper von König Manfred steckt ein böser Geist!
#. fr: Je l'ai vu de mes propres yeux. Il était là, au milieu des spectres qui m'ont attaqué... un esprit maléfique ressemblant trait pour trait à notre illustre roi Manfred.
#. column 56: “I should have known it would be impossible to hide from the undead. They can smell our very lifeblood!”
#. column 58: “Yet if I must die, let not my death be for naught. With these, my final words, let me forewarn any who might read them. The corpse of King Manfred the Mad has risen! Ware thee this evil spirit lest you find yourself trapped in a fate worse than mine.”<br>   - Royal Historian, Ancelot the Seventh
msgctxt "FateEvent:397:0:57"
msgid "“I managed to escape a second time, but not without suffering a deep wound to my temple─a wound from which thick blood still oozes, calling to me even more of the wraiths. It will not be long now before they are upon me once again, and this time I fear I will succumb.”"
msgstr "«Мне удалось сбежать во второй раз, но я получил глубокую рану на виске — из неё всё ещё сочится густая кровь и приманивает новых призраков. Скоро они снова настигнут меня, и на этот раз я боюсь не спастись»."

#. ja: 誰か、強健王の魂を浄化してくれ、それだけが私の願いだ……。
#. de: Bitte, erlöse seine geschundene Seele, damit der König seine wohlverdiente Ruhe findet!
#. fr: Si quelqu'un lit ce message... Qui que vous soyez, terrassez cette abomination et accordez à notre ancien monarque le repos éternel...“
#. column 56: “I should have known it would be impossible to hide from the undead. They can smell our very lifeblood!”
#. column 57: “I managed to escape a second time, but not without suffering a deep wound to my temple─a wound from which thick blood still oozes, calling to me even more of the wraiths. It will not be long now before they are upon me once again, and this time I fear I will succumb.”
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:397:0:58"
msgid "“Yet if I must die, let not my death be for naught. With these, my final words, let me forewarn any who might read them. The corpse of King Manfred the Mad has risen! Ware thee this evil spirit lest you find yourself trapped in a fate worse than mine.”<br>   - Royal Historian, Ancelot the Seventh"
msgstr "«Но если уж мне суждено умереть, пусть смерть моя будет не напрасной. Последними словами предупреждаю каждого, кто прочтёт эту запись. Восстал труп короля Манфреда Безумного! Берегитесь этого злого духа, иначе вас ждёт участь хуже моей».<br>   — Королевский историограф, Анселот Седьмой"

#. ja: ハァ、ハァ、ハァ……そ、そこな旅のお方……<br>恐ろしい悪漢どもに、追われているのです……。<br>どうか、お助けいただけませんか？
#. de: \<keuch> ... \<fiep> ... <if $gn4>Werte Abenteurerin<else>Werter Abenteurer</if>, hab Erbarmen! Ich werde von grässlichen Männern verfolgt! Du musst mir helfen!
#. fr: Haa... Haa... (souffle)... Je suis poursuivie par des affreux... Je vous en prie, <if $gn4>Madame l'aventurière<else>Monsieur l'aventurier</if>, aidez-moi...
#. column 57: Aid the well-spoken maiden?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: My thanks, fellow traveler!
#. column 62: Your answer to my plea is...unexpected. The nature of your kind has changed much since I last walked these lands.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "FateEvent:398:0:56"
msgid "\\<pant> \\<pant><br>Several men of ill intent harry mine every step. I would be in your debt if you were to scatter them to the four winds."
msgstr "<i>Тяжело дышит...</i><br>Меня повсюду преследуют люди с дурными намерениями. Буду вам признательна, если разгоните их во все стороны."

#. ja: 少女を助けますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Dem Mädchen beistehen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider la fillette<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: \<pant> \<pant><br>Several men of ill intent harry mine every step. I would be in your debt if you were to scatter them to the four winds.
#. column 60: My thanks, fellow traveler!
#. column 62: Your answer to my plea is...unexpected. The nature of your kind has changed much since I last walked these lands.
