#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:518:0:58"
msgid "Volunteer to collect nectar in the pixie's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Вызваться собрать нектар вместо пикси?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: そっかぁ……<br>でも、花蜜は諦めたくないし……。
#. de: Wirklich? Du bist aber ein Faulpelz! Pah!
#. fr: Elles te font peur aussi...<nbsp>? Comment je vais faire...<nbsp>? Je le voulais ce nectar, moi...
#. column 56: First anemones, and now I have to deal with bees! This is why I detest nectar duty!
#. column 57: I very much do not want to go over there. But I need the nectar. But...bees...
#. column 58: Volunteer to collect nectar in the pixie's stead?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:518:0:62"
msgid "Please... Not the bees..."
msgstr "Пожалуйста... Только не пчёлы..."

#. ja: 「黄金色の花蜜」を集めてきてくれたのね！<br>私に渡してくれるかしら？
#. de: Du hast es geschafft! Du hast unseren leckeren Nektar gesammelt! Juhu! Reich ihn mir nur fein, wir wollen Freunde sein!
#. fr: T'as trouvé du nectar<nbsp>!? Tu vas me le donner, hein<nbsp>!? Hein<nbsp>!? Hein<nbsp>!?
#. column 60: Yes, this is it! Thank you for braving the bees for me! Let me know if you manage to collect any more.
#. column 62: What brings you out here, anyway? You don't... Mortals don't <i>like</i> bees, do they?
msgctxt "FateEvent:519:0:56"
msgid "You got the nectar? Golden, right? Let me see..."
msgstr "Ты принёс нектар? Золотистый? Дай-ка взглянуть..."

#. ja: ありがとう！<br>まだまだ「黄金色の花蜜」を集めているから、<br>手に入れられたら、持ってきてね！
#. de: Vielen Dank! Ich sammel ihn fleißig jeden Tag. Bring mir ruhig mehr von dem güldenen Nektar, den ich so mag!
#. fr: Youpi<nbsp>! J'en veux plein<nbsp>! Alors ramène-m'en encore plus si tu peux, d'accord<nbsp>!?
#. column 56: You got the nectar? Golden, right? Let me see...
#. column 62: What brings you out here, anyway? You don't... Mortals don't <i>like</i> bees, do they?
msgctxt "FateEvent:519:0:60"
msgid "Yes, this is it! Thank you for braving the bees for me! Let me know if you manage to collect any more."
msgstr "Да, то что надо! Спасибо, что не побоялся пчёл! Если соберёшь ещё, дай знать."

#. ja: 貴方も「黄金色の花蜜」がほしかったの？
#. de: Suchst du auch nach dem güldenen Nektar?
#. fr: Non<nbsp>? Ça aime le nectar aussi, les humains<nbsp>?
#. column 56: You got the nectar? Golden, right? Let me see...
#. column 60: Yes, this is it! Thank you for braving the bees for me! Let me know if you manage to collect any more.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:519:0:62"
msgid "What brings you out here, anyway? You don't... Mortals don't <i>like</i> bees, do they?"
msgstr "А ты-то зачем сюда пришёл? Ты ведь... смертные же <i>не любят</i> пчёл, верно?"

#. ja: 蜂たちは、花蜜集めのライバルなの。<br>困ったものだわ……！
#. de: Die Bienen lieben den Blütennektar genauso wie wir, aber das hier ist nun mal unser Revier!
#. fr: Faut toujours que les abeilles viennent chiper du nectar<nbsp>! Et nous, alors<nbsp>!?
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:520:0:56"
msgid "I <i>hate</i> bees."
msgstr "Я <i>ненавижу</i> пчёл."

#. ja: 結構、「黄金色の花蜜」が集まってきたわ。<br>そろそろ戻ろうかしら……。<br>もし花蜜を持っているなら、受け取るわよ？
#. de: Ich habe schon fleißig Nektar gesammelt. Falls du noch mehr vom süßen Saft hast, den ich begehre, reich ihn mir, bevor ich in unser Dorf zurückkehre!
#. fr: J'ai récolté assez de nectar, alors je vais pas tarder à rentrer. Mais si t'en as encore, je prends<nbsp>!
#. column 60: I have more than enough nectar, now. Thank you, mortal! I'll remember to tell everyone not to turn you into a shrub.
#. column 62: What brings you out here, anyway? You don't... Mortals don't <i>like</i> bees, do they?
msgctxt "FateEvent:521:0:56"
msgid "This should be just enough. I suppose I can stay just a bit longer, if you were planning to bring more? But I would like to go soon. You know─away. From the bees. "
msgstr "Нектара у меня уже достаточно. Спасибо, смертный! Скажу всем, чтобы не превращали тебя в куст."

#. ja: ありがとう！<br>たくさん集められて、とっても嬉しいわ！
#. de: Oh, vielen Dank! Das ist reichlich vom goldenen Saft. Der verschafft uns Pixies gute Laune und mächtig viel Kraft!
#. fr: Super<nbsp>! Encore plus de nectar<nbsp>!
#. column 56: This should be just enough. I suppose I can stay just a bit longer, if you were planning to bring more? But I would like to go soon. You know─away. From the bees.
#. column 62: What brings you out here, anyway? You don't... Mortals don't <i>like</i> bees, do they?
msgctxt "FateEvent:521:0:60"
msgid "I have more than enough nectar, now. Thank you, mortal! I'll remember to tell everyone not to turn you into a shrub."
msgstr "Вот и славно! Ещё больше нектара!"

#. ja: 貴方も「黄金色の花蜜」がほしかったの？
#. de: Suchst du auch nach dem güldenen Nektar?
#. fr: Ah<nbsp>? Tu veux en garder un peu pour toi, c'est ça<nbsp>?
#. column 56: This should be just enough. I suppose I can stay just a bit longer, if you were planning to bring more? But I would like to go soon. You know─away. From the bees.
#. column 60: I have more than enough nectar, now. Thank you, mortal! I'll remember to tell everyone not to turn you into a shrub.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:521:0:62"
msgid "What brings you out here, anyway? You don't... Mortals don't <i>like</i> bees, do they?"
msgstr "А ты-то зачем сюда пришёл? Ты ведь... смертные же <i>не любят</i> пчёл, верно?"

#. ja: 蜂たちは、花蜜集めのライバルなの。<br>困ったものだわ……！
#. de: Die Bienen lieben den Blütennektar genauso wie wir, aber das hier ist nun mal unser Revier!
#. fr: Faut toujours que les abeilles viennent chiper du nectar<nbsp>! Et nous, alors<nbsp>!?
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:522:0:56"
msgid "I hate bees <i>so much</i>."
msgstr "Я <i>терпеть не могу</i> пчёл."

#. ja: ボク、モルドのスカベンジャー！<br>この辺りで、価値ある品、見つかった噂聞いて、<br>漁りに来たんだけど、魔物に襲われてしまったヨ！
#. de: Mein Partner Darmal und ich seien, ähm ... Archäologen! Ja, genau! Bitte, <if $gn4>Reisende<else>Reisender</if>, helfen uns diese Bestien zu besiegen, damit wir nachgehen können unserer ... ähm ... Ausgrabung! \<schwitz>
#. fr: Je suis un chasseur de trésors, oui, j'en suis un<nbsp>! Je suis venu ici parce que j'ai entendu dire qu'on trouve des objets de valeur dans le coin... Mais j'ai été attaqué par des méchantes créatures, des très méchantes<nbsp>!
#. column 57: We came here to see what has been dug up by the scissorjaws. How were we to know they would attack us?
msgctxt "FateEvent:523:0:56"
msgid "My partner Darmal and I are scavengers! Will you help us slay these beasts so that we can carry on searching for treasure?"
msgstr "Мы с моим напарником Дармалом — сборщики всякого добра! Поможешь нам расправиться с этими зверюгами, чтобы мы могли продолжить поиски сокровищ?"

#. ja: シザージョウ、身を隠すために穴掘るネ……！<br>だから、時々、埋もれたお宝、地表に出るのヨ！<br>お宝探し、ウキウキするネ～！
#. de: Wir untersuchen wollten, was diese Scherenmäuler ausgegraben. Wer ahnen konnte, dass die so angriffslustig!
#. fr: Les mandicisailles creusent des trous pour se cacher<nbsp>! C'est pour ça que les trésors enfouis remontent parfois à la surface, oui<nbsp>! J'ai hâte d'en trouver, j'ai vraiment hâte<nbsp>!
#. column 56: My partner Darmal and I are scavengers! Will you help us slay these beasts so that we can carry on searching for treasure?
msgctxt "FateEvent:523:0:57"
msgid "We came here to see what has been dug up by the scissorjaws. How were we to know they would attack us?"
msgstr "Скожелюсти роют норы, чтобы прятаться... Вот из-за них порой и оказываются на поверхности зарытые сокровища! Так здорово искать сокровища!"

#. ja: 旅人よ、力を貸してくれんか？<br>俺の雇い主が、地図らしき羊皮紙を発見してな……<br>宝探しに夢中なんだ。
#. de: Ah, du schon wieder! Du kommst gerade recht! Wir haben diese Scha... ahm ... alte Karte gefunden, auf der ein mysteriöses Kreuz eingezeichnet wurde. Wir sind auf dem Weg zum marktierten Ort, aber diese Eidechsen versperren uns den Weg!
#. fr: Voyageu<if $gn4>se<else>r</if>, j'ai besoin de ton aide... Mon employeur a découvert un parchemin qui a tout l'air d'être une carte, et depuis, il est com<shy>plè<shy>te<shy>ment obsédé par la chasse du trésor dont elle semble indiquer le lieu.
#. column 57: Once they're taken care of, we can continue the search. So, are you in?
#. column 58: Help Darmal slay the lizards?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: We're not expecting you to do it out of the kindness of your heart. You'll be rewarded, you know.
msgctxt "FateEvent:524:0:56"
msgid "Could you lend us a hand? We're trying to find the treasure marked on our map, but these damned lizards are in our way!"
msgstr "Не поможешь нам? Мы ищем сокровища, отмеченные на карте, но эти проклятые ящерицы не дают пройти!"

#. ja: で、地図が示す場所まで来たんだが、<br>ご覧のとおり、リザードの群れがいて立ち往生だ。<br>退治を手伝ってくれると、嬉しいんだがどうだろう？
#. de: Sobald wir die Viecher aus dem Weg geräumt haben, können wir unsere Suche fortsetzen, hilfst du uns?
#. fr: Mais comme tu peux le voir, il s'agit de l'endroit où vit une horde de lézards. J'aimerais que tu les chasses d'ici. Tu veux bien<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Could you lend us a hand? We're trying to find the treasure marked on our map, but these damned lizards are in our way!
#. column 58: Help Darmal slay the lizards?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: We're not expecting you to do it out of the kindness of your heart. You'll be rewarded, you know.
msgctxt "FateEvent:524:0:57"
msgid "Once they're taken care of, we can continue the search. So, are you in?"
msgstr "Разберёмся с ними — и продолжим поиски. Ну что, поможешь?"

#. ja: ダーマルに協力しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Darmal helfen, die Eidechsen zu besiegen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider Darmal<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Could you lend us a hand? We're trying to find the treasure marked on our map, but these damned lizards are in our way!
#. column 57: Once they're taken care of, we can continue the search. So, are you in?
#. column 62: We're not expecting you to do it out of the kindness of your heart. You'll be rewarded, you know.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:524:0:58"
msgid "Help Darmal slay the lizards?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь Дармалу расправиться с ящерицами?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ま、そうだよな……。<br>さて、雇い主にどう説明したもんか……。
#. de: Natürlich kannst du auch einen Anteil vom ... Ruhm ... abhaben. Überleg es dir noch mal!
#. fr: Je vois... Bon<nbsp>! Comment je vais pouvoir expliquer ça à mon employeur<nbsp>?...
#. column 56: Could you lend us a hand? We're trying to find the treasure marked on our map, but these damned lizards are in our way!
#. column 57: Once they're taken care of, we can continue the search. So, are you in?
#. column 58: Help Darmal slay the lizards?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
msgctxt "FateEvent:524:0:62"
msgid "We're not expecting you to do it out of the kindness of your heart. You'll be rewarded, you know."
msgstr "Не думай, что мы просим помочь просто так. Награду получишь, само собой."

#. ja: 旅人サン、シムーンの背骨、見に来たネ？<br>あれは巨大生物「シムーン」の骨、言われているヨ。<br>夜になるとシムーンの魂、やってくる言い伝えあるネ！
#. de: Du sehen diese Knochen dort? Manche behaupten, das Knochen von großen Samiel sein und sein Geist hier auftauchen manchmal. Gruselig!
#. fr: Oh, tu as vu l'Échine du Simoun, oui tu l'as vue, pas vrai<nbsp>? Comme son nom l'indique, c'était le dos d'une énorme créature appelée Simoun. On dit même que son âme apparaît la nuit, oui<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Young Mord go there to prove their bravery. Naturally, I did it too when I was a lad!
msgctxt "FateEvent:525:0:56"
msgid "Do you see those bones? Some believe they belonged to a great samiel and that its ghost sometimes appears! Spooky! "
msgstr "Видишь те кости? Говорят, они принадлежали огромному самиэлю, и его призрак иногда появляется здесь! Жуть! "

#. ja: だから、モルドの若者、<br>あの骨の下で一晩明かす度胸試しするヨ！<br>ボクも……もちろん、やったネ！　もちろんヨ！
#. de: Manch junger Mordh hierher kommt, um Mut zu beweisen. Als ich war junger Kerl, ich natürlich auch gemacht die Mutprobe.
#. fr: C'est pour cette raison que les jeunes Mords passent la nuit entière sur ces os pour prouver leur courage, ils démontrent leur courage comme ça<nbsp>! Bien sûr, moi aussi, je l'ai fait, oui<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Do you see those bones? Some believe they belonged to a great samiel and that its ghost sometimes appears! Spooky!
msgctxt "FateEvent:525:0:57"
msgid "Young Mord go there to prove their bravery. Naturally, I did it too when I was a lad!"
msgstr "Молодые морды ночуют под теми костями, чтобы доказать свою храбрость. Я, конечно, тоже проходил это испытание, когда был юнцом!"

#. ja: あれはクイジャテンダーで間違いないネ！<br>ギガテンダーの中でも長命で大きく成長する種ヨ！<br>とても手強いから、手を出すのは危険ネ！
#. de: Das Cuijatender sein muss, sehr alter und kratzbürstiger Riesenkaktor!
#. fr: Ça, c'est le cuijapampa, oui, c'est lui<nbsp>! C'est le cultivar le plus imposant et qui a la plus grande longévité parmi les gigapampas<nbsp>! Mieux vaut ne pas trop s'en approcher car il est très fort, oui<nbsp>!
#. column 57: As these creatures are growing, they become dormant for long periods of time, many years in some cases. The fact it was drawn on the map as a landmark means it must have been sleeping at the time!
msgctxt "FateEvent:526:0:56"
msgid "That must be Cuijatender, a very old and ferocious gigantender!"
msgstr "Это, должно быть, Куихатендер — древний и свирепый гигантендер!"

#. ja: でも、きっとあのクイジャテンダーが、<br>地図に記されたお宝の隠し場所に違いないヨ！<br>お宝を手に入れるには、倒すしかないネ！
#. de: Wenn Kaktoren wachsen, manchmal schlafen Jahre ohne einen Schritt zu bewegen. Dieser hier auf Karte verzeichnet wurde, bedeuten, dass noch geschlafen zu dieser Zeit!
#. fr: Mais je suis sûr qu'il se tient là où le trésor est indiqué par notre carte... Donc, pour l'obtenir, on doit abattre le cuijapampa, oui<nbsp>!
#. column 56: That must be Cuijatender, a very old and ferocious gigantender!
msgctxt "FateEvent:526:0:57"
msgid "As these creatures are growing, they become dormant for long periods of time, many years in some cases. The fact it was drawn on the map as a landmark means it must have been sleeping at the time!"
msgstr "Пока эти существа растут, они подолгу спят — иногда годами. Раз он отмечен на карте как ориентир, значит, тогда он как раз спал!"

#. ja: た、旅人サン！<br>ボクたちが見つけたお宝が、<br>光り物好きの怪鳥に盗まれたネ！
#. de: Wir endlich Schatz gefunden! Aber Amulett von Riesenvogel geklaut wurde!
#. fr: Vo-voyageu<if $gn4>se<else>r</if><nbsp>! Notre trésor a été emporté par un gros oiseau, oui, il l'a emporté, il l'a volé<nbsp>!
#. column 57: It is called Offscoursman, and like us scavengers, it loves shinies! Now we have to hunt it down to get our treasure back!
msgctxt "FateEvent:527:0:56"
msgid "We finally found the necklace, but it was stolen by a giant bird!"
msgstr "Мы наконец нашли ожерелье, но его украла гигантская птица!"

#. ja: あの怪鳥、通称「オフスカワーズマン」は、<br>ボクらスカベンジャーの天敵ヨ！<br>倒すのに協力してほしいネ！
#. de: Ungeheuer „Wüstenschatten“ sich nennt und Vorliebe für altes Glitzerzeug hat, genau wie wir! Wir ihn finden müssen und wiederholen unser ... Artefakt!
#. fr: Ce maudit volatile est connu sous le nom de Récureur<nbsp>! C'est l'ennemi juré des chasseurs de trésors comme nous, oui<nbsp>! Aide-nous à l'abattre, je t'en prie, aide-nous<nbsp>!
#. column 56: We finally found the necklace, but it was stolen by a giant bird!
msgctxt "FateEvent:527:0:57"
msgid "It is called Offscoursman, and like us scavengers, it loves shinies! Now we have to hunt it down to get our treasure back!"
msgstr "Его зовут пустынный чистильщик. Как и мы, мусорщики, он обожает всё блестящее! Теперь надо выследить его и вернуть нашу добычу!"

#. ja: ここはアンバーヒル…<br>ボクらスカベンジャーは「丘」って呼んでるネ！
#. de: Die Bernsteinfelder wahre Schatzgrube für Plün... ähm, Archäologen wie uns sind! \<hust>
#. fr: Ici, ce sont les Collines d'Ambre, oui. Nous autres chasseurs de trésors, on les appelle juste les “collines”, juste les “collines”<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Unfortunately, they are also full of bandits too lazy to find their own shinies. Look, there are some harassing that poor man!
msgctxt "FateEvent:528:0:56"
msgid "The Hills of Amber are full of all sorts of shinies!"
msgstr "На Холмах Янтаря полно всяких блестяшек!"

#. ja: 廃坑や遺跡が多いから、拾える物も多いけど、<br>治安も悪くて、危険な場所と言われているネ！<br>ホラ、今もあそこに強盗がいるヨ、笑えるネ！
#. de: Leider jede Menge ruchloser Banditen hier unterwegs, die es auf die alten Wertsachen abgesehen. Echte Hals<shy>ab<shy>schnei<shy>der. Schau, armer Kerl dort drüben überfallen wird!
#. fr: Il y a plein de mines abandonnées et de ruines dans les environs, et donc plein de choses à déterrer<nbsp>! Mais c'est aussi un lieu plein de dangers, oui, plein de dangers<nbsp>! Regarde, il y a même des brigands<nbsp>!
#. column 56: The Hills of Amber are full of all sorts of shinies!
msgctxt "FateEvent:528:0:57"
msgid "Unfortunately, they are also full of bandits too lazy to find their own shinies. Look, there are some harassing that poor man!"
msgstr "Жаль, что здесь полно бандитов, которым лень искать блестяшки самим. Вон, видишь? Пристали к бедолаге!"

#. ja: 秘宝「大老の剣」……<br>古いロンゾの巻物に記されていた強い魔力を持つ剣、<br>ぜったいに、手に入れてみせるネ！
#. de: Die Klinge der Ahnen hier irgendwo sein sollte. Sie einst einem großen Anführer der Ronso gehört. Sie mich zu einem reich... Uhm ... berühmten Mordh machen! Wenn finden wir!
#. fr: L'épée de l'ancien... Il s'agit d'une épée magique très puissante qui est mentionnée dans un vieux rouleau ronso, oui<nbsp>! Je dois l'obtenir à tout prix, je le dois<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:529:0:56"
msgid "The Elderblade should be somewhere nearby. It was owned by a great Ronso leader and will make me a rich Mord! Once we find it, that is."
msgstr "Клинок Старейшины должен быть где-то поблизости. Он принадлежал великому вождю ронсо и сделает меня богатым мордом! Вот только сперва его надо найти."

#. ja: 今でこそ、ヒュムに似た名を名乗っているロンゾだが、<br>かつては古語を使った独特の名前を使っていたそうだ。
#. de: Heutzutage nennen wir Ronso uns so, wie die anderen Völker es tun, aber einst trugen wir Namen aus der alten Sprache.
#. fr: De nos jours, les Ronsos ont des noms qui ressemblent à ceux des Humes, mais autrefois, ils en utilisaient des spéciaux qui provenaient de la langue ancienne.
#. column 57: Some of those names, like Kelk or Biran, were given to places in Amh Araeng, like mountains, mines, and towns.
msgctxt "FateEvent:530:0:56"
msgid "These days, we Ronso often use names similar to those of the Humes, but long ago, we took them from the old tongue."
msgstr "Теперь мы, ронсо, часто берём имена, похожие на имена хьюмов, но в давние времена выбирали их из древнего языка."

#. ja: 「ケルク」や「ビラン」といった、この辺りの地名には、<br>そうした古いロンゾの名が残っている。<br>偉人の名を山や町に付ける風習があったのさ。
#. de: Einige dieser Namen wurden dann auch Orten wie Bergen, Minen oder Ortschaften hier in Amh Araeng verliehen. Zum Beispiel „Kelk“ oder „Biran“.
#. fr: “Kelk” et “Biran” sont en fait les noms de Ronsos des temps anciens. C'est parce que ce peuple avait pour tradition d'appeler les montagnes et les villages par le nom de ceux qui s'étaient illustrés par leurs actes.
#. column 56: These days, we Ronso often use names similar to those of the Humes, but long ago, we took them from the old tongue.
msgctxt "FateEvent:530:0:57"
msgid "Some of those names, like Kelk or Biran, were given to places in Amh Araeng, like mountains, mines, and towns."
msgstr "Некоторые старые имена ронсо, например Келк и Биран, дали горам, рудникам и поселениям Амх-Араэнга."

#. ja: 宝探しのために遺跡に来たんだが、<br>アルマジロどもが、ウロついていて手がつけられん。<br>旅人よ、退治するのを手伝ってくれんか？
#. de: Wir wären wahrscheinlich schon längst am Ziel, wenn diese verdammten Gürteltiere nicht wären! Lust, uns zu helfen, sie zu verscheuchen?
#. fr: On est venus dans ces ruines pour trouver un trésor, mais il est impossible de s'approcher parce qu'il y a trop de trop de tatous qui flânent dans les environs... Tu veux bien nous donner un coup de main<nbsp>?
#. column 57: Help Darmal slay the armadillos?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: We're not expecting you to do it out of the kindness of your heart. You'll be rewarded, you know.
msgctxt "FateEvent:531:0:56"
msgid "We probably would've found the treasure by now if these armadillos weren't in our way. Fancy helping shoo them off?"
msgstr "Мы бы уже нашли сокровища, если бы не эти броненосцы. Не поможешь их прогнать?"

#. ja: ダーマルに協力しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Darmal helfen, die Gürteltiere zu vertreiben?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider Darmal<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: We probably would've found the treasure by now if these armadillos weren't in our way. Fancy helping shoo them off?
#. column 62: We're not expecting you to do it out of the kindness of your heart. You'll be rewarded, you know.
