msgctxt "FateEvent:684:0:58"
msgid "Aid the farmer? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь фермеру?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этой F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 助かるよ、本当に！<br>「豆入りの木箱」を壊されないよう、<br>護りながら鳥たちを撃退してね！
#. de: Danke, danke, danke! Was immer du auch tust, pass auf, dass diese glorifizierten Bussarde, also die Vögel, mein ich, unsere Kisten nicht aufknacken, ja?
#. fr: Vous nous sauvez la vie<nbsp>! Allez-y, défendez nos caisses de café contre ces sales piafs<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Oh gods, no! There's too many of them! And they're coming for our coffee beans!
#. column 57: We have to do something before they eat through our entire harvest! You there, traveler─please, grant us your succor!
#. column 58: Aid the farmer? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Look, I'm sorry to be pushy, but these beans are our livelihood─the birds mustn't be allowed near them!
msgctxt "FateEvent:684:0:60"
msgid "Thank you, thank you, thank you! Whatever you do, don't let those glorified buzzards bust open our crates, alright!?"
msgstr "Спасибо, спасибо, спасибо! Только не дай этим пернатым стервятникам расколотить ящики, ладно!?"

#. ja: 無理言ってごめんよ。<br>でも、みんな待ってるんだ……<br>僕らのコーヒービーンを。
#. de: Ich will dich wirklich zu nichts drängen, nein, nein! Aber mit diesen Bohnen verdienen wir unseren Lebens<shy>unter<shy>halt, verstehst du? Die Vögel dürfen sie auf keinen Fall in ihre gierig-schlierigen Schnäbel bekommen!
#. fr: Je sais que cela ne vous concerne pas, mais... on a des commandes à honorer, alors...
#. column 56: Oh gods, no! There's too many of them! And they're coming for our coffee beans!
#. column 57: We have to do something before they eat through our entire harvest! You there, traveler─please, grant us your succor!
#. column 58: Aid the farmer? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Thank you, thank you, thank you! Whatever you do, don't let those glorified buzzards bust open our crates, alright!?
msgctxt "FateEvent:684:0:62"
msgid "Look, I'm sorry to be pushy, but these beans are our livelihood─the birds mustn't be allowed near them!"
msgstr "Прости, что так настаиваю. Но эти зёрна кормят нас, так что птиц к ним подпускать нельзя!"

#. ja: おや、旅の方。<br>このようなところに珍しい……<br>もしや、我らの遺跡に興味がおありで？
#. de: Oh, Reisende verirren sich selten hierher. Du bist vermutlich an historischen Stätten interessiert?
#. fr: Oh, <if $gn4>une voyageuse<else>un voyageur</if>. Voilà qui est RARE. Auriez-vous par hasard un quelconque intérêt pour nos RUINES<nbsp>?
#. column 57: Perhaps you're just the kind soul I've been looking for. As vigilkeeper of these ruins, I have a problem in desperate need of a solution.
#. column 58: It's the gazelles, you see. They like to hone their horns against hard rock, and if left unchecked, they could cause irreparable damage to the stonework here. If you see any, could you drive them away?
#. column 59: Deter the gazelles? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Thank you, stranger. Truly, I am in your debt─ah, but speak of the devils! I will pray for your success from a safe distance!
#. column 62: Not to worry─I understand. Perhaps there is another way I can still protect the ruins...
msgctxt "FateEvent:685:0:56"
msgid "Not often do I see travelers in these parts. I take it you have at least a passing interest in historical sites, then?"
msgstr "Редко увидишь путников в этих краях. Полагаю, исторические памятники вас хоть немного да интересуют?"

#. ja: であれば嬉しいですが……。<br>実は、こうした遺跡の保存にあたり、<br>困ったことがありましてな。
#. de: Dann bist du vielleicht genau die Person, die ich gesucht habe. Ich bin nämlich mit dem Schutz dieser Ruinen beauftragt und habe ein großes Problem.
#. fr: Si oui, vous tombez à pic, car il se trouve que leur intégrité est MENACÉE...
#. column 56: Not often do I see travelers in these parts. I take it you have at least a passing interest in historical sites, then?
#. column 58: It's the gazelles, you see. They like to hone their horns against hard rock, and if left unchecked, they could cause irreparable damage to the stonework here. If you see any, could you drive them away?
#. column 59: Deter the gazelles? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Thank you, stranger. Truly, I am in your debt─ah, but speak of the devils! I will pray for your success from a safe distance!
#. column 62: Not to worry─I understand. Perhaps there is another way I can still protect the ruins...
msgctxt "FateEvent:685:0:57"
msgid "Perhaps you're just the kind soul I've been looking for. As vigilkeeper of these ruins, I have a problem in desperate need of a solution."
msgstr "Может, ты как раз тот добрый человек, которого я искал. Я присматриваю за этими руинами, и тут возникла серьёзная проблема."

#. ja: それが、ガゼルたちの角研ぎ……<br>角の生え変わる時期、彼らは壁面で角をこするのですよ。<br>もし可能であれば、追い払っていただけませんか？
#. de: Es geht um die Gazellen. Sie schärfen ihre Hörner an den Mauern hier, doch das könnte die Steinarbeiten auf lange Sicht irreparabel beschädigen. Könntest du die Tiere vielleicht für mich vertreiben?
#. fr: À cette période de l'année, les gazelles des environs ont les CORNES qui POUSSENT. Et elles se plaisent alors à venir les AFFÛTER sur les murs de nos vestiges. Il faudrait que quelqu'un les fasse déguerpir...
#. column 56: Not often do I see travelers in these parts. I take it you have at least a passing interest in historical sites, then?
#. column 57: Perhaps you're just the kind soul I've been looking for. As vigilkeeper of these ruins, I have a problem in desperate need of a solution.
#. column 59: Deter the gazelles? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Thank you, stranger. Truly, I am in your debt─ah, but speak of the devils! I will pray for your success from a safe distance!
#. column 62: Not to worry─I understand. Perhaps there is another way I can still protect the ruins...
msgctxt "FateEvent:685:0:58"
msgid "It's the gazelles, you see. They like to hone their horns against hard rock, and if left unchecked, they could cause irreparable damage to the stonework here. If you see any, could you drive them away?"
msgstr "Газели точат рога о твёрдый камень. Если их не прогнать, они могут безвозвратно повредить кладку. Увидишь их — прогонишь?"

#. ja: 協力しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Die Gazellen abwehren? <br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Chasser les gazelles<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Not often do I see travelers in these parts. I take it you have at least a passing interest in historical sites, then?
#. column 57: Perhaps you're just the kind soul I've been looking for. As vigilkeeper of these ruins, I have a problem in desperate need of a solution.
#. column 58: It's the gazelles, you see. They like to hone their horns against hard rock, and if left unchecked, they could cause irreparable damage to the stonework here. If you see any, could you drive them away?
