msgctxt "FateEvent:738:0:59"
msgid "Assist the forager?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь собирателю?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого события F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: 引き受けてくれるか、ありがとう！<br>それじゃ、「ヤクテルの霊茸」が採れたら引き取るから、<br>よろしく頼むよ！
#. de: Ausgezeichnet! Bring mir, was immer du finden kannst, auch die unförmigen. Jedes kleine Fitzelchen hilft, Leben zu retten.
#. fr: Tu acceptes ? C'est très gentil de ta part, ja ! Dans ce cas, je te laisse faire la récolte, tu n'auras qu'à me donner ensuite ce que tu auras ramassé. Bon courage, ja !
#. column 56: Ah, another traveler! I, myself, have journeyed from Tuliyollal to gather ik'iit ears. No, not their <i>actual</i> ears, but a rare variety of mushroom that resembles them, hence the name.
#. column 57: What I did not expect was to be greeted with so many <i>other</i> varieties...namely ones that are trying to eat me.
#. column 58: If you've nothing pressing, I could certainly use a hand collecting the ears, as well as ridding the area of any hungry fungi.
#. column 59: Assist the forager?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: \<sigh> Then I fear I have wasted a journey...
msgctxt "FateEvent:738:0:60"
msgid "Excellent! Bring me whatever you can find, no matter how small or ill-shaped. Every sliver will help save lives!"
msgstr "Отлично! Приноси всё, что найдёшь, даже самые мелкие или невзрачные кусочки. Каждая крошка поможет спасти чью-то жизнь!"

#. ja: そっか、それは残念。<br>もし気が変わるようなら、声をかけてもらえると助かるよ。
#. de: \<seufz> Dann bin ich wohl umsonst gekommen<nbsp>...
#. fr: Ah bon ? Dommage, ja. Reviens me voir si jamais tu changes d'avis.
#. column 56: Ah, another traveler! I, myself, have journeyed from Tuliyollal to gather ik'iit ears. No, not their <i>actual</i> ears, but a rare variety of mushroom that resembles them, hence the name.
#. column 57: What I did not expect was to be greeted with so many <i>other</i> varieties...namely ones that are trying to eat me.
#. column 58: If you've nothing pressing, I could certainly use a hand collecting the ears, as well as ridding the area of any hungry fungi.
#. column 59: Assist the forager?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Excellent! Bring me whatever you can find, no matter how small or ill-shaped. Every sliver will help save lives!
msgctxt "FateEvent:738:0:62"
msgid "\\<sigh> Then I fear I have wasted a journey..."
msgstr "<i>Эх...</i> Боюсь, я зря проделал такой путь..."

#. ja: 「ヤクテルの霊茸」を集めてくれたのかい？
#. de: Was gefunden?
#. fr: Alors, ja, la récolte a été bonne ?
#. column 60: Yes, these are fine specimens, indeed...though I shall require more for my long journey to have been worthwhile.
#. column 62: That is odd. I could have sworn I saw you─ No. I was probably mistaken.
msgctxt "FateEvent:739:0:56"
msgid "Have you had any luck?"
msgstr "Как успехи?"

#. ja: ありがとう、助かるよ。<br>可能なら、もう少し採ってきてくれないかな。<br>薬作りの材料にするんだが、数が必要なんだ。
#. de: Ja, das sieht gut schon ganz gut aus. Allerdings brauche ich noch mehr, damit der weite Weg sich gelohnt hat.
#. fr: Super, encore merci du coup de main. S'il te reste du temps, tu veux bien en ramasser encore quelques-uns ? Ils vont servir à la fabrication de remèdes, donc plus j'en ai, mieux c'est, ja.
#. column 56: Have you had any luck?
#. column 62: That is odd. I could have sworn I saw you─ No. I was probably mistaken.
msgctxt "FateEvent:739:0:60"
msgid "Yes, these are fine specimens, indeed...though I shall require more for my long journey to have been worthwhile."
msgstr "Да, грибы и правда хороши... Но чтобы поездка окупилась, нужно ещё больше."

#. ja: 面倒なことを頼んですまないね、<br>引き続き、よろしく頼むよ。
#. de: Sicher? Ich dachte, ich hätte gesehen, wie du<nbsp>... Ach, nichts für ungut.
#. fr: Désolé de t'embêter avec ça, mais je n'ai personne d'autre sur qui compter, ja... Bon courage.
#. column 56: Have you had any luck?
#. column 60: Yes, these are fine specimens, indeed...though I shall require more for my long journey to have been worthwhile.
msgctxt "FateEvent:739:0:62"
msgid "That is odd. I could have sworn I saw you─ No. I was probably mistaken."
msgstr "Как-то странно. Я бы поклялся, что видел тебя... Нет, наверное, обознался."

#. ja: 「ヤクテルの霊茸」の採集、どうかな？<br>手に入れたら、届けてもらえると嬉しいよ
#. de: Die Ik'iit-Ohren sind im Wirrwarr des Waldes schwer auszumachen. Zu unserem Glück heften sie sich aber gerne an andere Arten, um ihre Sporen zu verbreiten. Vermutlich kleben also auch welche an den Fliegenpilzen.
#. fr: Tu n'as pas encore commencé ta récolte, ja ? Je reste ici pour rassembler ce que tu auras ramassé.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:740:0:56"
msgid "The fungus can be difficult to find, as it blends in well with the chaos of the jungle. Fortunately for us, it has learned to hitch rides on <i>other</i> mushrooms to aid in spore dispersal─meaning there is like to be some on the fly agarics lurking about."
msgstr "В джунглях гриб легко потерять из виду. К счастью, он приспособился цепляться за <i>другие</i> грибы, чтобы разносить споры. Так что, скорее всего, он найдётся на мухоморах."

#. ja: 「ヤクテルの霊茸」を集めてくれたのかい？
#. de: Wie läuft die Jagd?
#. fr: Tu as apporté d'autres fongus mystiques, ja ?
#. column 60: And here I started the day worried that I would leave empty-handed. I cannot begin to thank you enough!
#. column 62: I shall be returning soon, but if you happen to find any more ik'iit ears before I leave, I will see they are put to good use.
msgctxt "FateEvent:741:0:56"
msgid "How fares the hunt?"
msgstr "Ну как охота?"

#. ja: ありがとう、おかげで多くのキノコが集まったよ。<br>これなら、備蓄ぶんを考えても十分な量の薬を作れそうだ。
#. de: Wenn man bedenkt, dass ich dachte, ich würde leer ausgehen<nbsp>... Ich kann dir gar nicht genug danken!
#. fr: Merci, ja. Je pense que j'en ai suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment pour fabriquer une belle quantité de remèdes, maintenant.
#. column 56: How fares the hunt?
#. column 62: I shall be returning soon, but if you happen to find any more ik'iit ears before I leave, I will see they are put to good use.
msgctxt "FateEvent:741:0:60"
msgid "And here I started the day worried that I would leave empty-handed. I cannot begin to thank you enough!"
msgstr "А я-то с утра боялся, что вернусь с пустыми руками. Даже не знаю, как тебя благодарить!"

#. ja: それじゃあ、私はそろそろトライヨラに戻ろうと思うけれど……<br>もしまだキノコがあるなら、引き取るよ。
#. de: Ich werde bald zurückkehren. Wenn du allerdings noch mehr Ik'iit-Ohren finden solltest, nehme ich sie gerne an mich.
#. fr: Je vais bientôt pouvoir me remettre en route pour Tuliyollal, ja... Si tu as d'autres fongus à me donner, n'hésites pas.
#. column 56: How fares the hunt?
#. column 60: And here I started the day worried that I would leave empty-handed. I cannot begin to thank you enough!
msgctxt "FateEvent:741:0:62"
msgid "I shall be returning soon, but if you happen to find any more ik'iit ears before I leave, I will see they are put to good use."
msgstr "Я скоро отправлюсь обратно. Если до моего ухода найдёшь ещё грибные ушки, я позабочусь, чтобы им нашли хорошее применение."

#. ja: それじゃあ、私はそろそろトライヨラに戻ろうと思うけれど……<br>もしまだキノコがあるなら、引き取るよ。
#. de: Ich werde bald zurückkehren. Wenn du allerdings noch mehr Ik'iit-Ohren finden solltest, nehme ich sie gerne an mich.
#. fr: Je vais bientôt pouvoir me remettre en route pour Tuliyollal, ja... Si tu as d'autres fongus à me donner, n'hésites pas.
msgctxt "FateEvent:742:0:56"
msgid "I shall be returning soon, but if you happen to find any more ik'iit ears before I leave, I will see they are put to good use."
msgstr "Я скоро отправлюсь обратно. Если до моего ухода найдёшь ещё грибные ушки, я позабочусь, чтобы им нашли хорошее применение."

#. ja: 織物に使うサンベアードの毛を集めてるんだけど、<br>見てのとおり大量にいるから、ひとりじゃ手に余るんだよ。<br>よかったら、手伝ってもらえないかな……？
#. de: Kannst du von Backenhaar ebenfalls nicht genug bekommen? Dann geht's dir wie mir, besonders wenn es von Sonnenbärten stammt. Ich bin hier, um mir flauschiges Fell zu besorgen und könnte jede Hilfe gebrauchen!
#. fr: Mon travail consiste à rassembler des touffes de laine de luminobarbes, mais elles sont tellement nombreuses que je n'en vois pas le bout<nbsp>! Tu veux bien me donner un coup de main<nbsp>?
#. column 57: Assist the trapper?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Excellent! Of course, I won't ask how you come by the sideburns. Find them on the ground, snatch them from the air, strip them from the scalps of the fluffy furballs themselves...it's all the same to me!
#. column 62: Afraid of being swarmed too, I see. Wholly understandable. Wholly.
msgctxt "FateEvent:743:0:56"
msgid "Don't you love the smell of sideburns in the morning? I do, especially when those sideburns are of the sunbeard variety! I'm here to collect the fairest of hairs from the rarest of hares, and would appreciate any help you can offer!"
msgstr "Разве не чудесно пахнут бакенбарды по утрам? Особенно когда это шерсть солнечных бородачей! Я пришёл собрать самые лучшие волоски с редчайших зайцев. Буду признателен за любую помощь!"

#. ja: トナワータ族の採集人に協力しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Dem Wildbeuter helfen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider ce Tonawawta à récolter de la laine<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Don't you love the smell of sideburns in the morning? I do, especially when those sideburns are of the sunbeard variety! I'm here to collect the fairest of hairs from the rarest of hares, and would appreciate any help you can offer!
#. column 60: Excellent! Of course, I won't ask how you come by the sideburns. Find them on the ground, snatch them from the air, strip them from the scalps of the fluffy furballs themselves...it's all the same to me!
#. column 62: Afraid of being swarmed too, I see. Wholly understandable. Wholly.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:743:0:57"
msgid "Assist the trapper?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь зверолову?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого события F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ありがとう、助かるよ！<br>落ちてる毛を拾うのでも倒して刈るのでも、<br>方法は任せるから、よろしく頼むよ。
#. de: Ausgezeichnet! Wie du an das Zeug rankommst, überlass ich ganz dir. Manchmal liegt was auf dem Boden rum, und manchmal, na ja, muss man halt etwas nachhelfen.
#. fr: Merci bien, noble <if $gn4>voyageuse<else>voyageur</if>. Peu m'importe la méthode de récolte, je veux que tu m'amènes autant de touffes de laine que possible. Bonne chance<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Don't you love the smell of sideburns in the morning? I do, especially when those sideburns are of the sunbeard variety! I'm here to collect the fairest of hairs from the rarest of hares, and would appreciate any help you can offer!
#. column 57: Assist the trapper?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: Afraid of being swarmed too, I see. Wholly understandable. Wholly.
msgctxt "FateEvent:743:0:60"
msgid "Excellent! Of course, I won't ask how you come by the sideburns. Find them on the ground, snatch them from the air, strip them from the scalps of the fluffy furballs themselves...it's all the same to me!"
msgstr "Отлично! И неважно, откуда ты их возьмёшь. Подберёшь с земли, поймаешь на лету, сдерёшь с пушистых зверьков вместе со скальпом... Мне всё равно!"

#. ja: そっか、それは残念。<br>サンベアードの毛、触るとふわっふわで気持ちいいんだけどなあ……。
#. de: Keine Lust, überrannt zu werden, hm? Kann ich verstehen. Völlig verstehen.
#. fr: Ah, c'est dommage. Tu as déjà touché une luminobarbe<nbsp>? Ces bestioles sont si douces, c'est fou<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Don't you love the smell of sideburns in the morning? I do, especially when those sideburns are of the sunbeard variety! I'm here to collect the fairest of hairs from the rarest of hares, and would appreciate any help you can offer!
#. column 57: Assist the trapper?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Excellent! Of course, I won't ask how you come by the sideburns. Find them on the ground, snatch them from the air, strip them from the scalps of the fluffy furballs themselves...it's all the same to me!
msgctxt "FateEvent:743:0:62"
msgid "Afraid of being swarmed too, I see. Wholly understandable. Wholly."
msgstr "Боишься, что тебя тоже затопчут? Понимаю. Ещё как понимаю."

#. ja: サンベアードのふわ毛、引き続き採集よろしくね。<br>落ちてる毛を拾うのでも倒して刈るのでも、<br>方法は任せるよ。
#. de: Wo genau bei einem Sonnenbart das Backenhaar sitzt, fragst du? Na überall!
#. fr: Je compte toujours sur toi pour récupérer des touffes de laine<nbsp>! Bon courage<nbsp>!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:744:0:56"
msgid "Exactly what part of a sunbeard is the sideburn, you ask? Why, they're <i>all</i> sideburn!"
msgstr "Спрашиваешь, где у солнечного бородача бакенбарды? Да они <i>везде</i>!"

#. ja: サンベアードのふわ毛、<br>採れたかな？
#. de: Und? Hattest du Erfolg?
#. fr: Alors, tu as réussi à récupérer suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment de laine<nbsp>?
#. column 60: Hah hah! You smell that? Some call it musk. I call it mint!
#. column 62: No? You sure don't <i>smell</i> like you haven't.
msgctxt "FateEvent:745:0:56"
msgid "Had any luck?"
msgstr "Ну как, удалось что-нибудь найти?"

#. ja: うんうん、いい毛だ。<br>でももう少し量がほしいから……<br>引き続き、お願いできると嬉しいよ。
#. de: Haha, riechst du das? Gibt nichts Besseres auf der Welt!
#. fr: Oh, en voilà de belles touffes<nbsp>! J'aurais préféré en avoir encore un peu plus, mais je ne vais pas faire la fine bouche. Reviens me voir si tu veux m'aider<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Had any luck?
#. column 62: No? You sure don't <i>smell</i> like you haven't.
msgctxt "FateEvent:745:0:60"
msgid "Hah hah! You smell that? Some call it musk. I call it mint!"
msgstr "Ха-ха! Чуешь запах? Кто-то скажет, что мускусом несёт, а я скажу: мятой!"

#. ja: おや、持ってなかった？<br>ふわ毛の採集、引き続きお願いできると嬉しいよ。
#. de: Nein? Du riechst aber anders.
#. fr: Tiens, tu n'as rien ramassé<nbsp>? Bon, ce n'est pas grave, tu peux toujours tenter ta chance une autre fois<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Had any luck?
#. column 60: Hah hah! You smell that? Some call it musk. I call it mint!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:745:0:62"
msgid "No? You sure don't <i>smell</i> like you haven't."
msgstr "Нет? А по <i>запаху</i> и не скажешь, что ничего не нашёл."

#. ja: ありがとう、おかげで十分な量の毛が集まった。<br>そろそろ帰ろうと思うから、<br>もしまだ渡してない毛があるなら引き取るよ。
#. de: Ehrlich gesagt hab ich genug von dem Zeug, um mir einen ganzen Teppich zu knüpfen, aber ich nehm gerne noch mehr. Von Gutem kann man nie genug haben, pflegte schon meine Mutter immer zu sagen.
#. fr: Merci bien, j'ai tout ce qu'il me faut<nbsp>! Je ne vais pas tarder à rentrer, s'il te reste des touffes de laine, n'hésite pas à me les donner<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:746:0:56"
msgid "Most like I have more than enough fluff to tide me over, but that doesn't mean I won't take more. You can never have enough of the stuff, my dear old ma used to say."
msgstr "Похоже, шерсти у меня и так с избытком, но от добавки не откажусь. Как говорила моя покойная матушка, хорошей шерсти много не бывает."

#. ja: ありがとう、おかげで十分な量の毛が集まった。<br>そろそろ帰ろうと思うから、<br>もしまだ渡してない毛があるなら引き取るよ。
#. de: Ehrlich gesagt hab ich genug von dem Zeug, um mir einen ganzen Teppich zu knüpfen, aber ich nehm gerne noch mehr. Von Gutem kann man nie genug haben, pflegte schon meine Mutter immer zu sagen.
#. fr: Merci bien, j'ai tout ce qu'il me faut<nbsp>! Je ne vais pas tarder à rentrer, s'il te reste des touffes de laine, n'hésite pas à me les donner<nbsp>!
#. column 60: Mint, I tell you. Mint!
#. column 62: Looking to spin some of your own then, is it? I won't fault you. Softest wool you'll ever touch!
msgctxt "FateEvent:747:0:56"
msgid "Most like I have more than enough fluff to tide me over, but that doesn't mean I won't take more. You can never have enough of the stuff, my dear old ma used to say."
msgstr "Похоже, шерсти у меня и так с избытком, но от добавки не откажусь. Как говорила моя покойная матушка, хорошей шерсти много не бывает."

#. ja: うん、ありがとう。<br>君のおかげで助かったよ。
#. de: Ah, dieser Geruch!
#. fr: Ah vraiment, tu m'as rendu un fier service<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Most like I have more than enough fluff to tide me over, but that doesn't mean I won't take more. You can never have enough of the stuff, my dear old ma used to say.
#. column 62: Looking to spin some of your own then, is it? I won't fault you. Softest wool you'll ever touch!
msgctxt "FateEvent:747:0:60"
msgid "Mint, I tell you. Mint!"
msgstr "Вот именно! Мятой несёт!"

#. ja: おや、持ってなかったかな。<br>なんにせよ、手伝ってくれてありがとうね。
#. de: Willst wohl selbst was weben, was? Kann ich dir nicht verübeln, ist die weichste Wolle, die du je in die Finger kriegen wirst.
#. fr: Tu n'as récupéré aucune touffe<nbsp>? Ce n'est rien, je suis déjà ravi que tu aies accepté de m'aider.
#. column 56: Most like I have more than enough fluff to tide me over, but that doesn't mean I won't take more. You can never have enough of the stuff, my dear old ma used to say.
#. column 60: Mint, I tell you. Mint!
msgctxt "FateEvent:747:0:62"
msgid "Looking to spin some of your own then, is it? I won't fault you. Softest wool you'll ever touch!"
msgstr "Собрался сам прясть? Не осуждаю. Мягче шерсти ты ещё в жизни не трогал!"

#. ja: ああ、<if $gn4>お姉さん<else>お兄さん</if>、いいところに！<br>釣り上げた魚が魔物に奪われそうなんだ……！<br>どうか助けてくれよ！
#. de: Siehst du die Körbe da? Die quillen über vor Fischen, auf die sich die Bewohner des Sees nur zu gerne stürzen würden, aber das lassen wir nicht zu, oder?
#. fr: Ah<nbsp>! Tu tombes bien, <if $gn4>étrangère<else>étranger</if>. Des monstrrres veulent s'en prendre à mes prises. Aide-moi à garder mes précieux poissons<nbsp>!
#. column 57: Volunteer to protect the angler's baskets?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Exactly! Let the raptors eat my fish, and what's next? Before you know it, they'll be devouring our daughters, inhaling our in-laws! Protect those baskets with your life, adventurer, or <i>you</i> may be next!
#. column 62: And you would have those creatures just take everything I worked so hard for? For shame, adventurer. FOR SHAME!
msgctxt "FateEvent:748:0:56"
msgid "Do you see these baskets!? Well, do you? They're practically bursting with bream and bass─bream and bass the lake's denizens would devour if they could! But we cannot let that happen, can we!?"
msgstr "Видишь эти корзины?! Да видишь же? Они ломятся от лещей и окуней — рыбацкой добычи, которой обитатели озера только и ждут, чтобы поживиться! Но мы ведь этого не допустим, правда?!"

#. ja: ヘイザ・アロ族の釣人に協力しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Die Körbe des Anglers beschützen?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider le pêcheur hhetsarro<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: Do you see these baskets!? Well, do you? They're practically bursting with bream and bass─bream and bass the lake's denizens would devour if they could! But we cannot let that happen, can we!?
#. column 60: Exactly! Let the raptors eat my fish, and what's next? Before you know it, they'll be devouring our daughters, inhaling our in-laws! Protect those baskets with your life, adventurer, or <i>you</i> may be next!
#. column 62: And you would have those creatures just take everything I worked so hard for? For shame, adventurer. FOR SHAME!
