msgctxt "FateEvent:752:0:58"
msgid "Help the Hhetsarro herder?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь пастушке из хетсарро?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого события F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: ありがとうございます……！<br>かなり数が多いようなので、<br>どうかお気をつけて……！
#. de: Danke! Aber pass bitte auf dich auf. Es waren viele, ziemlich viele!
#. fr: Merrrci infiniment<nbsp>! Les monstres sont plutôt nombreux, alors faites attention<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Friend! Your scars tell the tale of many battles, and the Hhetsarro are in need of a great warrior today.
#. column 57: Lunyucaua'pyas─terrible hulking creatures─have descended from the hills and frightened off our rroneek. But the herd will not have gone far, which means they're still in danger!
#. column 58: Help the Hhetsarro herder?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: I see. Then I shall pray to the gods that the monsters do not find the herd, for it would mean my people starve...
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:752:0:60"
msgid "Thank you! And please take care. There were...more than one. <i>Many</i> more than one."
msgstr "Спасибо! И будь осторожен. Их было... не один. <i>Много</i> не один."

#. ja: そう……ですよね、<br>無理を言ってしまい、申し訳ございません。<br>ですが……ああ、どうすれば……！
#. de: Verstehe ... Dann will ich beten, dass die Ungeheuer unsere Herde verschonen. Sonst bricht womöglich eine Hungersnot aus.
#. fr: Oui, vous avez rrraison, je vous demande l'impossible... Aaah... Que faire<nbsp>? Les pauvres bêtes...
#. column 56: Friend! Your scars tell the tale of many battles, and the Hhetsarro are in need of a great warrior today.
#. column 57: Lunyucaua'pyas─terrible hulking creatures─have descended from the hills and frightened off our rroneek. But the herd will not have gone far, which means they're still in danger!
#. column 58: Help the Hhetsarro herder?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Thank you! And please take care. There were...more than one. <i>Many</i> more than one.
msgctxt "FateEvent:752:0:62"
msgid "I see. Then I shall pray to the gods that the monsters do not find the herd, for it would mean my people starve..."
msgstr "Понимаю. Тогда буду молить богов, чтобы чудовища не нашли стадо. Иначе мой народ останется без еды..."

#. ja: 私たち自身がロネークを狩ることも当然あるのですが、<br>群れが消えるような殺戮はなんとしても避けたいのです。
#. de: Wenn die Lunyucaua'pya so klein wie die Rroneek wären, würde ich mich ja selbst um sie kümmern. Aber leider<nbsp>... \<seufz>
#. fr: Il nous arrive également de chasser les rroneeks, mais nous évitons toujours de décimer des trrroupeaux entiers<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:753:0:56"
msgid "Were that the lunyucaua'pyas as meek as the rroneek, I might herd the monsters myself. Alas... \\<sigh>"
msgstr "Если бы луньюкауа-пья были такими же смирными, как рронеки, я бы сам их пас. Увы... <i>Эх...</i>"

#. ja: こんな場所で、ほかの人に会うなんてね。<br>あたしは拾得人の仕事で、出張ってきたんだけど……<br>ボルトハウンドに出くわして、困ってたのさ。
#. de: Es überrascht mich, hier jemandem zu begegnen. Weißt du, ich bin meiner Arbeit als Wiederschafferin stets gewissenhaft nachgegangen, doch nun bereiten mir die Blitzhunde große Probleme.
#. fr: Je ne pensais pas croiser quelqu'un ici<nbsp>! Je suis venue pour mon travail, mais des limiers fulgurants m'empêchent de continuer.
#. column 57: You're <i>not</i> here for salvage? Well, my apologies. I've had to deal with more than a few knobs trying to jump my claim today...not to mention these damn bolt hounds.
#. column 58: Speaking of which, if you're not here to <i>ruin</i> my life, might I interest you in making it a little better? I could definitely use a hand collecting scrap, as well as scaring off the curs...and I can pay.
#. column 59: Aid the reforger?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Wonderful. Now as for what <i>exactly</i> to collect, well...it's not like all scrap has a helpful sign above it that says “useful” and “useless,” so you'll just have to bring me everything you find and let me be the judge. Happy hunting!
#. column 62: Well, you can't fault a girl for asking, can you? Now, if you don't mind, you can kindly get the hell off my claim.
msgctxt "FateEvent:754:0:56"
msgid "If you're from the camp, you can slog off because I've already claimed this spot for salvage. Reforger's rights say I've got a good six bells left. It's there in the charter."
msgstr "Если ты из лагеря, проваливай: это место уже моё, я здесь собираю лом. По правам восстановителей мне ещё целых шесть часовых колоколов. В уставе всё сказано."

#. ja: このまま手ぶらで帰ったんじゃ、<br>生活が成り立たない。
#. de: Die Gefahr, die von ihnen ausgeht, macht es mir unmöglich, etwas zu sammeln. Aber ich kann auch nicht mit leeren Händen heimkehren!
#. fr: Si je ne fais rien, je vais devoir rentrer bredouille...
#. column 56: If you're from the camp, you can slog off because I've already claimed this spot for salvage. Reforger's rights say I've got a good six bells left. It's there in the charter.
#. column 58: Speaking of which, if you're not here to <i>ruin</i> my life, might I interest you in making it a little better? I could definitely use a hand collecting scrap, as well as scaring off the curs...and I can pay.
#. column 59: Aid the reforger?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Wonderful. Now as for what <i>exactly</i> to collect, well...it's not like all scrap has a helpful sign above it that says “useful” and “useless,” so you'll just have to bring me everything you find and let me be the judge. Happy hunting!
#. column 62: Well, you can't fault a girl for asking, can you? Now, if you don't mind, you can kindly get the hell off my claim.
