#. macro: <ui-color 500> — text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color; color = 500 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <ui-edge-color 501> — text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color; color = 501 (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: </ui-edge-color> — end of: text outline color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-edge-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </ui-color> — end of: text color from the UIColor sheet; </ui-color> restores the previous color (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:759:0:58"
msgid "Aid the herder in calming the unruly rroneek?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"
msgstr "Помочь пастуху успокоить буйного рронека?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※Рекомендуемый уровень для этого события F.A.T.E. — <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>"

#. ja: やってくれるか、ありがたい……！<br>ボスに敗れたとはいえ、あの若いロネークは力強い、<br>十分に気をつけてくれよ！
#. de: Wenn ein Rroneek einmal von Sinnen ist, können ihn nur noch ein paar ordentliche Schläge beruhigen. Sei aber vorsichtig. Nur weil er gegen den Bullen verloren hat, ist er noch lange nicht ungefährlich.
#. fr: Excellente nouvelle<nbsp>! Méfie-toi quand même. Il a beau avoir perrrdu contre le chef du troupeau, ce jeune rroneek fougueux n'en reste pas moins dangereux<nbsp>!
#. column 56: \<pant> \<pant><br>Please... A moment...<br>Earlier today, one of our herd's more...<i>ambitious</i> males challenged the dominant bull, and was thoroughly humiliated.
#. column 57: This behavior is not at all uncommon, but in this particular instance, the male─we call him Hwittaeki─did not take well his humbling, and has grown...let's say, “agitated.” So much so, I fear for the safety of the calves and cows.
#. column 58: Aid the herder in calming the unruly rroneek?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 62: I cannot say I blame you for wanting to keep a wide berth. I've seen a good too many of my friends gored.
msgctxt "FateEvent:759:0:60"
msgid "Once in a frenzy such as this, I'm afraid the only thing that will calm a rroneek is a good cuffing. But please be careful. Just because he lost to the bull, doesn't make him any less dangerous."
msgstr "Когда рронек впадает в такое бешенство, успокоить его может только хорошая трёпка. Но будь осторожен. Проиграв вожаку, он не стал менее опасным."

#. ja: そうか……怪我しそうだもんな。<br>こうなったら、俺が命懸けで……いや……うーむ。
#. de: Kann dir nicht verübeln, dass du lieber einen Bogen um ihn machst. Hab schon den ein oder anderen gesehen, der auf die Hörner genommen wurde, und schön war es nicht.
#. fr: Je comprends, ce n'est pas une tâche aisée... Moi non plus je n'ai pas envie de finir couverrrt de bleus. Mais il va bien falloir que quelqu'un s'en occupe...
#. column 56: \<pant> \<pant><br>Please... A moment...<br>Earlier today, one of our herd's more...<i>ambitious</i> males challenged the dominant bull, and was thoroughly humiliated.
#. column 57: This behavior is not at all uncommon, but in this particular instance, the male─we call him Hwittaeki─did not take well his humbling, and has grown...let's say, “agitated.” So much so, I fear for the safety of the calves and cows.
#. column 58: Aid the herder in calming the unruly rroneek?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Once in a frenzy such as this, I'm afraid the only thing that will calm a rroneek is a good cuffing. But please be careful. Just because he lost to the bull, doesn't make him any less dangerous.
msgctxt "FateEvent:759:0:62"
msgid "I cannot say I blame you for wanting to keep a wide berth. I've seen a good too many of my friends gored."
msgstr "Не виню тебя за то, что предпочитаешь держаться подальше. Я видел, как многих друзей насаживали на рога."

#. ja: ロネークの雄同士は、ときどき力比べをするんだ。<br>真正面から額をゴツゴツぶつけてよ……<br>そりゃもう、すげぇ迫力なんだぜ。
#. de: Ein Kampf zwischen zwei Bullen ist ein ziemliches Spektakel, vor allem klanglich. Das Krachen der Schädel, das ohrenbetäubende Brüllen. Manchmal fragt man sich, ob es wirklich so eine gute Idee war, diese Biester zähmen zu wollen.
#. fr: Chez les rroneeks, les mâles rivaux se livrent parfois à des duels de force. Ils s'élancent à toute berrrzingue l'un contre l'autre, cornes contre cornes<nbsp>! Imagine un peu le fracas...
msgctxt "FateEvent:760:0:56"
msgid "A fight between two males is quite the sight, but it's the sound that you'll never forget. The crack of the heads, the echoing of the roars. It makes you wonder why we ever thought we could truly tame the beasts."
msgstr "Схватка двух самцов — зрелище что надо, но звук запомнишь навсегда. Треск лбов, гул рёва... И невольно задумываешься, зачем мы вообще решили приручить этих зверей."

#. ja: おぬし、見たところかなり腕が立つようじゃな。<br>ならばどうか、眼前の混乱を鎮めるため、<br>力を貸してはもらえんか。
#. de: Höchst erfreut, deine Bekanntschaft zu machen, <if $gn4>Reisende<else>Reisender</if>. Du riechst nach Blut und Trauer, aber scheinst das Herz am rechten Fleck zu haben. Womöglich kannst du mir helfen.
#. fr: Toi, je peux voir à ton allure que tu sais manier ton arme avec aisance<nbsp>! J'aimerais que tu m'aides à apaiser le chaos qui s'est abattu non loin d'ici.
#. column 57: The lunyuhiyshahe are gentle creatures, but the eyes of those gathered before us burn with hatred. Something wicked has bestained their hearts, and turned them against their very nature.
#. column 58: Driven to violence, they are trapped in a purgatory not of their own making. A cruel fate─one I wish to release them from. One I hope you might, as well.
msgctxt "FateEvent:761:0:56"
msgid "Well met, traveler. You smell of blood and sadness, yet I sense within you a kindred spirit─one I would entreat for aid."
msgstr "Здравствуй, путник. От тебя пахнет кровью и печалью, но я чувствую в тебе родственную душу. Хотел бы попросить тебя о помощи."

#. ja: こやつらは本来おとなしい草食獣なんじゃが、<br>見てのとおり、手の付けられん恐慌状態に陥っておる。<br>人里を護るため、多少手荒でも止めてやらねば……。
#. de: Die Lunyuhiyshahe sind für gewöhnlich friedliche Tiere, doch die Augen von diesen hier brennen vor Hass. Etwas Böses hat von ihnen Besitz ergriffen.
#. fr: Ces bêtes sauvages sont plutôt dociles en temps normal, mais quelque chose les effraie au plus haut point... Il va falloir les calmer par la manière forte avant qu'elles ne causent des dégâts.
#. column 56: Well met, traveler. You smell of blood and sadness, yet I sense within you a kindred spirit─one I would entreat for aid.
#. column 58: Driven to violence, they are trapped in a purgatory not of their own making. A cruel fate─one I wish to release them from. One I hope you might, as well.
msgctxt "FateEvent:761:0:57"
msgid "The lunyuhiyshahe are gentle creatures, but the eyes of those gathered before us burn with hatred. Something wicked has bestained their hearts, and turned them against their very nature."
msgstr "Луныухийшахе — кроткие создания, но глаза собравшихся здесь горят ненавистью. Нечто зловещее очернило их сердца и заставило идти против собственной природы."

#. ja: ワシは、古傷ゆえに戦えぬ身……。<br>手間をかけるが、助力を求めたいのじゃ。
#. de: Jetzt kennen sie nur noch Gewalt und Leid, ein Schicksal, von dem ich sie gerne erlösen würde. Du vielleicht auch?
#. fr: Mal<shy>heu<shy>reu<shy>se<shy>ment une vieille blessure m'empêche de me battre cor<shy>rec<shy>te<shy>ment. Si tu voulais bien m'aider dans cette tâche...
#. column 56: Well met, traveler. You smell of blood and sadness, yet I sense within you a kindred spirit─one I would entreat for aid.
#. column 57: The lunyuhiyshahe are gentle creatures, but the eyes of those gathered before us burn with hatred. Something wicked has bestained their hearts, and turned them against their very nature.
msgctxt "FateEvent:761:0:58"
msgid "Driven to violence, they are trapped in a purgatory not of their own making. A cruel fate─one I wish to release them from. One I hope you might, as well."
msgstr "Они обезумели от ярости и оказались в аду, которого не заслужили. Жестокая участь. Я хочу избавить их от неё. Надеюсь, ты тоже."

#. ja: 見ろ、ワニどもの様子を……。<br>強大な魔物、蛇王トクローネの目覚めを察知し、<br>怖れ慄き暴れておるのじゃ。
#. de: Sieh doch nur, <if $gn4>Reisende<else>Reisender</if>. Nicht einmal die mächtigen Alligatoren können ihre Furcht vor dem kommenden Sturm verbergen. Wie sie sich winden und mit den Kiefern knirschen.
#. fr: Regarde, les crocodiles ne sont pas dans leur état normal. Ils doivent sentir que Ttokrrone, le roi des serpents, est à nouveau éveillé...
#. column 57: Once, I believed I could stand against his scaled phalanx, and paid dearly for my hubris.
#. column 58: But still, I cannot sit idle as those I am honor-bound to protect are threatened. I would hope you, too, are of the same mind.
msgctxt "FateEvent:762:0:56"
msgid "Behold, traveler. Not even the mighty alligator can hide his fear of the coming storm. Behold as he rakes and gnashes in anticipation of the Serpentlord's return."
msgstr "Взгляни, путник. Даже могучие аллигаторы не могут скрыть страха перед надвигающейся бурей. Смотри, как они мечутся и скрежещут зубами в ожидании возвращения Змеиного владыки."

#. ja: かくいうワシもトクローネに敗れ、<br>狩人の道を断たれた身でな……。<br>正直なところ恐怖を感じておる。
#. de: Einst glaubte ich, ich könnte es selbst mit seiner geschuppten Phalanx aufnehmen. Eine Anmaßung, die ich teuer bezahlt habe.
#. fr: J'ai été vaincu par cette diabolique créature par le passé. Voilà pourquoi je me suis éloigné de la chasse... En vérité, j'étais trop terrifié de la croiser à nouveau.
#. column 56: Behold, traveler. Not even the mighty alligator can hide his fear of the coming storm. Behold as he rakes and gnashes in anticipation of the Serpentlord's return.
#. column 58: But still, I cannot sit idle as those I am honor-bound to protect are threatened. I would hope you, too, are of the same mind.
msgctxt "FateEvent:762:0:57"
msgid "Once, I believed I could stand against his scaled phalanx, and paid dearly for my hubris."
msgstr "Когда-то я думал, что смогу противостоять его чешуйчатому войску, и дорого заплатил за свою самонадеянность."

#. ja: じゃが、民を護るは狩人の務めじゃ。<br>哀れなワニどもを鎮めるため、<br>おぬしの力を貸してはくれんか？
#. de: Dennoch kann ich nicht tatenlos dabei zusehen, wie jene bedroht werden, deren Schutz mir obliegt. Ich hoffe, dass auch du so fühlst.
#. fr: Cependant le devoir d'un rôdeur vipère est de protéger le peuple des monstres avant tout<nbsp>! Acceptes-tu de m'aider à calmer ces reptiles avant qu'ils ne fassent des blessés<nbsp>?
#. column 56: Behold, traveler. Not even the mighty alligator can hide his fear of the coming storm. Behold as he rakes and gnashes in anticipation of the Serpentlord's return.
#. column 57: Once, I believed I could stand against his scaled phalanx, and paid dearly for my hubris.
msgctxt "FateEvent:762:0:58"
msgid "But still, I cannot sit idle as those I am honor-bound to protect are threatened. I would hope you, too, are of the same mind."
msgstr "И всё же я не могу сидеть сложа руки, когда грозит опасность тем, кого поклялся защищать. Надеюсь, ты тоже не останешься в стороне."

#. ja: 地霊を倒すか、地面に露出した水晶を集め、<br>ワシのところに持ってきてくれい。
#. de: Wenn man genau hinsieht, findet man Tropfen getrockneten Bluts am Boden<nbsp>- öfter aber noch in den Klauen boshafter Exergone.
#. fr: Tu peux vaincre des ennemis ou récupérer des cristaux formés au sol, mais quoi qu'il en soit, amène-les-moi<nbsp>!
msgctxt "FateEvent:763:0:56"
msgid "Those keen of eye may find crystalline “droplets” of the blood lying upon the earth, but more often than not, they'll be in the hands of mischievous sprites."
msgstr "Если у тебя острый глаз, ты найдёшь на земле кристаллические «капли» крови. Но чаще всего ими завладевают озорные духи."

#. ja: 地霊水晶が集まっておるなら、<br>ワシに手渡してくれい。
#. de: Wenn du etwas von dem Blut des Bodens finden solltest, dann bringe es zu mir.
#. fr: Lorsque tu auras amassé des cristaux, amène-les-moi<nbsp>!
#. column 60: Yes, this is the crystal I spoke of. But we will require much more if we are to stoke the flames of wroth in the Serpentlord's heart.
#. column 62: May you find the path you seek.
msgctxt "FateEvent:764:0:56"
msgid "If you happen upon the blood, bring it to me that I might keep it safe."
msgstr "Если найдёшь кровь, принеси её мне. Я сохраню её в безопасности."

#. ja: おぬしの尽力に感謝を！<br>しかし、ワシの策を成すにはまだ数が足りんでな、<br>引き続き、よろしく頼むぞ。
#. de: Ja, das ist, wovon ich sprach. Aber wir werden noch viel mehr dieser Kristalle benötigen, wenn wir Erfolg haben wollen.
#. fr: Merci pour ton aide<nbsp>! En revanche il n'y a pas assez de cristaux pour mettre mon plan en marche. Je compte sur toi pour en amener davantage.
#. column 56: If you happen upon the blood, bring it to me that I might keep it safe.
#. column 62: May you find the path you seek.
msgctxt "FateEvent:764:0:60"
msgid "Yes, this is the crystal I spoke of. But we will require much more if we are to stoke the flames of wroth in the Serpentlord's heart."
msgstr "Да, это тот самый кристалл. Но чтобы разжечь гнев Змеиного владыки, нам понадобится куда больше."

#. ja: ふむ、もう少し採集してくるつもりかの？<br>ならば引き続き、よろしく頼むぞい。
#. de: Mögest du den Weg finden, auf dessen Suche du bist.
#. fr: Oh, tu comptes retourner ramasser des cristaux<nbsp>? À la bonne heure<nbsp>!
#. column 56: If you happen upon the blood, bring it to me that I might keep it safe.
#. column 60: Yes, this is the crystal I spoke of. But we will require much more if we are to stoke the flames of wroth in the Serpentlord's heart.
msgctxt "FateEvent:764:0:62"
msgid "May you find the path you seek."
msgstr "Да найдёшь ты путь, который ищешь."

#. ja: おぬしのおかげで、十分な数の地霊水晶が集まった。<br>もしまだ持っているなら受け取るが……<br>あるかの？
#. de: Dank dir habe ich mehr Kristalle erhalten, als ich jemals zu träumen gewagt hätte. Falls du allerdings noch mehr haben solltest, nehme ich sie gerne entgegen.
#. fr: Grâce à tes efforts, j'ai suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment de cristaux pour passer à la suite de mon plan<nbsp>! S'il t'en reste encore, n'hésite pas à me les confier.
msgctxt "FateEvent:765:0:56"
msgid "With your help, I have gathered more crystal than I thought possible. Still, I will accept more if it is more that you have."
msgstr "С твоей помощью я собрал куда больше кристаллов, чем мог надеяться. Но если у тебя есть ещё, я их приму."

#. ja: おぬしのおかげで、十分な数の地霊水晶が集まった。<br>もしまだ持っているなら受け取るが……<br>あるかの？
#. de: Dank dir habe ich mehr Kristalle erhalten, als ich jemals zu träumen gewagt hätte. Falls du allerdings noch mehr haben solltest, nehme ich sie gerne entgegen.
#. fr: Grâce à tes efforts, j'ai suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment de cristaux pour passer à la suite de mon plan<nbsp>! S'il t'en reste encore, n'hésite pas à me les confier.
#. column 60: You have proved an eager ally today, traveler. You have my thanks.
#. column 62: My legs grow tired, though my pack remains painfully light. Perhaps I will have better luck with the coming morn.
msgctxt "FateEvent:766:0:56"
msgid "With your help, I have gathered more crystal than I thought possible. Still, I will accept more if it is more that you have."
msgstr "С твоей помощью я собрал куда больше кристаллов, чем мог надеяться. Но если у тебя есть ещё, я их приму."

#. ja: これでワシの策を成すに十分な量が確保できた。<br>おぬしの尽力に、あらためて感謝を……！
#. de: Deine Hilfe hat sich als unschätzbar wertvoll erwiesen. Hab Dank, <if $gn4>Reisende<else>Reisender</if>
#. fr: Ta con<shy>tri<shy>bu<shy>tion ne sera pas vaine, je te le promets<nbsp>! Tu as toute ma gratitude, sache-le.
#. column 56: With your help, I have gathered more crystal than I thought possible. Still, I will accept more if it is more that you have.
#. column 62: My legs grow tired, though my pack remains painfully light. Perhaps I will have better luck with the coming morn.
msgctxt "FateEvent:766:0:60"
msgid "You have proved an eager ally today, traveler. You have my thanks."
msgstr "Сегодня ты оказался верным союзником, путник. Благодарю тебя."

#. ja: ふむ、地霊水晶は持っておらんかの？<br>十分な量が集まったことじゃし、<br>そろそろ切り上げようぞ。
#. de: Meine Beine werden müde, wiewohl mein Gepäck schmerzhaft leicht ist. Vielleicht wird der nächste Tag mi mehr Glück bescheiden.
#. fr: Hmmm<nbsp>? Tu n'as aucun cristal<nbsp>? Je pense en avoir déjà suf<shy>fi<shy>sam<shy>ment. Il est bientôt temps de passer à la suite.
#. column 56: With your help, I have gathered more crystal than I thought possible. Still, I will accept more if it is more that you have.
#. column 60: You have proved an eager ally today, traveler. You have my thanks.
msgctxt "FateEvent:766:0:62"
msgid "My legs grow tired, though my pack remains painfully light. Perhaps I will have better luck with the coming morn."
msgstr "Ноги уже устали, а сумка всё ещё обидно пуста. Может, завтра повезёт больше."

#. ja: ワシは元狩人でな……。<br>かつて東の平原で強大なトラルヴィドラール、<br>蛇王トクローネと闘い、敗れたことがあっての。
#. de: Seit meiner Kindheit habe ich hart daran gearbeitet, ein Jäger zu werden. Denn ich wusste, dass es eines Tages an mir liegen würde, mein Volk zu retten.
#. fr: J'étais un rodeur vipère autrefois, et je suis parti affronter le Tural vidraal Ttokrrone à l'est des plaines... et j'ai échoué.
#. column 57: But when the Serpentlord loomed before me, I failed in my duty.
#. column 58: But for that failure it was not I who paid, but my people. My family.
#. column 59: And now, he seeks to return that he might kill again. I am all that stands in his way. <i>We</i> are all that stand in his way.
msgctxt "FateEvent:767:0:56"
msgid "Since I was but a pup, I trained to be a hunter, knowing that one day I would be called upon to use my talents to save my kin."
msgstr "С малых лет я готовился стать охотником, зная, что однажды мне придётся спасти свой народ."

#. ja: そのときに負った傷のせいで、<br>狩人の道を断たれはしたが、復讐のため追い続けてきたのじゃ。
#. de: Doch im Angesicht des Schlangenkönigs versagte ich.
#. fr: La blessure qu'il m'a infligée lors de notre combat m'a rendu incapable de continuer mes activités. Mais le désir de vengeance ne m'a jamais quitté<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Since I was but a pup, I trained to be a hunter, knowing that one day I would be called upon to use my talents to save my kin.
#. column 58: But for that failure it was not I who paid, but my people. My family.
#. column 59: And now, he seeks to return that he might kill again. I am all that stands in his way. <i>We</i> are all that stand in his way.
msgctxt "FateEvent:767:0:57"
msgid "But when the Serpentlord loomed before me, I failed in my duty."
msgstr "Но, когда передо мной предстал Змеиный владыка, я не справился со своим долгом."

#. ja: ヤツはワシの同胞を、<br>愛する者たちを殺した憎き仇敵……。<br>自らの手で仕留められずとも、この機に必ず討ちとりたい。
#. de: Und dieses Versagen bezahlte nicht ich, sondern mein Volk. Meine Familie.
#. fr: Cette créature m'a tout pris<nbsp>: ma vie, ma santé, mes camarades et les personnes chères à mon cœur. Je dois l'arrêter de mes mains... il le faut<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Since I was but a pup, I trained to be a hunter, knowing that one day I would be called upon to use my talents to save my kin.
#. column 57: But when the Serpentlord loomed before me, I failed in my duty.
#. column 59: And now, he seeks to return that he might kill again. I am all that stands in his way. <i>We</i> are all that stand in his way.
msgctxt "FateEvent:767:0:58"
msgid "But for that failure it was not I who paid, but my people. My family."
msgstr "За эту неудачу заплатил не я, а мой народ. Моя семья."

#. ja: トクローネを放置すれば、<br>ワシの故郷と同じ惨劇が繰り返されることじゃろう。<br>どうか、おぬしも討伐に力を貸してくれい。
#. de: Jetzt schickt er sich an, erneut zurückzukehren und sein tödliches Werk zu verrichten. Nur ich kann das verhindern. Nur <i>uns</i> kann es gelingen.
#. fr: Si on laisse le roi des serpents n'en faire qu'à sa guise, bientôt ce sera un autre village qui sera englouti, comme le fut le mien... J'ai besoin de ton aide pour enfin terrasser cet horrible monstre<nbsp>!
#. column 56: Since I was but a pup, I trained to be a hunter, knowing that one day I would be called upon to use my talents to save my kin.
#. column 57: But when the Serpentlord loomed before me, I failed in my duty.
#. column 58: But for that failure it was not I who paid, but my people. My family.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:767:0:59"
msgid "And now, he seeks to return that he might kill again. I am all that stands in his way. <i>We</i> are all that stand in his way."
msgstr "Теперь он хочет вернуться и снова убивать. Только я могу ему помешать. <i>Мы</i> можем ему помешать."

#. ja: すまぬが「地霊水晶」を集めるのに手を貸してもらえんか。<br>採集しようにも、地霊が多くて弱っておったのじゃ。
#. de: Niemand weiß, wann der Schlangenkönig das nächste Mal erwachen wird, aber wenn es erst einmal so weit ist, gibt es kein Entrinnen mehr. Wenn wir ihn besiegen wollen, müssen wir ihn hervorlocken und unter unseren Bedingungen bekämpfen.
#. fr: Accepterais-tu de m'aider à amasser plus de cristaux spirituels<nbsp>? Ceux en ma possession se sont affaiblis.
#. column 57: And how might we do that, you ask? Why, by taking what is most dear to him─his children. And that will require the <i>Blood of the Land</i>.
#. column 58: Collect Blood of the Land for Br'uk Vaw?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Asps of the Shaaloani are drawn to this crystal, so the more we collect, the more of the snakes we can slay. I will do my best to search, but my tired legs can only carry me so far.
#. column 62: That is...unfortunate. However, I shall not abandon hope. I will gather what I can and face the Serpentlord myself, if I must.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:768:0:56"
msgid "We cannot know when the Serpentlord will next awaken, but by the time he has risen, it will already be too late. No, if we are to take down the fiend, we must lure him forth that we might fight on <i>our</i> terms."
msgstr "Мы не знаем, когда Змеиный владыка пробудится в следующий раз. Но когда это случится, будет уже поздно. Нет, чтобы одолеть чудовище, нужно выманить его и сразиться на <i>наших</i> условиях."

#. ja: この水晶があれば、荒野を脅かす危険な魔物、<br>蛇王トクローネを誘き出す罠が作れるでな。<br>ヤツを始末するためにも、力を貸してくれい。
#. de: Wie ich das anzustellen gedenke? Nun, indem wir ihm nehmen, was ihm am teuersten ist: seine Brut. Und dafür brauchen wir das Blut des Bodens.
#. fr: À l'aide de ces minéraux, je compte bien forcer Ttokrrone à sortir de sa tanière. Je dois mettre fin à son règne de terreur, mais seul je n'arriverai à rien.
#. column 56: We cannot know when the Serpentlord will next awaken, but by the time he has risen, it will already be too late. No, if we are to take down the fiend, we must lure him forth that we might fight on <i>our</i> terms.
#. column 58: Collect Blood of the Land for Br'uk Vaw?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※The recommended level for this FATE is <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 60: Asps of the Shaaloani are drawn to this crystal, so the more we collect, the more of the snakes we can slay. I will do my best to search, but my tired legs can only carry me so far.
#. column 62: That is...unfortunate. However, I shall not abandon hope. I will gather what I can and face the Serpentlord myself, if I must.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "FateEvent:768:0:57"
msgid "And how might we do that, you ask? Why, by taking what is most dear to him─his children. And that will require the <i>Blood of the Land</i>."
msgstr "Как это сделать, спрашиваешь? Отнять у него самое дорогое — его потомство. А для этого понадобится <i>Кровь земли</i>."

#. ja: 赤日のブルクバーに協力しますか？<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>※このF.A.T.E.の推奨レベルは<num $n1>です。</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. de: Blut des Bodens für Br'uk Vaw sammeln?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>Empfohlene Stufe: <num $n1></ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. fr: Aider Br'uk Vaw à ramasser des cristaux<nbsp>?<br><br><ui-color 500><ui-edge-color 501>* Le niveau recommandé pour cet ALÉA est <num $n1>.</ui-edge-color></ui-color>
#. column 56: We cannot know when the Serpentlord will next awaken, but by the time he has risen, it will already be too late. No, if we are to take down the fiend, we must lure him forth that we might fight on <i>our</i> terms.
#. column 57: And how might we do that, you ask? Why, by taking what is most dear to him─his children. And that will require the <i>Blood of the Land</i>.
#. column 60: Asps of the Shaaloani are drawn to this crystal, so the more we collect, the more of the snakes we can slay. I will do my best to search, but my tired legs can only carry me so far.
#. column 62: That is...unfortunate. However, I shall not abandon hope. I will gather what I can and face the Serpentlord myself, if I must.
